Constitutional Council: Amendments to some of the Rules of Procedure of the National Assembly are in line with the Constitution (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Constitutional Council unanimously decided by a 9-vote majority of all members of the Constitutional Council that The National Assembly is in line with the Constitution.
The unanimous decision on the above amendment was made on December 7, 2022 in a plenary session chaired by Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council.
The Internal Rules of the National Assembly of Cambodia were promulgated on October 27, 1993. The Internal Rules of the National Assembly of Cambodia have been amended 10 times in a row in order to be consistent with the provisions of the Constitution and additional constitutions to ensure the normal functioning of national institutions as well as the actual situation.
Proposed amendments to 2 new articles (two), 5 new articles (two), 10 new articles (three), 16 articles and 35 new articles of the Rules of Procedure of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia are made for the following main purposes:
1. The content is consistent with the provisions of Article 89, new Article 98 (a) and the supplementary Constitution to ensure the normal functioning of the new Article 4 (one) of national institutions.
2. Ensure that the National Assembly, as a legislative body, operates smoothly, smoothly and sustainably in all circumstances to ensure the protection and maintenance of peace, social security, public order, and political stability of the nation.
3. Ensuring respect for the principle of separation of powers, liberal democracy, pluralism and constitutional monarchy.
5. Ensure that the General Secretariat of the National Assembly to communicate more effectively outside the National Assembly with ministries, institutions and development partners, as well as parliamentary diplomacy more effectively. King orders 35 members of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's secretariat to be promoted
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, has issued a Royal Decree ordering the promotion of 35 members of the Secretariat of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to the rank of Director General and Undersecretary of State. This is according to the Royal Decree obtained by Fresh News on December 7, 2022.
Takhmao Water Treatment Plant, worth more than $ 30 million, can produce more than 30,000 cubic meters of water per day, 11% completed
(Kandal): The Takhmao Water Treatment Plant, which has a production capacity of more than 30,000 cubic meters per day, has achieved about 11% of the total project, while this project is scheduled to be completed by the end of 2024.
Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority expects that after the commissioning of this Takhmao Water Treatment Plant, it will provide the people in Takhmao City and its suburbs with sufficient water and encourage the poor people in Takhmao City to have access to the network. Clean water to use.
On the afternoon of December 6, 2022, Dr. Cham Prasidh, Senior Minister, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, inspected the progress of the construction of Takhmao Water Treatment Plant with the participation of Mr. MIKAMI Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan. In Cambodia, Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province and officials of specialized departments and other authorities
Dr. Cham Prasidh said that the construction of a project to expand the water supply system in Takhmao City in Kandal province, as the population continues to increase, which doubles the demand for water to supply water to the new airport. .
He said that in the Takhmao area since 2004, drinking water is supplied by a small factory with a capacity of only 50 cubic meters per day, which makes the water supply is scarce, despite the addition. Connected from Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority.
The Senior Minister called on the local authorities and relevant units to pay attention to the protection of water resources, the safety of the treatment plant and the maintenance of the underground pipeline system to prevent risks, because if there is a problem, it will affect the supply. Tens of thousands of households in Kandal province as well as Phnom Penh, in particular, affect the new Phnom Penh International Airport, which may need from 25,000 cubic meters to 27,000 cubic meters per day.
The project to expand Takhmao water production capacity uses a total construction budget of 3,421 million yen or about 30 million US dollars.
