Ministry of Economy and Finance issues a decision on mechanisms and procedures for implementing cash assistance programs for families severely affected by floods
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance has issued a decision on the mechanism and procedures for implementing social assistance programs in cash for vulnerable families affected by floods in order to start providing subsidies to victims. According to the decision of the Ministry of Economy, which was received by Fresh News on December 6, 2022.
This decision applies to vulnerable families who have been severely affected by the floods in 16 provinces, including Phnom Penh, Kandal, Takeo, Pursat, Battambang, Banteay Meanchey, Siem Reap, Kampong Thom, Kampong Cham, Tbong Khmum, Kratie, Kampong Chhnang, Prey Veng, Kampot, Svay Rieng and Oddar Meanchey.
The Social Assistance Program for Flood-Affected Families, which is severely affected by the floods, must be implemented once a month for three months, using the existing mechanism of the Cash Support Program for poor and vulnerable households. During the fight against Kovid 19 under the auspices of the National Social Assistance Fund.
According to the announcement received by Fresh News, the writing process of the high school diploma exam took place over two days, on December 5 and 6, 2022, with a total of 128,135 candidates registered for the exam. 68771 females, 221 examination centers, and 5174 rooms.
The writing process was co-organized by a total of 17,240 judges and committees across the country, a total of 2756 student assistants, 350 members of the Anti-Corruption Unit and 2,700 capital and provincial observers. People.
According to the Ministry of Education, in this year's exam, a total of 2,400 candidates were absent, accounting for 1.87% of the total candidates (1036 females), 70 candidates had health problems, including 4 minor traffic accidents and suspected positive Kovid 19 has four cases. There were 3 cases of candidates who could not continue the writing process due to health problems, 14 members of the jury had health problems, 1 of whom was in serious condition and was sent to the hospital.
Although it rained in some provinces, it did not affect the candidates' writing process. Candidates have complied well with the rules of the exam. Candidates make 1 mistake.
The writing process ended at 4:30 pm on December 6, 2022. Candidate transcripts and exam-related documents will be thoroughly inspected and sent to Phnom Penh on December 7, 2022 to prepare for the revision process.
The Ministry states that, in general, the writing phase of the Higher Secondary Diploma Examination, examination period: December 5, 2022, was conducted in accordance with the principles of law, transparency, justice and acceptable results, and in accordance with the principle of "those who know are successful".
