Mr. Ith Sam Heng stated that the ASEAN Engineering Federation Conference has made a significant contribution to the promotion of goodwill and mutual understanding, which is a necessary requirement for the establishment and development of ASEAN Engineering Professional Standards as a step towards Towards the mobilization of engineers in the ASEAN region in line with the ASEAN Master Plan 2025 and the core of ASEAN is one vision, one identity and one community.
In addition, to accelerate ASEAN's transition to Industry 4.0, focusing on SME start-ups, smart cities and vocational education, the Minister also encouraged all members of the ASEAN Engineering Federation. Focuses on the feasibility study of new mechanisms and the creation of an open platform to support government in education and industry, including the promotion of digital connectivity.
Share information, experiences and best practices on the formulation and implementation of industry promotion policies 4.0.
Develop an ASEAN Integration Strategy on Industrial Development 4.0, emphasizing the promotion of innovation and the technology industry.
Strengthen cooperation in the development of legal frameworks to support ASEAN-to-Industry Transformation 4.0 through public-private dialogue with partnerships with international organizations and development partners to facilitate compliance and certification of digital standards; Cross-border data and develop a common platform for linking industry statistics through the use of digital technology.
Participate in solving the challenges that will arise from the growth of Industry 4.0 in ASEAN and find solutions to meet those challenges.
