China completes space rice cultivation experiment
(Beijing): Rice is the most important food crop of mankind, feeding about half of the world's population. Researchers at the Chinese Academy of Sciences have completed the world's first space-based rice-seeding experiment.
CCTV.com reported on December 5 that the rice breeding experiment started on July 29, 2022 and ended on November 25, 2022, for a total of 120 days in the space station room. China, which has completed the experimental stages of germination, flowering and grain transfer.
