Minister Ith Sam Heng: Cambodia may host ASEAN Digital Engineers Workshop in March 2023
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia may host the ASEAN Digital Engineers Workshop in March 2023 to better share experiences and information from each other. This is according to Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training.
The statement was made during a meeting with the President of the ASEAN Federation of Engineers, led by Bambang Goeritno, Secretary General of the Indonesian Institute of Engineers, to discuss the progress of the ASEAN Engineering Federation's efforts so far. The meeting was held after the opening of the 40th ASEAN Engineering Federation Conference held at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh on the morning of December 6, 2022.
On that occasion, the Minister requested the support of representatives of ASEAN engineering institutions to initiate the ASEAN Digital Engineers Workshop, which Cambodia can host during March 2023 to share experiences and Information from each other for the better.
In addition, representatives of the ASEAN Engineering Institutions fully supported the Minister's initiative to organize the ASEAN Digital Engineers Workshop hosted by Cambodia.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng would like to see the ASEAN Engineering Federation play a more important role in contributing to the development of the engineering sector and want to see the engineering skills of all countries in the ASEAN region more. Cambodia-Australia Holds Workshop on Knowledge Exchange on Wastewater
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ros Vanna, Secretary of State, Representative of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, on December 6, 2022, presided over the opening ceremony of the Cambodia-Australia Knowledge Exchange Workshop on Wastewater.
The workshop was attended by the Australian Embassy, leaders of relevant ministries, institutions of Phnom Penh administration, representatives of development partners, as well as officials of the Department of Public Works and Transport of the capital-province.
