The people expressed their deep gratitude to the leaders at all levels and the team of volunteer doctors.
During the pre-departure meeting of the two exchange teams, General Sem Sovanny, Vice Chairman of the National Committee and Director General of the National Peacekeeping Center, stated that Cambodia has contributed to the deployment of peacekeeping forces within the framework of the United Nations. Nations to help countries facing and affected by landmines and explosive remnants of war and to participate in infrastructure construction and airport maintenance.
The General stated that Cambodia has become one of the leading countries in sending its deminers to alleviate the suffering of the people of the world.
From 2006 to 2022, Cambodia has decided to send a total of 8,475 peacekeepers to nine countries, including Sudan, South Sudan, Chad, Central Africa, Lebanon, Cyprus, Syria, Mali and Yemen.
More than 800 Cambodian Blue Hat troops are currently on peacekeeping missions in South Sudan, Lebanon, Mali and the Republic of Central Africa. Preah Vihear Meanchey Agricultural Community Union and Cambodian Standard Company Sign a Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation in Promoting Agricultural Product Chains in Preah Vihear Province
(Preah Vihear): The Preah Vihear Meanchey Agricultural Community Union and Cambodian Standard Development Co., Ltd. on the morning of December 6, 2022, held a signing ceremony of a Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation for the Promotion of Agricultural Products Chain in Cambodia. Preah Vihear Province.
The event was attended by Mr. Peng Trida, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, and attended by Mr. Tek Sophea, General Director of Cambodian Standard Development Co., Ltd., Mr. Nuon Dey, Chairman of Preah Vihear Meanchey Agricultural Community Union and Many more involved.
Mr. Tek Sophea stated that Cambodian Standard Development Co., Ltd. was established in 2009 as an agricultural company and collects produce as well as agricultural products from local farmers. The main goal of the company is to help increase the potential of production in Cambodia, as well as create jobs to reduce poverty, especially the migration of farmers.
He said that the company will create jobs locally as well as create agricultural productivity will promote the possibility of cultivation in our country. The partnership with Preah Vihear Meanchey Agricultural Community Union today is a new starting point as well as the beginning of a new era for the company in capturing potential areas for organic rice production, as well as some other products. There are cashews, cassava and other crops.
Mr. Tek Sophea requested the Preah Vihear Meanchey Agricultural Community Union to jointly produce safe agricultural products because the company will not only supply locally, but also export to European and Arab markets. The company will be able to order between 500 tonnes and 1,000 tonnes, 2,000 tonnes if orders are from the European Union and other overseas trading partners.
Separately, Mr. Peng Trida said that Preah Vihear province has 43 agricultural communities with more than 10,000 families, focusing on organic rice, cashews, potatoes, peanuts and some vegetables.
He said that the process of contracting to buy and sell organic rice in Preah Vihear province as of this year has been 6.7 years, and they have high experience related to the implementation of contract farming with honesty, making partners confident.
Vietnamese man arrested by Phnom Penh police and sent to court in connection with torture and possession of drugs
(Phnom Penh): A Vietnamese national was arrested by the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal punishment in connection with the torture of a Vietnamese national and the possession of drugs.
Colonel San Sok Seiha, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, told Fresh News on the afternoon of December 6, 2022 that the suspect was arrested by police at Kob Srov Road, Trapeang Reang Chas Village, Khmuonh Commune. Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh on December 3 and was sent to court on December 6.
According to a spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, the suspect was identified as 25-year-old Chang Ngong Thang alias Thang, while the victim, 29-year-old Vieng Veng Lin, suffered bruises on his back. The police confiscated a handkerchief and a white gram (suspected to be a drug, a bag of the suspect).
According to the police report, on December 2, 2022, before the incident, the suspects, 25-year-old Chang Ngong Thang and five other unidentified accomplices, brought the victims, Vieng Veng Leung and Vieng Van Chung, riding The bus from Kampong Som to Phnom Penh stayed at a guesthouse in Prek Pnov for one night.
On the morning of December 3, 2022, an unidentified suspect handed over a black handkerchief and a small bag of drugs to the suspect, Chang Ngong Thang, in his pants pocket, then the suspect came to the room. The victim rested and told the victim that they would take them to work as laborers for a Chinese man named Vieng Van Chung, while the victim refused. Bruises.
Afterwards, the victim was taken into an unknown car by a gray mother from Twee Damney Guesthouse to a restaurant on Kob Srov Road (Khmuonh Sangkat). Fleeing immediately, the suspect and his accomplices chased after him, causing a commotion.
At that time, the police of Khmuonh police station received the information and immediately intervened and arrested the suspect named Chang Ngong Thang, finding a black knot and a white transparent gram, suspected to be a small package of drugs in the suspect's pocket. His name is Chang Ngong Thang. After questioning the suspect, Chang Ngong Thang admitted that he and five other unidentified accomplices actually used a cheese stick and an electric baton to hit the victim, causing real injuries.
The suspects have now been sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal action, while the two victims have been questioned by the competent authorities, but no documents, including passports, have been forwarded to them. The Department of Investigation and Enforcement of the General Department of Immigration to seek the principle of deportation from Cambodia.
The Ministry of Environment continues to provide training on standard operating procedures for the investigation and money laundering offenses that extend from the original offenses of natural resource offenses to law enforcement officers under the Ministry.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment has continued to open training courses on guidelines on standard operating procedures and procedures for investigating and preparing criminal cases and money laundering offenses that extend from the original crime of natural resource crime to officials. Judicial police and law enforcement officers of the units under the Ministry.
The training was held on the morning of December 6, 2022 under the chairmanship of Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Permanent Deputy Chairman of the Anti-Money Laundering Task Force of the Ministry of Environment, and was attended by judicial police officers and law enforcement officers. 100 people.
Mr. Pheaktra said that all judicial police officers have an important role to play in enforcing relevant laws against money laundering and terrorist financing.
He stressed the importance of strengthening the capacity of judicial police and law enforcement officers in enforcing anti-money laundering and terrorist financing and financing, which has led to the proliferation of weapons of mass destruction resulting from natural resource crimes.
The Secretary of State stressed that the Ministry of Environment has actively cooperated with the relevant ministries and institutions of the Royal Government to strengthen the mechanisms and permanent working system of the Ministry of Environment in combating money laundering and terrorist financing and increase the effectiveness of money laundering prevention.
