A New House Donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to the Families of Veterans in Kampong Thom Province
(Kampong Thom): A new house, a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, was handed over to the family of a veteran victim in Meanchey commune, Sandan district, Kampong Thom province, Mrs. Mey Kan, 64 years old, who is the wife of Brigadier General Kim Roeun. He served in the army in 1992 in the 5th Battalion, Kampong Thom province, but due to malaria and old wounds, he died in 2010.
Lt. Gen. Som Sun stated that seeing that Mey Kan's livelihood was difficult and she could not afford to build a suitable house on her own, the committee of the Kampong Thom Provincial Association of Cambodian Veterans with the approval of General Kun Kim Akka The Secretary of the Cambodian Veterans Association decided to build a house for him now, the back of the 228th house of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen.
Lt. Gen. Som Sun said that the construction of this house is high above the ground, concrete pillars, steel bones, planks, wall boards, smart roofs, galvanized roofs and stairs.
During the handover ceremony, Lt. Gen. Som Sun also brought the gifts of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet and Ms. Pech Chanmony to the families of the veterans, Ms. Mey Kan, including 50 kg of rice, 2 boxes of noodles, fish sauce 2 Soy sauce and kitchen utensils such as pots, plates, spoons, metal plates and other items, as well as some budget.
Ms. Mey Kan and her family expressed their gratitude and best wishes to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as Mr. Hun Manet and her, as well as to the Committee of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Kampong Thom Province. Citizens are committed to continuing to support Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Citizens request Phnom Penh authorities to prevent gangsters from burglary and expedite the provision of housing ownership in the forum and consultation.
(Phnom Penh): In the Dissemination and Consultation Forum of Phnom Penh Capital Council at the National Olympic Stadium, Sangkat Veal Vong, Khan 7 Makara, on the morning of December 6, 2022, the people requested and requested the authorities to help repair the stairs. Ask for help to prevent gangsters, prevent burglars and request to help speed up the provision of home ownership.
The forum was held in the presence of Mr. Mop Sarin, Chairman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Council and Ms. Keo Sok Pisey, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, representing Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh. At this forum, people raised 4 questions and requests orally and 7 written requests.
For oral questions and requests, including residents of Village 5, Sangkat Orussey IV, requested and requested the authorities to help repair the stairs, as the stairs were rotten and could be dangerous to dozens of families. Residents of Village 12, Sangkat Veal Rong, asked to help prevent gangsters, burglars and asked to help speed up the provision of home ownership, while Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, paid close attention to this issue.
Regarding the above-mentioned oral request by Mr. Theng Sothol, the Governor of Makara District, he confirmed that he had already sent a professional officer to study the request to repair the stairs in Village 5, Sangkat Orussey IV. He added that the repair of the stairs together is not just done, that is, it requires a study of the technical characteristics before it can be repaired to avoid accidents. However, the authorities have taken care of this work.
South Korea's exports are expected to fall 4 percent by 2023 after rising 7.1 percent in 2022, Reuters reported, citing a trade outlook report released by KITA. The highest amount is $ 690 billion, or probably the sixth largest in the world.
The decline will be the first annual decline since 2020, when exports from Asia's fourth-largest economy fell 5.5 percent due to the Kovid epidemic. 19 disrupted the global supply chain.
"However, both exports and imports will decline due to the ongoing conflict between the United States and China and the effects of worsening external conditions over the last two years," the association added. After this.
As a result, South Korea's annual trade deficit will narrow to $ 13.8 billion next year, after a deficit of $ 45 billion for the full 2022 period. According to a Reuters report.
