Separately, some of the money she will use to organize a cultural village to attract tourists to visit. In addition, she would also like to invite guests to visit and hold with the elephant, especially at the association that cares for elephants. US Investors See Cambodia as a Key Food Stamp Contributing to Global Food Security
(Phnom Penh): A group of US investors see Cambodia as an important food warehouse to contribute to ensuring global food security. US investors also highlighted that the global crisis is causing the United States to face high inflation and that Cambodia is one of the key players in solving this problem.
US investors made the remarks at a keynote meeting with Commerce Minister Pan Sosak on December 5, 2022.
The meeting between Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, and the US delegation of investors and business people was organized under the coordination of Mr. Huot Kimcha, Honorary Consul General of the Cambodian Embassy in Long Beach. This is an important meeting to expand trade and investment cooperation between Cambodia and the United States, one of Cambodia's largest markets.
At the meeting, a US company representative informed the Secretary of Commerce that the ongoing crisis in the region and the world has made the United States one of the countries affected by the sharp rise in commodity prices. In the specialty markets are food and agricultural products.
The US delegation of investors said that Cambodia is an important warehouse of agricultural products that can play an important role in ensuring food security in the region and the world, especially the United States. Cambodia's main potential commodities include: cashew nuts, mango, pepper, salt, fish sauce, soy sauce, eggs, fish, oranges, Pursat, snacks, rice and plywood products.
In response, the Minister of Commerce extended a warm welcome and thanked the US delegation for their commitment to investing and exporting agricultural products from Cambodia to the US and global markets.
The Minister said that in order to facilitate export to foreign markets and avoid the problems of phytosanitary and product standards, the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia has encouraged US investors and traders to invest in processing and packaging. Direct agricultural products in Cambodia first and then export, rather than exporting fresh agricultural products without pre-processing.
The Minister of Commerce added that some Cambodian agricultural products have already received GI registration, while others are in the process of applying, which shows that Cambodian agricultural products are high quality and have International recognition.
