Senior Health Officer: The practice of midwifery is the provision of health services, not a trading profession, must consider the client first, do not go beyond skills
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Thea Kruy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chairman of the National Medical Council, stated that the practice of midwifery is to provide health services, not to trade, is a case to be considered. Customers in advance and have a duty to prevent illness and to provide understanding because customers come to us, both sick and healthy.
This statement was made by the professor at the seminar disseminating the decision on the implementation of professional limits and professional standards for midwives in Cambodia, which took place on December 5, 2022 at the Phnom Penh Hotel.
Professor Thea Kruy said that all midwives working in midwifery are important because they need to take care of women, both normal and sick, to ensure that they live a balanced life to ensure time. Pregnancy, postpartum, postpartum, mother and baby are healthy.
"Midwifery is not a trade or business, midwifery is a job that we have to do and must first consider the interests of our patients or clients, then our own interests are different. "Businesses that start trading think of him first, but midwives, please remember that we are working on the health and life of our clients, we must consider him first and provide a quality and effective service."
