Japanese company provides futsal court to Tonle Bati National Football School
(Phnom Penh): Japan's Taika Corporation has built an artificial grass football field for the Tonle Bati National Football Center and School to support football in Cambodia.
The handover ceremony of the futsal court was held on December 3, 2022, presided over by Mr. Sao Sokha, President of the Football Federation of Cambodia and Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia. The event was also attended by Mr. Suzuki Tito, CEO of Taika Corporation, the management of the National Football Center and School, as well as students who are training football in the center.
Tonle Bati National Football Center and School is a major training ground for sports, especially football in Cambodia. This training requires facilities to support student training.
Mr. Sao Sokha expressed his deep gratitude to the Japanese company Tai Kha for building the futsal court. He stressed that the football field responds to the need for training in the center.
Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, commended Tai Kha for its contribution to the promotion of sports in Cambodia. The Ambassador considers the sports support from Japanese companies also contributing to the improvement of relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Japan as the two countries reach the age of 70 by 2023.
The Japanese company Tai Kha has contributed greatly to the support of football in Cambodia. The company used to build a futsal court for the Cambodia-Japan Friendship School in Prey Veng province and for Prek Leap High School.
Mr. Suzuki Tito, CEO of TaiCa Corporation, emphasized that Cambodia and Japan have a good relationship for a long time, so he will do his best to help strengthen good relations through sports. The CEO of Tai Kha has confirmed that he will continue to build more artificial turf futsal stadiums in Cambodia to support football training.
