(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Mine Authority and forces, has re-launched plans to increase mine clearance faster to achieve the goal of a mine-free Cambodia by 2025. There are more than 700 square kilometers of minefields.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch continued, "In order to achieve the goal of a landmine-free Cambodia by 2025, the Mine Authority and stakeholders have put in place a plan to strengthen demining work more efficiently and faster." "All improve their work efficiency and speed up more than 200 to 300 square kilometers per year to be successful."
Senior Minister Ly Thuch added that in addition, stakeholders called on all operators to improve safety and avoid accidents due to demining work, the Mine Authority and all forces continue to work together to complete the procedure. Existing streamlines the work and urges all parties to be informed of the progress of demining work and to develop a specific plan.
