It is remembered that 2014 was the time of the beginning of the unprecedented restrictions on the bankruptcy process after Hang Chuon Naron was trusted by the Royal Government to be the Minister of Education.
The Baccalaureate is an important testament to the 12 years of general education of a student. Before 2014, the Baccalaureate exam was seen as so lax that some students were so overwhelmed that they stopped worrying about their studies and waited for a copy when they returned. This habit has reduced the quality of education of some students until some students end up failing to read and write Khmer script almost incorrectly.
But since 2014, things have changed. Mr. Hang Chuon Naron not only strives to improve the quality of education in the classroom, but he also set strict rules during the exam without any plagiarism. The rigor of the exam not only helps to improve the exam, but also signals to the students to wake up and study without having to rely on copying.
The Minister of Education emphasized, "What we are happy to see is that our students are working hard to learn and change their attitudes from coming to the exam on the basis of their knowledge."
The Minister emphasized that the success of the Baccalaureate exam as well as the general education education has four important factors, including: the principal factor, the teacher factor, the student factor and the parental involvement. In addition, the honor of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, for the A-level students to meet in person, is also a motivating factor for the students to study hard to get this rare opportunity.
Education at the general education level is an important knowledge base for learners before they set foot in higher education. If general education is not good, it will make it difficult to study higher education.
Mr. Hun Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, who has been an active participant since 2014 on the process of reforming the Baccalaureate, expressed his support and saw that the reform of the Baccalaureate is very important for education. Mr. Hun Many called this reform in line with global development.
