Mr. HUN Many: Saying that Cambodian children's diplomas are not valuable is a personal opinion and a disgrace to the Cambodian people themselves (Phnom Penh) Like other countries, Mr. Hun Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia (UYFC), stated that such a statement is a personal opinion and only a disgrace to the Cambodian people.
This morning, December 5, 2022, Mr. Hun Many, on the occasion of accompanying Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, opened the 2022 Baccalaureate exam at Preah Sisowath High School.
Mr. Hun Many said, "The education system, youth and sports, especially our education system has never been a problem, we have a series of stages, although some people say that the degree of Cambodian children is not as valuable as this country. That country is a personal opinion and a derogatory opinion of the Cambodian people themselves and the system of the nation itself.
"But for me, if our education system has human resource problems that support all aspects of the country, society, economy, it will not lead to Cambodia to grow as it is today," he said.
In the past, opposition groups abroad, especially Sam Rainsy, have attacked the Cambodian education system, mocking the country's diplomacy. This criticism led to a series of reactions from many Cambodians.
Mr. Hun Many believes that what has led to the development of the Cambodian education system so far is what Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, when he took over as Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, is to reform it in line with the context of The need for global evolution, in which the education system also plays a fundamental role, and general knowledge must evolve in the same context, as it could have been 10 to 15 years ago.
Mr. Hun Many added that for the long-term vision of the leadership of the Minister of Education in the reform of education is really important, our education system is not a problem, but we need to evolve according to the context and the resources. The Cambodian people are the foundation for us to grasp any skill in line with the context, and the most important resource, no matter what the country, is human resources.
In addition, Mr. HUN Many, as a Cambodian citizen, also asked all teachers, guardians of students to have confidence in the Royal Government, especially the Ministry of Education and all stakeholders who participated and thanked the students. Have worked hard to strengthen their ability from year to year and already know themselves well, you know is stuck.
