Chinese astronaut returns to Earth successfully after six-month mission at Chinese space station
BEIJING (Reuters) - Three Chinese astronauts successfully returned to Earth on Sunday after completing a six-month mission on a Chinese space station, state-run CCTV reported. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Sunday, December 4, 2022.
The space station is a milestone in China's three-decade manned space program, first adopted in 1992, and also marks the beginning of China's permanent stay in space.
Construction of the station began in April last year with the launch of the first and largest of its three modules, Tianhe, the home of the visiting astronauts.
China has built its own station after it was withdrawn from the International Space Station due to US opposition to the Chinese space program's close ties with the People's Liberation Army, the military wing of the ruling Communist Party. Hold power.
