So far, there have been no reports of casualties from the eruption of Semeru, which occurred at around 3am. The Indonesian Ministry of Transport said air travel was unaffected but sent a message to two airports in the area to remain vigilant.
The Indonesian Disaster Management Agency (BNPB) said 1,979 people had been evacuated to 11 shelters and authorities were distributing masks as rescue and search-and-rescue efforts continued. Go.
