The Tehran government on Sunday executed four people convicted of collaborating with Israel's Mossad intelligence agency, state media reported. This was released by the AFP news agency on Sunday, December 4, 2022.
The execution comes after state media in Iran reported on Wednesday that the Supreme Court of Iran had upheld the death sentences of four men for crimes committed in collaboration with the Israeli spy network. . The detainees have been detained since June, before protests erupted across Iran.
The Islamic Republic has long accused Israel, the region's top enemy, of carrying out secret intelligence operations in its territory. In particular, Tehran has recently accused Israeli spies, including the West, of inciting civil war in Iran, which has been plagued by large-scale anti-government protests in recent months.
