Speaking at the Closing Ceremony of the ASEAN Governors' Forum (AMF) 2022 on December 3, 2022, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, expressed his deep gratitude for the active participation with a realistic vision and consideration. In a constructive sense, help each other to contribute to improving the discussion on all aspects, which are all recommendations for the common direction of the development of ASEAN cities in the sub-national administration.
Mr. Khuong Sreng emphasized that the challenges facing the current situation and the global perspective and the future of ASEAN city leaders agreed on the importance of partnership and cooperation for sub-national administrations in responding to common challenges. Based on the spirit of solidarity and high responsibility, which is an essential basis for promoting economic and social recovery after the Kovid 19 crisis.
In addition, it has accelerated the development of smart, resilient and sustainable smart cities with a new and normal environment, as we have identified as the theme of this year's ASEAN Mayors' Forum.
He said that the forum held in-depth discussions on the importance and necessity of good cooperation among ASEAN capitals, provincial administrations, sister cities and ASEAN cities in order to promote smart, resilient and sustainable cities. Sustainability, especially in the context of digital technology modernization as well as the global crisis caused by Kovid 19.
According to Mr. Khuong Sreng, through this forum and meeting, two historical documents were achieved, namely: 1: Joint Statement of the ASEAN Capital and Capital Governors 'Meeting with 6 points and 2: Statement of the Governors' Forum ASEAN Cities (AMF) or Phnom Penh Declaration 2022, which has 12 points, which is appropriate to the set topic.
These two historical documents really reflect the common will and commitment of the Governors / Deputy Governors of the capitals, capitals, provinces and cities of the ASEAN Member States to work together to move forward together and promote cooperation. Closer operations to build smart, resilient and sustainable cities to serve inclusive economic growth and prosperity in line with the ASEAN Community Vision 2025 and beyond 2025.
