Article 1 of the Sub-Decree: Established the Cambodian Mine Action Fund 2025, abbreviated as "CCHR-2025" to manage the budget for clearing mines and unexploded ordnance and clearing suspected areas. Mine and Unexploded Ordnance to support the Cambodian goal of demining by 2025.
Article 2 of the sub-decree states that the resources for the fund are from: * The initial phase of the state budget is 123,180 million Riels, equivalent to approximately $ 30 million.
* Contribution to the state budget for 2023, 2024 and 2025 as necessary and contributions from other legal sources.
After receiving approval from the Prime Minister, the Cambodian Authority for Mine Action and Mine Action Disabled must prepare a budget request to the Ministry of Economy and Finance for review and provision.
The flames of war from the late 1960s to the late 1990s left millions of landmines and unexploded ordnance strewn across Cambodia. For 30 years, Cambodia has been working to clear mines and unexploded ordnance from the ground to provide a safe and smiling land for the Cambodian people. However, this clearance is not yet complete, Cambodia has set 2025 to clear all landmines in Cambodia.
The issuance of the Sub-Decree on the Establishment of the Cambodian Mine Action Fund 2025 is another strong commitment of the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to clear mines, bring safe land and bring a smile to the people of Cambodia.
Five Cambodian capitals and provinces have been declared demining, including Stung Treng, Kep, Prey Veng, Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville. The next provinces that will be declared demining under the Samdech Techo project for mine action "Provide safe land, create a smile" include Tbong Khmum, Kampong Cham, Kampong Chhnang, Takeo, Kampot, Svay Rieng, Kampong Speu and Kratie. Cambodian Minister of Commerce Visits Ngov Heng Kampot Fish Sauce Production Line to Boost Exports to South Korea
