Mr. Khuong Sreng: The exchange of views of the representatives of ASEAN capitals and capitals confirms the strong commitment together to achieve a more cohesive ASEAN community in all areas
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, said that the exchange of views through the presentation of the representatives of ASEAN capitals and capitals and participation in the discussion clearly highlighted our strong commitment. Together to achieve the building of an ASEAN community that is more cohesive in all areas.
Mr. Khuong Sreng's speech was made at the closing ceremony of the 2022 ASEAN Capital and Capital Governors' Meeting on "Promoting Comprehensive Cooperation for a Clean, Resilient and Sustainable City" on the evening of December 2. This year 2022, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will host. The meeting took place at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Khuong Sreng affirmed that the cohesiveness of the ASEAN community, whether at the national or sub-national level, for the ASEAN nations, the people of the capitals-capitals through the construction of smart, resilient and sustainable cities. This is in line with the theme of the recent 40-41 ASEAN Summit: "ASEAN Working Together: Solving Challenges Together."
According to Mr. Khuong Sreng, during the meeting, the ASEAN Capital Governors successfully exchanged views and recommendations, and it can be said that this meeting has become a meaningful forum that allows the parties All share knowledge, experience and excellence around the development of capitals, capitals and cities and promote closer cooperation between stakeholders for ASEAN economic growth and common prosperity.
In fact, the meeting approved and signed a six-point declaration, reflecting on the importance of cooperation between the 10 capitals and capitals of ASEAN member countries, namely the Central Capital. ASEAN capitals are the main driving force for achieving the overall growth and prosperity of the countries in the region.
The Governor of Phnom Penh emphasized that no matter what the situation, if we maintain the spirit of unity, solidarity and good cooperation, we can work together to solve and prevent challenges for our ASEAN-Capital families effectively and efficiently. High.
Phnom Penh strongly believes that the Jakarta capital of the Republic of Indonesia, which will host the upcoming "ASEAN Governors' Meeting and Capitals Meeting 2023", will continue to lead the sub-national administrations of ASEAN member countries to achieve Get more new achievements like what we are working together to achieve today.
