ASEAN Governors and Capital Capitals Discuss Group Focusing on Balancing Sustainable Urban Development Plans and ASEAN Local Governments
(Phnom Penh): Implementation of Sustainable Development Goals at the grassroots level is a key topic in the discussions of the ASEAN Governors' Forum (AMF) and the ASEAN MGMAC 2022 Capital and Capital Governors Meeting to explore cooperation and implementation of inclusive development goals. Sustainability that balances urban sustainable development plans at each and regional levels, as well as at ASEAN local administrations.
At the beginning of the discussion, Mr. Long Dimanche mentioned the potential that Sihanoukville already has and that Sihanoukville is a province that receives as much attention as other provincial capitals from the Royal Government of Cambodia.
He said that in recent years, the Sihanoukville administration has expanded its image to become more modern and smarter by constantly launching sub-national development strategies in all areas, especially infrastructure and providing opportunities for investors. Foreigners are investing to revive the economy after the 19-crisis Kovid, which has delayed its progress to achieve the SDGs or sustainable development goals.
He said the talks were an exchange of experiences on the strategic development plans of each city, including the challenges that have arisen, and compared them to those set by the United Nations. Respond to any level to address towards achieving sustainable urban development goals.
According to Long Dimanche, the implementation of the UN Sustainable Development Plan is very important to meet the goals that truly serve the interests of the people. The opinions and experiences raised in this discussion will be incorporated into the Joint Statement of the ASEAN Mayors 'Forum and the ASEAN Capital Governors' Meeting 2022 on December 3, 2022.
It should be noted that the AMF Forum and MGMAC 2022 have organized 5 discussion groups, the first discussion: focusing on the financing of sustainable projects for urban development, the second discussion: the implementation of development goals. Sustainable at the grassroots level, 3rd: Digital Governance, 4th: Sustainable ASEAN Urban Planning, and 5th: Urban Climate Resilience and Disaster Risk Reduction in ASEAN.
