(Kampong Chhnang): Ancient Khmer art and tradition is returning to modernity with the Autumn Festival, a two-day grueling ceremony held to celebrate Khmer culture and heritage in the center of Kampong Chhnang province.
A variety of events will feature a variety of entertainment events, including rice threshing competitions, Khmer kite flying competitions, folk dances, long chapei performances, bokator performances, concerts, and fireworks display. Great and there are many other programs that will take place in the territory of Damnak Kak Koh village, Po commune, Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province to contribute to the promotion of Khmer culture.
"Autumn Festival" is a mass event of the autumn season in Cambodia, coinciding with the time when Cambodians across the country have been harvesting rice, punching, flying kites and celebrating the new season in villages and districts. .
The purpose of this festival is to join the Royal Government, led by Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, as a wise leader and long-term vision, especially in efforts to promote, preserve and preserve Ancient traditions are very long ago.
It should be noted that the Autumn Festival is held for 3 days, on December 2, 2022 in the territory of Teuk Phos district, Kampong Chhnang province and on December 17 and 18 in the territory of Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province. Today's program (December 2) is the first part of the ambok boxing competition called the rice harvest competition. Harvesting competitions include threshing, threshing, and threshing to select the grain for the second stage, the punching competition.
The main events of the Autumn Festival include the Dok Ambok competition and the kite flying competition, which is attended by representatives of each district of Kampong Chhnang province. Eight members from 6 districts equal to 64 people, while the kite flying competition has 11 teams in a group of 4 members equal to 44 people.
The first place winner will receive 4 million Riel, the second place winner will receive 3 million Riel, the third place winner will receive 2 million Riel, there will be a consolation prize for the non-winning team. The winner in each group is 1 million riels. Other important programs of the Autumn Festival include:
• Autumn harvest parade includes rice, palm juice, palm fruit, sugar cane, cakes, pastries, cakes, mixed fruits in season, with about 500 participants. • Kite flying of all kinds, recreation • Local traditional dance performances; Classical dance; Chapey Dang Veng; Theater; • 15 types of popular games • Community product exhibitions and fall markets • Concerts featuring famous singers and artists
• Serey Soursdey Lantern Launch and Fireworks Launch
He added that the Eng Fund Design is highly committed to continuing to organize this fall festival every year. In addition, we will organize other mass events such as marathons in the near future.
The Ing Foundation Design has a mission to promote the rich culture, traditions and customs of the Khmer people, the soul of the nation, to lively and to improve the lives of the people in Kampong Leng district and the people around this area who will directly benefit. From the conservation and development of eco-tourism in the area of the Foundation.
In addition to promoting Cambodian culture and traditions, the Eng Foundation has focused on a number of other social activities, including capacity building for local students in Kampong Leng, support for Buddhism, participation in environmental protection, forest protection, and wildlife and biodiversity presence. Diversification and participation in local development such as roads, water and sanitation.
Looking at the opportunity to train the human resource nursery during this great event, Duke Ing Bun Hou organized the recruitment of 150 young students of Kampong Leng High School as volunteers to facilitate the Autumn Festival. Trained by Phleung Kob, a company with a reputation for casting and rich experience in organizing traditional cultural arts events.
Through this training, all students will gain both knowledge, skills and experience to prepare a good standard program, which is part of the development of hard and soft skills for them. This is also an opportunity for all students to start thinking about their future careers well.
