He said that currently Tbong Khmum province has two protected areas, including: Ponhea Krek multi-use area in Trapeang Phlong commune and Krek commune, Ponhea Krek district, with an area of 199 hectares and Boeung Kadey multi-use area. It is located in Chumnic Commune, Rokar Khnor Commune, Chhouk Commune, Krouch Chhmar District and Seda Commune, Tambor District and covers an area of 1643 hectares.
At the same time, the provincial administration has been studying the designation of two more natural protected areas, including the first: the flooded forest area of Khmong, located in Tbong Khmum district, and the second area: Boeung Krapit, located in Ou Raing Ov district.
In order to protect the environment in the cities / districts, there are also 3 garbage collection companies providing garbage collection services, such as 1: Pun Ches Company provides garbage collection services in Ou Raing Ov and Tbong Khmum districts, 2: Pech Kim Sea Company Provide garbage collection service in Ponhea Krek and Memot districts and 3: Cintri provides garbage collection service in Suong city and Tambor district as well.
