Senior Foreign Ministry official: The proliferation of weapons of mass destruction is a threat to world security
(Phnom Penh): Luy David, Secretary of State for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, said that the proliferation of weapons of mass destruction is a threat to world security, which is of concern to the people and the international community as a whole.
In this sense, each state must freeze the assets of individuals or entities on the UN Security Council sanctions list. This work requires the participation and cooperation of all circles, both physical and legal persons, both public and private, as well as non-governmental organizations.
Luy David said that under the strong commitment of the Royal Government as a member of the United Nations. In the sense of participating in the implementation of the FATF standards, the Royal Government of Cambodia has achieved many important achievements in establishing a comprehensive legal framework and restructuring to prevent and suppress activities against the spread of weapons of mass destruction, such as:
1: Prepared and promulgated the PF Law on June 27, 2020 and prepared three sub-decrees to facilitate the implementation of this law.
2: Launch a campaign to disseminate and provide continuous training on PF law and implementation to all ministries and institutions in Cambodia, including government institutions, the private sector and civil society, as well as the public through training workshops and public outreach roundtables online. Newspapers and official websites of relevant ministries and institutions.
3: At the same time, in view of the implementation of the PF law, which requires each state to freeze without delay the assets of individuals or entities on the UN Security Council sanctions list, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has prepared and submitted Use guidance documents (known as Guidelines) to facilitate the relevant ministries and institutions to take the above steps quickly and effectively.
