For more details, please read the announcement of the Election Commission of Phnom Penh Chamber of Commerce below: Letter to readers: Flexible coordination is the driving force for ASEAN success
This theme shows the efforts to promote the spirit of ASEAN as a single family with ten strong members "all together" working together to achieve common goals to contribute to the building More on maintaining and promoting peace, stability and sustainable development in the region and the world.
In this regard, the key priorities under the pillars of the ASEAN Security-Political Community for ASEAN for 2022 include maintaining and strengthening the ASEAN Center for Peace and Prosperity, promoting regional contribution to world peace by accelerating and expanding Partner with an external partner.
Please be reminded that in the program to transfer and assume the ASEAN chairmanship of Cambodia at the end of 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister emphasized that as the chair of ASEAN in 2022, Cambodia will lead ASEAN to achieve more important achievements. In particular, accelerate the process of building an ASEAN community with equity, strength and environment in line with ASEAN's core spirit of "one vision, one identity and one community."
In this spirit, Cambodia would like to highlight some important work priorities for 2022, including:
First, the political and security pillars: Cambodia will focus on strengthening the ASEAN Community and ASEAN unity, both in regional mechanisms and in cooperation with external partners, based on the ASEAN path and principles as enshrined in the ASEAN Charter, the Treaty of Amity. And Southeast Asian Cooperation and the ASEAN Perspectives on the Indo-Pacific.
ASEAN also needs to be resilient and resilient to the pressures and effects of rising geopolitical competition, transnational crime, terrorism, climate change and epidemics. To ensure peace, security and prosperity.
And Third: Socio-Cultural Pillars: Cambodia will promote the development of human resources to meet the real needs of community building, as well as promote the participation of women and youth in maintaining and building peace and developing an environmentally friendly social protection system. Also. And another important priority is to promote people-to-people communication aimed at strengthening the ASEAN identity.
Overall, Cambodia will continue to mobilize support and cooperation to achieve the goal of building the three ASEAN communities from the ASEAN Community Vision 2025. At the same time, we will also push forward the process of preparing the ASEAN Community Vision for the post-2025 period.
* For regional affairs
Over the last four days, ASEAN and its external partners have had extensive and constructive discussions on many of the most important issues facing our region and the world, such as the alarming security situation, the economic downturn and the economic downturn. Global epidemics, climate change, food and energy crises, etc., and at the same time we discussed potential and practical areas of cooperation that we can work together to move forward together.
Notable achievements during Cambodia's chairmanship of ASEAN this year are Timor-Leste's 11th ASEAN membership after 11 years of strong Cambodian support and Provides observer status to allow Timor-Leste to attend all ASEAN meetings, including the Plenary Meeting of the Summit.
The ASEAN Coordinating Council is tasked with developing the roadmap and submitting it to all ASEAN leaders for approval during the 42nd ASEAN Summit. All ASEAN Member States and external partners must fully support Timor-Leste in achieving those milestones through capacity building and other necessary support for membership. Full rights of Timor-Leste.
The 15-point resolution and assessment of ASEAN leaders on November 10, 2022 states that the situation in Myanmar remains serious and fragile with the escalation of violence, which is a major concern. Not only to Myanmar, but also to the efforts to build the ASEAN community. ASEAN is committed to assisting Myanmar in finding a peaceful and lasting solution to the current crisis.
With little progress achieved in implementing the five-point consensus, the Myanmar military has a role to play in fulfilling its commitment to ASEAN leadership. Another important point of the 15-point resolution and evaluation is that ASEAN needs to consider other ways that can support the implementation of the five-point agreement.
Myanmar's presence was excluded from a series of ASEAN meetings following the military regime came to power in February 2021. For the ASEAN Summit to be held in Phnom Penh this November, Myanmar seats are left vacant.
* For external communication
At the ASEAN Summit, Ukraine signed an instrument of accession to the Treaty of Amity and Cooperation in Southeast Asia (TAC).
He says Ukraine's involvement with the TAC has been on the agenda for many years. But it has finally been achieved and it has taken Ukraine's relations with ASEAN to a new level.
"We will seek and use every opportunity to build deeper relationships with ASEAN countries in the areas of politics, trade, business and food security," Dmytro said. "These are all priorities for both us and ASEAN countries."
The second ASEAN-Australia Summit welcomed new areas of practical cooperation and looked forward to launching the Australia Initiative for the Future of ASEAN. In addition, ASEAN and Canada also held a summit to commemorate the 45th anniversary of their dialogue relationship and pledged to enhance ASEAN-Canada relations to the level of a strategic partnership.
ASEAN and China have adopted three important documents: the ASEAN-China Joint Statement on the 20th Anniversary of the Declaration on the Conduct of Parties in the South China Sea, and the ASEAN-China Joint Statement on Strengthen common and sustainable development, and the ASEAN-China Joint Statement on Food Security Cooperation.
Another success as the chair of ASEAN this year is that the two ASEAN dialogue partners, India and the United States, have upgraded the level of relations to a "comprehensive strategic partner", while Japan also gave a good signal to agree to improve the level of relations. It is also a "comprehensive strategic partnership" with ASEAN and is scheduled to be announced in 2023 at the ASEAN-Japan Summit in Tokyo.
At the ASEAN-US Summit, ASEAN and US leaders agreed to increase cooperation from a strategic partnership to a comprehensive strategic partnership to enhance cooperation in all areas and address common challenges in the region.
Kong Phok, spokesman for the ASEAN Summit, said that ASEAN-US cooperation had reached another level, with US President Joe Biden announcing the establishment of a comprehensive strategic partnership with ASEAN. Therefore, after such an announcement, it is necessary for ASEAN member states and the United States to find out which priority areas should be included in the partnership.
At the ASEAN-India Summit, through this Summit, ASEAN-India also agreed to further enhance relations by continuing to promote existing sectors and increase the focus on people-to-people contacts. People on trade and other potential sectors of the two countries.
At the 19th ASEAN-India Summit, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that over the past three decades, despite the challenges, ASEAN and India have made steady progress and become important socio-economic poles. In the world.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also emphasized that with the results of this development, ASEAN-India cooperation has further developed and has a broader base.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also continued: "Due to the strong commitment to strengthen the partnership so that ASEAN-India has a closer relationship and a higher capacity to ensure and bring peace and prosperity to the people. Our present and future.
At the ASEAN-Japan Summit, the two sides welcomed the ASEAN-Japan Innovative and Sustainable Economic Partnership Plan for 2023 to promote economic cooperation towards the restoration of the supply chain. Resilience, sustainability and innovation.
The 23rd ASEAN-ROK Summit welcomed the good progress in the implementation of its common vision and welcomed the Republic of Korea's intention to achieve a comprehensive ASEAN-ROK Strategic Partnership.
Year of the ASEAN Chairmanship Cambodia welcomed the 25th anniversary of ASEAN Plus Three (APT) Cooperation and commended the framework's contribution to regional priorities. The 17th East Asia Summit (EAS) noted with satisfaction the significant progress adopted under the Manila Action Plan to implement the Phnom Penh Declaration on the East Asia Summit Development Initiative (2018-2022). .
In addition, Cambodia also hosted the Second ASEAN Global Dialogue under the theme "Extensive Recovery after Kovid 19" with the participation of ASEAN leaders, external partners and heads of international institutions.
Finally, we also take the opportunity to announce the major end of the ASEAN-Australia-New Zealand Free Trade Agreement upgrade.
At the ASEAN-UN Summit also expressed concern that the war in Ukraine has severely affected the food, energy crisis for many countries and ASEAN leaders supported the efforts of the UN Secretary-General. Nation in finding a peaceful solution.
* ASEAN and flexibility
Cambodia, the third rotating chair of ASEAN, has tried to act as a facilitator or facilitator as much as possible because ASEAN does not have the strength or power of the United Nations. ASEAN has the power that is part of politics, such as: statements, declarations, condemnations, or acting as a facilitator, as well as providing a place for conflicting counterparts to facilitate negotiations to ease tensions.
For example, as the host of the ASEAN Summit and related summits, Cambodia has tried to coordinate the countries involved. For example, Ukraine also visited and participated in the signing of the Treaty of Amity and Cooperation in Southeast Asia-TAC in Cambodia. This is because Cambodia wants Ukraine to be able to meet with the Russian side to reach an agreement to find a solution, but no meeting has taken place.
ASEAN faces many challenges, especially in 2022, when Cambodia hosts the 40th and 41st ASEAN Summits, at a time when tensions are running high, with some events lingering in the past. . The old problems of ASEAN at each summit are two that have lasted for decades.
First, the problem in the South China Sea or the East Sea
And secondly, the problem on the Korean Peninsula, which is the problem of North Korea. In 2022, the issue of the South China Sea seems to be declining, but it is not over yet, but the issue of North Korea is still heating up and has added three more hot issues: the issue of Myanmar, the issue of the Taiwan Strait. And the war in Ukraine.
Therefore, the role of ASEAN as a whole and the rotating chair of Cambodia, in particular, always plays the role of a flexible, creative and active facilitator during major problems, both regional and international, to seek peaceful solutions to Preserve and strengthen the ASEAN Center for Peace and Prosperity, Harmony, enhance the region's contribution to world peace by accelerating and expanding partnerships with external partners.
By: Ouch Leang Researcher, Department of Asia-Africa and Middle East Studies, Institute of International Relations of Cambodia, Royal Academy of Cambodia
Dr. Ouch Leang, Researcher, Department of Asian, African and Middle Eastern Studies, Institute of International Relations of Cambodia, Royal Academy of Cambodia
