GENEVA (Reuters) - The United Nations (UN) and its partners on Thursday launched an unprecedented $ 51.5 billion fundraiser for 2023, with tens of millions more to come. Further, humanitarian assistance is expected. This was released by the AFP news agency on Thursday, December 1, 2022.
The UN annual report, which assesses global humanitarian needs, estimates that an additional 65 million people will need emergency assistance next year, bringing the total number of people in need to 339 million out of 68. Countries around the world. This figure represents more than 4% of the total population on earth, or equal to the total population in the United States.
