This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presides Over the 11th Anniversary of Japanese Minibia Operations in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Thursday, November 1, 2022, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen presided over the celebration of the 11th anniversary of the operation of the Japanese company Minibia in Cambodia.
The company has stated that in 2019, the company's investment in Cambodia is up to 400 million US dollars and provide employment to more than 6,000 Cambodians.
The company currently has a total investment of 1,124 billion yen ($ 8 billion) in 95 locations worldwide.
Prior to the operation in Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen strongly persuaded the management of this company to invest in Cambodia, while the company is already investing in Thailand. Not only did he try to persuade this company to invest in Cambodia, but Samdech Techo maintained a strong position to protect the company's investment.
Before the company came to invest in Cambodia, a company came to persuade Samdech to cancel the company's investment. But the proposal was rejected by the Prime Minister.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen is considered to be the midwife who created the presence of this large Japanese company in Cambodia.
To date, Minibia has operated and grown significantly in its operations in Cambodia, providing economic benefits for the Cambodian nation and providing many jobs for Cambodians with excellent wages and working conditions.
Mr. Yoshihi Sakainuma, CEO of Minneapolis, was very pleased with the progress of the company in Cambodia and thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for his strong support of the company's investment process.
