View Photo: Closing Ceremony of the 3rd National Sports Competition and the 1st National Sports for the Disabled at Moradok Techo National Stadium
(Phnom Penh): On Wednesday evening, November 30, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the opening ceremony of the 3rd National Sports Competition and the 1st National Sports for the Disabled, which was held at the Techo Heritage National Stadium. .
The 3rd National Games and the 1st National Paralympic Games will be held under the slogan "Sports bring peace and development" for about 12 days, from November 19 to 30.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also emphasized that sports play an important role in strengthening relations, increasing solidarity and promoting social capital, which are important determinants of high efficiency. . The organization and participation in sports competitions increase the ties of friendship and closer cooperation between athletes, as well as ministries, institutions and capitals and provinces that participate in sports.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's presentation of the seven points was made on the occasion that Samdech presided over the closing ceremony of the 3rd National Sports Competition and the 1st National Sports for the Disabled under the slogan "Sport brings peace and Development "which was held at the Moradok Techo National Stadium on Wednesday evening, November 30, 2022.
The seven views and key points of Samdech Techo Hun Sen are as follows:
First, ministries, institutions and capital-provincial authorities that do not yet have sports teams participating in the competition must establish sports units or sports associations in their ministries, institutions, capital-provincial authorities with clear and transparent management mechanisms to manage and increase the capacity of players. - Athletes regularly to participate in national and international competitions.
Second, Ministries, Institutions and Capital-Provincial Authorities must pay attention to the formation of sports teams that are superior and must organize competitions within the internal framework at appropriate times to strengthen the ability of athletes to participate in sports. 4th National and 2nd National Disability Sports to be more.
Third, the National Organizing Committee of the 2023 SEA Games and the ASEAN Para Games must accelerate the pace of readiness to ensure the high level of success in hosting the historic major international sports event. This.
Fourth, all relevant ministries and institutions and capital-provincial authorities must expand close cooperation with a high sense of responsibility and in accordance with the "one-player system" approach to address all challenges urgently. Ensure effective leadership, management and organization of major sporting events in 2023.
Fifth, we call on the private sector, companies, enterprises and philanthropists to join the 2023 SEA Games and ASEAN Para Games Fund to contribute to the success of this international sporting event.
