Samdech Techo Hun Sen's announcement comes after the Intergovernmental Commission for the Protection of Intangible Cultural Heritage of UNESCO approved the inclusion of "Bokator" in the UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity list on 30 November. 2022.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, I would like to take this opportunity to re-announce the success and pride that Cambodia's "bokator" has been inscribed on UNESCO's Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity list. Samdech mentioned three points related to this success, including:
1: First of all, we must thank our ancestors of all generations who try to leave the work to the next generation. If our ancestors did not leave us anything, we would not be able to be inscribed on the World Heritage List or both tangible and intangible.
3: Samdech took this opportunity to thank the Ministry of Culture, Fine Arts and the Arts and the Olympic Committee of Cambodia for their efforts to promote this work until it is achieved. Prior to the ASEAN Summit, Samdech had already received a report on the approval of UNESCO in France, but we have to wait until yesterday when the bell-ringing committee accepted Cambodia's "bokator" as an intangible asset of humanity.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this statement on the occasion of closing the third national sports event and the first national sports for the disabled in 2022 at the Moradok Techo Stadium on the evening of November 30.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the fact that Cambodia's "bokator" was soon included in the UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity list also contributed to the preparation of this martial art in Angkor Sankranti in the past.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "I would also like to confirm to my compatriots all over the country that in the upcoming Khmer New Year, April 2023, we will do Angkor Sankranti again then. "Hopefully, our bokator will become an important symbol of the gathering in Angkor Sankranti at that time."
Please be informed that due to the outbreak of Kovid 19, the event was missed for two years. However, for 2023, the Royal Government has allowed the Siem Reap Provincial Authority to cooperate with relevant institutions to re-organize Angkor Sankranti in the Angkor resort area to attract national and international tourists to enjoy the traditional Khmer New Year. .
