Minister of Labor urges agencies that recruit and send workers abroad to protect workers' rights and interests
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, urged private agencies that select, train, manage and send Cambodian workers abroad to protect the rights and legitimate interests of workers in order to contribute to the protection of the Royal Government. Cambodian workers abroad.
The call was made during the signing ceremony of the Code of Conduct for Cambodian Private Recruitment Agencies and the launch of a pilot evaluation system of code of conduct for Cambodian private recruitment agencies at the Sunway Hotel on the morning of November 30. 2022.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng considered the code of conduct for Cambodian private recruitment agencies as a tool to set the basic principles in accordance with national law and international labor standards for all Cambodian recruitment agencies to implement effectively in a responsible and highly ethical manner. In managing, recruiting, training, sending and managing workers to work abroad.
This code will contribute to strengthening the effectiveness of the protection and promotion of labor rights as well as the well-being of workers both at home and abroad. In addition, this Code will play an important role in supporting the performance of the Cambodian Private Recruitment Agency with accountability and is also a useful resource for migrant workers to confirm the expectations of workers from the Private Recruitment Agency. Related to their work migration experience.
The Code of Conduct for Cambodian Private Recruitment Agencies and the Ethical Testing System for the Implementation of the Code is supported by technical assistance and cooperation from the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and the International Labor Organization, ILO, ACRA and MAC to raise awareness and raise awareness. On fair recruitment to all private recruitment agencies and other stakeholders.
The Minister encouraged all private recruitment agencies licensed by the Ministry to participate in the implementation of this important code of conduct to demonstrate their high commitment to protecting the rights and legitimate interests of workers. .
