The Federation of Cambodian Investors Association sets 11 goals in the 2023 Strategic Plan
(Phnom Penh): In order to participate in development with the Royal Government, the Federation of Investors Federation of Cambodia has been pursuing its strategic plan further, in which the Board of Directors of this association has set 11 goals in its 2023 strategic plan.
The launch of the plan took place during a meeting to review the report on the results of 2022 and 2023 on November 29, 2022 at The Terrace Restaurant, Khan Toul Kork, chaired by Mr. Suon Rindy, Member of Parliament for Phnom Penh and Chairman. Board of Directors of the Federation of Cambodian Investors.
On that occasion, Mr. Ley Sopheap, President of the Federation of Investors of Cambodia, said that during the socio-economic recovery in the post-Kovid 19 context, starting from the favorable situation and challenges, and based on the strong will, the association has set the direction for work. In 2023, 11 points in continuous implementation.
1. Prepare to summarize the work results of the association in the field of expertise in the implementation of the three-year rolling strategic plan 2021-2023 of the association.
2. Revise the organizational structure of the association by sector.
3. Update members and expand members, including physical persons, legal entities, especially organizations, associations and the private sector, the systemic and informal economy.
4. Organize uniforms of the Federation of Cambodian Investors Associations and associations under the sectoral structure of each sector to strengthen the identity of the people, pay attention to strengthen the capacity
5. Open vocational training courses in areas such as food safety, infrastructure for pharmaceutical sellers, business, marketing, network, land and construction development, agricultural development and e-commerce environment, etc.
6. If the forum promotes and consults by sector by sector.
7. Provide scholarships for technical training courses, associate degrees, bachelor's and master's degrees.
8. Participate in the development of e-commerce.
9. Continue to cooperate with the Anti-Counterfeiting Committee, Cambodian Standards Institute of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation and relevant authorities in cracking down on counterfeit and illegal products that harm consumers and strengthen the protection of your interests. Use to get a real standard product.
10. Continue to cooperate with the Royal Government in educating members about the hygiene and prevention of communicable and non-communicable diseases to its members and citizens.
11. In response to the Industrial Revolution 4.0, strive to promote the development of digital systems by mobilizing experts to compile and study the development of digital systems.
Mr. Suon Rindy said that after active participation with the Royal Government and fulfilling the priority work of the Association of Cambodian Investors Federation, which achieved many goals so far until 2022, the association's leaders and sectoral committees continue. Strive to overcome all difficulties, complex actions until you get remarkable results.
