Plans to resume talks on US-Russia nuclear disarmament treaty postponed
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - Russia has decided to postpone talks on a nuclear weapons treaty scheduled for this week in Cairo, Egypt, the two sides said on Monday. Pause this or a new date. This was released by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, November 29, 2022.
Officials from the two countries are scheduled to meet in the Egyptian capital from November 29 to December 6 to discuss re-inspections under the Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty. New START, which has been suspended since March 2020 due to the Kovid 19 epidemic crisis.
A State Department spokesman said Russia had informed the United States that Moscow had unilaterally decided to postpone the meeting and had offered to reschedule the meeting. Responding to inquiries, the Russian Foreign Ministry confirmed that the talks had been postponed, as neither side had given a specific reason for the suspension.
