Community honey trade helps protect Cambodia's natural resources
(Phnom Penh): People who buy wild honey have a clear source from the community to protect natural resources, even if they buy only 1 liter or half a liter, also contribute to the protection of natural resources, forests and wildlife, because the community receives income from the collection Honey in the right way and during the walk to help protect the forest and wildlife.
At the Certificate Awarding Ceremony for 3 Wild Bee Collection Groups at Tonle Bassac Restaurant, Phnom Penh on November 29, 2022, Mr. Sim Bunthoeun, President of NTFP-EP / Cambodia, said that the collection work Community wild honey is paid and encouraged to continue to conserve natural resources in their community.
President Sim Bunthoeun continued that the honey that people buy from the community, even one liter and a half liters is an indirect contribution to encourage the community to continue to protect natural resources in their community.
Mr. Sip Cheang from Kratie Province Teuk Khmao Honey Collection Team told Fresh News that when entering the forest to get honey, they always patrol to protect the community forest, prevent deforestation, and release wildlife traps. If they find any crime, they report it to the community leader or local authority and the competent official. Each time they enter the forest, they spend 3-4 nights.
Mr. Sip Cheang continued that for the honey that is found and sold, it is necessary to pay a contribution of 1,000 Riels per liter to support the protection of natural resources in the community and the administration of the community.
NTFP-EP President Sim Bunthoeun added that the wild honey obtained by the community is made according to the honey quality system with the participation of PGS, which is a system to ensure the quality of sustainable honey extraction, filtration and packaging. Hygienic and participatory protection of natural resources. This vital system helps sustain the community and provides customers with confidence in the quality of wild honey.
Due to the proper implementation of the PGS quality system, three wild beekeepers were encouraged to receive certificates and bonuses from NTFP-EP, including Prasat Teuk Khmao, Prey Kratie, and Andong Dang. Preah Vihear province and Prey Krom wild honey collection group in Stung Treng province.
