Cambodia's first commercial court to resolve trade disputes to emerge in 2023
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Justice and related partners are busy preparing some procedures and procedures before proceeding to the official launch of the Commercial Court, which deals only with commercial disputes. As expected, the Ministry of Justice may launch a commercial court during 2023.
This was stated by Mr. Chiv Songhak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Justice in the seminar on "Establishment and operation of the Cambodian Commercial Court" this morning, November 29, 2022 in collaboration with the Asian Development Bank in Cambodia. Also in attendance were representatives from the Ministry of Commerce, the Chamber of Commerce, and student judges of the Royal Academy of Judicial Professions.
Mr. Chiv Songhak pointed out that the opening of the Commercial Court was originally scheduled for 2022, but the Ministry of Justice has faced some challenges that need to be studied further and need more time. These challenges include a lack of human resources, a lack of financial resources, a lack of appropriate locations and a lack of legal procedures.
"What is expected for the establishment and operation of this commercial court, the Ministry of Justice expects to emerge in 2023," said Chiv Songhak. Although a little late, we have created a court that is good, fair and acceptable to the public. "Because we have peace and economic growth, we must have a specialized court."
A senior official of the Ministry of Justice claimed that the launch of the Commercial Court is the first step in Phnom Penh, and that both the Court of Appeal and the Court of Appeal are together. He added that the next step could be planned in Sihanoukville, especially in areas with a lot of trade.
He added that the establishment of this specialized court is also to increase the trust of investors by improving the quality of services in handling cases according to each skill, which contributes to reducing congestion in court cases through the process. Faster.
Regarding the process leading to the establishment of the Commercial Court, Mr. Oknha Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, expressed the view that this is a good mechanism for traders doing business in Cambodia and also to increase confidence. Mr. Oknha Lim Heng continued that what is very interesting for business people is that we want a court that has quality, especially a fast process, transparency, justice and no corruption.
According to Mr. Oknha Lim Heng, in the past as well as now, when Cambodia did not have a commercial court, businessmen who had problems to complain about disputes in their business must file a complaint to the Capital-Provincial Court, while the Capital Court - The province has so many cases pending and it seems to be slow and cause some difficulties for traders, so the establishment of a commercial court is one of the most important.
"If we have a special commercial court, it will encourage more investment so that business people have confidence in our justice system," said Lim Heng. "In the past, we avoided trade disputes that led to criminal offenses, which is a concern for business people, but if we have a fair, transparent and non-corrupt court for traders, this is a very attractive investment opportunity." .
