CCHR calls for strengthening professional ethics in journalism and post-foreign radio broadcast in Khmer, entitled "King Norodom Sihamoni: From a former ballet dancer to a traitor?"
(Phnom Penh): The Union of Cambodian Journalists (UCJ) has seen a foreign radio unit in Khmer broadcast an article entitled "King Norodom Sihamoni: From a former ballet dancer to a traitorous king?" » Issued on November 28, 2022, in the form of an editorial in the form of an accusation that is baseless and completely reflects the essence of the radio that has seriously insulted the King, the highest revered deity of the Cambodian people.
The Union of Cambodian Journalists would like to point out that the King is a symbol of national unity, which is of the highest value to the nation and the people, and he does not interfere in politics, which should not be taken as an object of No insults and attacks on him. Your morals should not be degraded in the same way that the pagan Tamil Pol Pot did to the King, his family, and his nation.
The Union of Federation of Cambodian Journalists calls on all media to continue to adhere to the highest ethics of journalism, upholding the four fundamental principles of journalism, which are the sacred values of journalism: "Truth, Integrity, Balance and Integrity." "Verifiable."
