(Sihanoukville): Cambodia plans to organize an international delegation to attend the "Conference of the Most Beautiful Beaches in the World" to beaches, islands and some ecotourism communities on the coast of Cambodia to show off high-end tourist destinations. And will spread to the world at this great event.
This statement was made during the meeting to prepare for the conference of the most beautiful beach club in the world and the ninth round of the Sea Festival in Sihanoukville on November 28, 2022, chaired by Mr. Thong Khon Minister of Tourism Mr. You Sunlong, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province.
The Conference on the Most Beautiful Beaches in the World will be held from December 9-14, 2022 in conjunction with the Sea Festival in Sihanoukville, Sihanoukville, which is scheduled to receive a total of more than 120 international delegates from around the world. Mr.
In those preparatory meetings, Minister Thong Khon urged the technical working group to arrange visits to luxury tourist destinations, beaches, islands and ecotourism communities.
Mr. Chuk Chumnor, Director of Tourism Promotion Department of the Ministry of Tourism, mentioned the main destinations planned to visit the international delegation, including Koh Rong, Koh Thansur, Koh Song Saa, Koh Krabei, Koh Russey, Peam Krasop Ecotourism Community. Koh Kong province as well as the beaches in Sihanoukville.
Minister Thong Khon emphasized that "in the post-19th phase of tourism recovery, only the beaches, islands and ecotourism destinations play an important role in attracting and attracting more tourists."
Minister Thong Khon and Provincial Governor Kouch Chamroeun on the organization of the visit, time, means of food security, the content of the introduction, as well as the main content of the dissemination to the international delegates.
It should be informed that the event of the conference of the most beautiful beach club in the world and the Sea Festival will show the ability of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the past in terms of management, peacekeeping and development, achievements and local infrastructure. 60 Police from the Heritage Protection Police Department Announced New Positions and Rankings
(Siem Reap): The Department of Heritage Protection Police of the Ministry of Interior on the afternoon of November 28, 2022 officially announced the transfer of duties and ranks to a total of 60 leaders and heritage protection police forces under the chairmanship of General Ek Lim Phanphearak, Director of the Central Department of Public Order of the General Commission of the National Police, held at the Heritage Protection Police Unit in Angkor, Siem Reap Province.
The above leadership and heritage protection police force are working in 5 specialized offices and 4 units under the Department of Heritage Protection Police, including: Angkor Heritage Protection Police Unit (A1) Heritage Protection Police Unit Preah Vihear Temple Area (A2), Banteay Chhmar Heritage Protection Police Unit (A3) and Sambor Prei Kuk Heritage Protection Police Unit (A4).
Lt. Gen. Lim Phan Phearak reminded and urged the leaders and the police force to protect the heritage, which has been transferred to appoint the position and equip this rank to continue to perform their duties:
Assign, investigate and arrest the perpetrators involved in causing disasters, the national cultural and historical heritage to build a case and send the perpetrators and exhibits to court to be punished according to law. Cooperate with authorities at all levels and relevant authorities to prevent and suppress the perpetrators who destroy the national cultural and historical heritage.
Liaise with UNESCO, national and international organizations for guidance, dissemination of principles, and support for the protection of national cultural and historical heritage.
Cooperate with the tourist police in protecting security, safety and organizing order for national and international delegations and tourists who come to visit and visit historical sites.
Implement professional measures in accordance with the guidelines of the General Commission of the National Police and the Ministry of Interior.
Strictly and strictly implement the discipline of the National Police Force, build the achievements and honor of the Police, and protect the heritage of the Ministry of Interior.
Perform other duties assigned by the General Commission of the National Police and the Ministry of Interior.
