Tehran vows not to accept UN probe over erupting protests in Iran
(Tehran): The Iranian Foreign Ministry announced on Monday that Tehran will reject the recent UN-sponsored independent probe into the Iranian government's crackdown on protesters. Now there seems to be no sign of deterioration. This was released by the AFP news agency on Monday, November 28, 2022.
According to Iran's human rights news agency HRANA, 450 protesters have been killed in more than two months of unrest across the country, while 60 security forces have been killed and 18,173 protesters. Was arrested. Tehran has blamed foreign forces for the unrest.
