Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng agrees to study the possibility of determining the year of production of imported cars in Cambodia to reduce the risk to consumers
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee for Road Safety (NCRC), agreed with the proposal to request the National Committee for Road Safety to consider the possibility. Request the Royal Government to determine the year of production of cars to be imported to Cambodia.
On the morning of November 28, 2022, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng claimed that the study to determine the year of the car imported into Cambodia was to reduce the National Road Safety Decade Decade at the Ministry of Interior Used cars that pose a risk to consumers.
During the meeting, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng expressed his satisfaction with the plan of the National Committee for Road Safety because of its long-term and realistic vision to solve traffic problems in Cambodia. In addition, the prince also urged efforts to establish security cameras on the streets.
Please be informed that this morning's meeting was attended by Mr. Sun Chanthol, Senior Minister, Minister of Public Works and Transport and Permanent Vice President of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, and Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, Deputy Director General of the Ministry. All relevant institutions, ladies and gentlemen, leaders and officials under the General Secretariat of the National Committee for Road Safety.
In that, Mrs. Mon Manvi, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the NCDD. The National Road Safety Decade is a 10-year action plan from 2021 to 2030 and the second national plan from 2011 to 2021. This plan is a tool to contribute to the success of the Royal Government of Cambodia's Rectangular Strategy and in line with the National Road Safety Policy.
She said that the national plan is coordinated with the United Nations (UN) action plan based on the law on land traffic and in line with the national progress in all areas, especially areas related to road traffic activities such as population growth. Population growth, vehicle growth, road development, road accident conditions, good experience of law enforcement measures and challenges.
According to the report, a key part of the Second National Road Safety Decade aims to reduce road deaths and injuries by 50 percent by 2030, focusing on two main goals: Reduce the number of deaths and injuries according to the risk factors of road traffic accidents; and second, increase the efficiency of road traffic safety work based on the six pillars.
The six pillars were reported by Mrs. Men Manvi to Samdech Krala Hom and the meeting: First, to strengthen the management mechanism and lead the work of road traffic safety, second: to strengthen the implementation of laws and relevant legal documents, and third: to strengthen Road safety education, 4th: Strengthen the management of road safety engineering, 5th: Strengthen the efficiency of first aid and emergency services, and 6th: Strengthen the management of vehicle safety.
Kampong Cham Leaders Pay Tribute to Lieutenant Colonel Keo Mara, Commander of Chamkar Leu District Military Operations Area
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on the afternoon of November 28, 2022, led his colleagues to pay their condolences and pay their respects to the late Major General Keo Mara, Commander of Chamkar Leu District Military Operation Area, who passed away. The 59-year-old was found dead in his home in Andong Chros village, Ampil commune, Kampong Siem district, Kampong Cham province.
