Kep Province Launches Landscape Tower in Kep National Park
(Kep): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment said that with the view tower built by the Ministry of Environment for Kep will provide national and international tourists the opportunity to see the view of Kep from the top of the mountain. Filled with beautiful scenery is the sea and beaches of the archipelago and the sea of trees in Kep.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra made this remark on the occasion of the pressure to open a viewing tower in Kep National Park on the morning of November 28, 2022, with the participation of Mr. Som Piseth, Provincial Governor, relevant officials And local authorities.
The Secretary of State considered this tower to be another new potential of Kep National Park in attracting tourists to visit this beautiful and small province.
The 12-meter-high observation tower was built at the expense of the sale of carbon credits within the framework of the protection and conservation of natural resources and the promotion of eco-tourism. This observation tower is an additional means of entertainment for tourists visiting Kep National Park, in addition to the natural beauty, wildlife and mountain ring road that can walk and exercise for the general public.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra pointed out that Kep is the only province in Cambodia that has a national park in the center of the city and attracts more tourists to the food, especially the delicious seafood.
The Secretary of State called on national and international tourists to visit Kep National Park and see the scenery of Kep province from above the newly erected tower.
At the same time, he requested the Kep Provincial Department of Environment, which is in charge on behalf of the provincial administration, to take care of the protection and to implement safety measures to protect the safety of national and international tourists as best as possible.
