Minister Khieu Kanharith Leads a Team of Doctors to Free Consultation and Treatment in Prek Tanong Commune, Koh Sotin District, Kampong Cham Province
(Kampong Cham): Minister Khieu Kanharith, Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group on Koh Sotin District, and Ms. Tep Rainsy, Honorary President of the Volunteer Doctors, HE Khieu Kanharith, led a group of doctors on the morning of November 27, 2022. Distribute free glasses to people in Prek Tanong commune, Koh Sotin district, Kampong Cham province.
Mr. Sao Sambo, Advisor to the Ministry of Information and Chairman of the Volunteer Medical Team, HE Khieu Kanharith, stated that in the past, the medical team has provided free medical check-ups and treatment to the people without any political affiliation. .
He said that the humanitarian work on this occasion confirms the concern of Minister Khieu Kanharith and Mrs. on the well-being of the people in the village, commune, district, Koh Sotin, Kampong Cham province.
The activities of the volunteer doctors of HE Khieu Kanharith resumed their work on September 4, 2022 in Pong Ror commune and on October 16 in Lve commune, with 888 general medical examinations and dental check-ups. 105 people examined and measured the eyes of 205 people, a total of 1,280 people in both communes.
Minister Khieu Kanharith confirmed that the volunteer doctors who came here not to replace the district and commune referral doctors, but to come and help treat and provide medicine only if you have a serious illness can not travel. The provincial department has to contact the local authority so that the Koh Sotin district referral doctor, who has two ambulances, can transport him to the hospital, and the commune team will also provide some money for medical treatment.
Taking this opportunity, Minister Khieu Kanharith thanked Mr. Sao Sambo, together with the team of doctors and nursing students who always volunteered to provide medical treatment to the people of Koh Sotin district.
It should be reminded that the medical examination campaign for the people of Koh Sotin district started on April 9, 2022, with a team of 58 volunteer doctors, HE Khieu Kanharith, 13 of whom are regular dentists. 4 dentists, nurses and dental students. The other 40 are nurses and midwives at Koh Sotin District Hospital, 7 health centers and staff of Koh Sotin District Health Office.
The program of services on this occasion includes general consultation and treatment for the elderly and children, special dental check-ups, tooth extractions, eye examinations, eyeglasses and binoculars for the elderly.
On the morning of the same day, Minister Khieu Kanharith and Lok Chumteav Prof. Dr. Khieu Tep Rainsy Kanharith, Honorary President of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development, Ministry of Information, together with leaders and local team from Koh Sotin District, met and shared Give gifts to orphans under 13 years old in Prek Tanong commune, Kampong Cham province.
According to a report by Chea Lai Heng, Prek Tanong commune chief, the overall situation in the commune is good. Prek Tanong commune has a population of 3,029 families, equal to 10,706 people, 5,527 females. 13-year-old orphans, a total of 176 people, 83 females. Separately, 69 orphans, including 30 girls, received gifts from Minister Khieu Kanharith and Lok Chumteav.
Minister Khieu Kanharith addressed a message from the head of government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to local authorities, civil servants, people in Prek Tanong commune, as well as throughout Koh Sotin district, Kampong Cham province. The lives of grandchildren and great-grandchildren are all orphans now.
