Mr. Eang Sophalleth planted 1 million flowers to decorate his daughter's wedding day
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Personal Assistant to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, led the planting of about 1 million curtains to decorate his daughter's wedding day.
Mongkul Serey Soursdey, the beloved daughter of Mr. Eang Sophalleth, will take place on December 5, 2022. To decorate the house on the day of the wedding for his daughter and to show the big heart of love, Mr. Eang Sophalleth chose to plant about 1 million flowers by hand.
In the past, flowers that were used to decorate weddings or other events were mostly bought from abroad. Therefore, if they can be locally to meet these needs, also contribute to the employment of Cambodians.
