The wedding will take place over two days at the residence of Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, who is the bride's grandfather.
The wedding will be organized with many traditional Khmer programs, such as: hairdressing ceremony, flower cutting ceremony, flower procession to Rong Chey, Krong Pali ceremony, Bok Lok ceremony and dental work.
More than 100 Families of Veterans in Kampong Chhnang Vote for Land Donated by Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit
(Kampong Chhnang): On the morning of November 28, 2022, 100 families of Cambodian Veterans in Kampong Chhnang Province held a lottery to hand over land to veterans and their families, provided by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. And Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen in return for the merits they have sacrificed for the motherland.
The land donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to this veteran is located in Oka Kob village, Kraing Lvea commune, Samaki Meanchey district, Kampong Chhnang province. One family received 30x40 meters of residential land and 1 hectare of agricultural land. The drawing ceremony was presided over by General Kunt Sangkhab Dr. Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Sun Sovanrith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province and Honorary President of the Provincial Veterans Association, Mr. Commander of the Provincial Military Operations Area and President of the Provincial Veterans Association, Mr. Deputy Governor, Leaders Departments around the province and many other officials.
During the handing over ceremony, Senior Minister Kun Kim conveyed the greetings and greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Veterans Association and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross. .
In front of the veterans, Senior Minister Kun Kim highlighted that Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit always remember and always think about the well-being of all veterans. He said that in the circumstances of the difficulties caused by Kovid 19, both Samdech always reminded him, who is the staff and the leader of the association to go to the residence of the veterans and help solve the difficulties.
He said that today's lottery to give land to veterans is a clear testament to the high attention of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to veterans who are all meritorious and do. High sacrifice for the motherland.
The senior minister also asked the leaders of the Veterans Association in Kampong Chhnang province to speed up the clearing of land and build houses for veterans so that they can move in and grow crops on the land provided by the state.
