For the outcome of the meeting, please read the following statement: General Sao Sokha: The remains of 49 Cambodian fighters were exhumed from the Cambodian Martyrs' Monument in Dong Nai while the team was cleaning to bring them back. Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the National Gendarmerie and Chairman of the Technical Working Group, confirmed to Fresh News on November 28, 2022 that the remains of 49 Cambodian fighters Members of the Armed Forces of the Cambodian National Salvation Army, kept at the Cambodian Martyrs' Monument in Sous Ram Village, Long Yao Commune, Cammy District, Dong Nai Province (Don Nai), Vietnam, have been exhumed.
General Sao Sokha said that for today, the team has been cleaning the remains of the 49 Cambodian fighters, drying and wrapping the border to put in the ashes and transfer to hand over the cremation ceremony. According to the Buddhist tradition of Cambodia.
General Sao Sokha said: "As of yesterday, the team has completed the preparation. From today onwards, the cleaning is done, we dry it, we wrap the border and put it in the box. "Remains, transport and transfer - hand over and arrange our traditional cremation ceremony, pick up the items and put them in the coffin after the construction of the stupa in April, we will march the remains to be placed in the stupa."
"The 7th Military Zone, the authorities and the Vietnamese people in Dong Nai province have provided support and sharing in the situation where the country has just liberated its national unity and territory to the establishment of the Armed Forces of the Cambodian National Salvation Army at the request of the Prince," he said. Techo Hun Sen was the same fighter.
The general said that more than 44 years have passed since the 49 comrades who were sacrificed and died in the difficult circumstances were buried in Dong Nai province. Take care to provide land, issue a certificate from the Ministry of Culture, leaving the area as a historical site.
As the content of the song says, "Motherland, I will always miss you." Today, the 49 people will be assigned by the Royal Government of Cambodia to the technical team to cooperate with the Vietnamese friends to bring them back to their homeland to reunite with their families. Relatives and compatriots.
Although the remains of the 49 warriors were repatriated, in order to preserve the historical site and the values of Vietnam-Cambodia friendship, at the request of the Cambodian side, the Vietnamese friend will continue to prepare the inscription, preserving the area as a historical heritage as a proof of truth. History for tourism researchers and a reminder of the Cambodia-Vietnam friendship.
Director General Sao Sokha asked the Acharya's team to work hard to organize in accordance with national traditions and good cooperation with the Vietnamese side.
(Phnom Penh): The "ASEAN Village" exhibition, which was held for three days, closed with a large number of members of the public to visit and get new knowledge different from the traditional culture of ASEAN member countries.
The "ASEAN Village" exhibition is organized by the Cambodian Youth Parliament for 3 days, November 25-27, 2022. The exhibition aims to introduce Cambodians to the culture and traditions of the 10 ASEAN member countries, featuring food and folk games from each country, highlighting the culture and traditions of each of the 10 ASEAN member countries. Live and eat in these 10 ASEAN member countries.
Ms. Ly Sopheakdra, the organizer of the ASEAN Village Expo, said, "The ASEAN Village Expo is organized to celebrate Cambodia's hosting of the ASEAN Summit in 2022 and to share with the Cambodian people a greater understanding of the country's culture." "The 10 ASEAN countries, showing the way of life and eating of each country."
A representative of the Ministry of Culture said that the "ASEAN Village" exhibition is very important in highlighting the Khmer culture and culture of ASEAN members, so that the Cambodian people, students who participated in the exhibition program understand the culture and culture of ASEAN. Cambodia and other member countries.
He added that during the three days of the exhibition, Cambodia exhibited a variety of traditional artefacts, including: theatrical trousers, kites, Hanuman, statues of women, royal dancers, etc. Some of the artefacts are almost lost. And so this exhibition is a show again and again to the Cambodian people to understand and know more and more.
