Two groups of villagers in Choul Kiri district, Kampong Chhnang province, are in conflict over the decision to install two barricades in their locality, 304 people on one side oppose the construction of barricades and 300 people on the other side support the community
(Kampong Chhnang): More than 300 people living in Chulkiri district, Kampong Chhnang province, gave their thumbs up to the provincial authorities not to allow the installation of two fishing nets in Peam Chkork commune, Choul Kiri district, Kampong Chhnang province.
They claim that such practices are detrimental to their family fishing, as they find it difficult to travel as well as transport cattle, and allow traders to intercept fish. The canal above has never been developed in their locality.
On the evening of November 26, 2022, 10 people representing the 304 people living in Kbal Konlong village, Peam Chkork commune, Choul Kiri district met with the media and showed their thumbprints to the 304 protesters. The Anlong Metrey Sen Chey fishing community is not allowed to sell fishing lots (Prek Banak, formerly Lot 10) to traders throwing fishing nets in violation of the decision of the head of the Royal Government, which affects the family fishing of the people.
Ms. Steng Nak, a representative of the fishermen in Kbal Konlong village, said that on the morning of November 26, Mr. Ly La, Director of Kampong Chhnang Fisheries Administration, led his team to call five representatives to a meeting at the Peam Chkork Administrative Police Station to Discuss the above two canals.
As for Mr. Keo Met, the chief of Peam Chkork commune, he also confirmed that in the above case, he only knew that there were people who gave their thumbs up to prevent the construction of the two canals. As you know, there are similar people who have given their thumbs up to allow the community to continue building the canal. He did not know how many thumbs were stamped because they did not pass through him.
The other party, who gave a thumbs-up not to support the canal, said that allowing the canal would affect their access, especially for their cattle. Take to the shepherd as well. As for the law approved by the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, he also saw that the experts showed him the law, as far as he knows, it is still valid in 2022, only three more days.
The first letter of the Ministry dated December 28, 2020, then in 2021, the community asked for permission to build a fishing net, the Ministry allowed to catch three more fish in 2021 according to the letter dated October 22 2021. Based on the above two permits, fishing communities are allowed to serve their interests for community development, and fishing lots are not allowed to be sold to traders.
Regarding the above case, Mr. Ngin Hun, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampong Chhnang Province, told Fresh News this morning, November 28, 2022, The above two, he will not be allowed to be temporary pending resolution.
He stated that according to the order of the provincial governor, it is necessary to re-research the fingerprints of the people to be accurate and clear, both the thumbprints of the supporters for the fishing community and the thumbprints of the people who do not support to make Do. In particular, there is a need to conduct a thorough research on the impact on local fishermen, as more than 300 of them have given their thumbs up.
