(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Taxation of the Ministry of Economy and Finance has notified all business owners who owe tax debts to pay tax debts or to settle tax debts by the end of 2022 before the General Department of Taxation Implement strict measures to collect tax debts that cause the enterprise to lose money. This is according to the announcement of the General Department of Taxation, which was received by Fresh News on November 28, 2022.
The General Department of Taxation further states that in accordance with the Law on Taxation, the General Department of Taxation has the right to apply the following strict measures to collect tax debts from taxpayers:
* Suspend the enterprise value-added tax certificate (APT) without allowing the request for tax refund or use of tax credit
* Temporal detention of property tax transfer request
* Cooperate with the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia to stop export-import operations
* Cooperate with the competent authorities to suspend or suspend the enterprise temporarily
* Cooperate with the National Bank of Cambodia to withhold bank accounts of enterprises and / or related persons
* Cooperate with the Ministry of Commerce to withhold new company registration and / or share transfer
* Cooperate with the competent authorities to cancel the license or other licenses
* File a complaint to the court against the enterprise that owes tax and refuses to come to pay.
