Minister of Health: Cambodia is a model country for countries with low resources and just escaped the war can achieve health goals quickly
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Professor Mam Bunheng, said that Cambodia is a model country for countries with low resources and countries that have just escaped the war can achieve health goals quickly.
The Minister made the remarks while presiding over the opening ceremony of the 4th Regional Forum of the World Health Organization (WHO) Regional Cooperation Center for the Western Pacific, which was held in a hybrid format on 28 November. 2022 at Sokha Angkor Hotel, Siem Reap, with the participation of Dr. Corinne Capuano, Program Manager of the World Health Organization (WHO) in the Western Pacific.
The forum aims to share experiences from among the member countries of the World Health Organization in the Western Pacific, especially on primary health care and prevention of the spread of Kovid-19, with participants from Member of the World Health Organization for the Western Pacific, with a total of more than 200 Cooperation Centers.
"We are proud that Cambodia is a model country for low-income countries and countries that have just escaped the war can achieve their health goals quickly," he added. "Progress and innovation in health financing and services have contributed to the achievement of the Millennium Development Goals in health, making Cambodia one of the few countries in the world to achieve this." .
The World Health Organization (WHO) has been working with the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Ministry of Health to promote public health by supporting the development and implementation of strong health policies and providing technical advice on strengthening public health systems and health services. Quality, equity and sustainability.
With technical and financial assistance from development partners, the Royal Government of Cambodia is rapidly improving its human resource development infrastructure, continuing its efforts to improve the quality of health services, incorporating performance-based financing programs and strengthening efforts. Regulations and modernization of digital technology innovations.
Dr. Jakab, Deputy Director-General of the World Health Organization (WHO) at the Central Level and in-charge of the World Health Organization (WHO) in the Western Pacific, emphasized that the World Health Organization (WHO) vision for the future has been adopted by member states. The Western Pacific in 2019 and has been pushing for implementation.
Dr. Corinne Capuano, WHO Program Manager for the Western Pacific, thanked the Cambodian Ministry of Health for co-sponsoring the World Health Organization in the Western Pacific to host the 4th Regional Forum of the Organization for Cooperation. World Health in the Western Pacific.
The program manager recalled the priorities raised since the first forum, including: Security, health (immunity, antiviral drugs), non-communicable diseases and aging, climate change, health and the environment, ensuring that no one is abandoned. Disposal without access to health care services can only be achieved with the support and encouragement of implementation in line with the health plans and policies of each member state.
Comment: China-Cuba relations have become a model of solidarity and cooperation between socialist countries and sincere mutual assistance between developing countries.
It should be noted that the Commonwealth between China and Cuba is the first Commonwealth established by China with Latin America and the Caribbean, which indicates the direction for the development of bilateral relations in the new era. Cuba was the first country in the Western Hemisphere to establish diplomatic relations with the People's Republic of China.
Today, China is Cuba's first major trading partner and Cuba is China's second largest trading partner in the Caribbean. In 2021, the bilateral trade volume between China and Cuba increased by 7.2 percent, and in the first nine months of this year, the bilateral trade volume continued to increase.
In Latin America, there is a saying that "true friends can excite people on the other side of the world." Towards a future, China and Cuba will continue to be partners in the path of socialist development, a good partner for common development and a good ally for strategic cooperation for the well-being and interests of its people. Both sides for the better.
