Mr. Sinith said that if you want to take beautiful photos, you need to understand the light and the light triangle that are the basis of photography. If you are new to photography, you can avoid taking standard photos using automatic settings. However, if you want to produce quality images, you need to understand this basic concept before moving on to the next level.
He explained that light in photography is about light and the process of controlling how much light touches the digital sensor in the camera to create an image. The effect is to use an umbrella to control the light or darkness of the photo. There are three main components or components that work together and have an impact: depth, speed and ISO.
The light triangle is described as the basis of photography. Once you understand how it works, you will be able to take better photos using various settings on your camera. Understanding it may sound a bit complicated at first. This is the confirmation of the experts.
