Malaysian PM says government will use subsidies to tackle poor living conditions
KUALA LUMPUR: Malaysian Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim announced on Sunday that his government would review the use of its subsidies to provide better assistance to those most in need. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on Sunday, November 27, 2022.
Speaking at a press conference after chairing a meeting with the National Action Council on Living Costs, Anwar said previous approaches of comprehensive subsidies could not effectively address living costs, especially among the population. Low income and poor.
"I will give two weeks (to the relevant institutions) to assess all the impacts of the defined subsidies and discuss with the private sector as well as investors so that all stakeholders "Everyone understands that the purpose of the subsidy is to reduce the burden on the poor."
Anwar stressed that although he did not oppose the use of the subsidy, it must be implemented effectively to help those most in need.
Anwar was sworn in on November 24 but has not yet formed a cabinet, continuing discussions with other parties to form a coalition government.
