Honorary General Dr. Kun Kim Receives Veteran Leadership Medal from ASEAN Veterans Federation
(Phnom Penh): General Sangkhabandit Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, was awarded the Veterans Leadership Medal by the ASEAN Veterans Federation. The medal recognizes the role model and efforts of the General on Veterans Affairs during Cambodia's chairmanship of the ASEAN Veterans Federation in 2019.
The award ceremony was held at the 21st General Assembly of the ASEAN Veterans Federation to be held on November 23, 2022 in Bangkok, Thailand. Thai Prime Minister Prayuth Chan-o-cha presented the medal directly to General Kun Kim.
The General Assembly also awarded the Medal of Honor to General Meas Savon, Director General of the General Department of Military Service and Secretary-General of the ASEAN Veterans Federation, during Cambodia's rotating presidency in 2019.
Seeing the tireless efforts for the benefit of the veterans, the ASEAN Veterans Federation decided to award the medal to General Sangkhab Dr. Kun Kim.
It should be noted that last week, the Honorary General Dr. Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, led a delegation to attend the 21st General Assembly of the ASEAN Veterans Federation held in Bangkok, Thailand. Presided over by Mr. Prayuth Chan Ocha, Prime Minister of Thailand.
Please note that the ASEAN Veterans Federation was established in 1980. The federation was established to promote the luxury of life, the impact of age and the impact of war on the health and social well-being of war victims, and to raise awareness among the people in order to achieve advanced cooperation. Towards harmony, social justice and peace.
The federation also has a mission to promote a global understanding of the views, values, praises and interests of countries in the region and to promote the legitimacy of the interests of war veterans and war victims with legal recognition. Of the Veterans Association of Federal Member States.
