(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries came out to shed light on some of the criticisms that the Minister of Agriculture did not pay attention to the issue of falling rice prices, showing a number of strategies. The ministry is working to address the issue of rice prices.
Ms. Im Rachana, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, told Fresh News that in the future, the Ministry of Agriculture will support all parties to move the agricultural sector forward and reduce the problem of falling prices during the harvest season. Year through four strategies that the Ministry will implement, including:
1. Measures to produce good pure seeds that Samdech Techo Prime Minister has handed over to the Ministry to implement while the Ministry has been working closely with the private sector. 2: Measures to sell and distribute seeds at a reasonable price below the normal market price. 3. Measures: Buyers of seeds will receive a production contract.
Responding to criticism of the recent fall of rice, the Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture said that the recent decline in rice prices in some provinces, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. Noted that some social media users read the news only under the headline and accused the Ministry of Agriculture of blaming farmers who harvested rice at the same time, causing the price of rice to fall.
She said that in the press release of the Ministry dated November 15, 2022, the Ministry has made it clear that the decline in rice prices occurs every year from early November to mid-December because it is the harvest season. The fruits of the farmers. This is an indisputable justification, and it is not the farmer's fault at all when his rice is harvested and must be harvested on time.
However, this year, since November 15, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has addressed this issue to local people through the facilitation of rice trade between millers and people. Farmers at a reasonable price that is acceptable to all parties.
According to Ms. Rachana, as of Friday, November 25, 2022, rice mills in Battambang and Banteay Meanchey provinces have already collected more than 150,000 tons of rice from farmers, while the yield of rice is not yet on time. Harvest is about 20% in Battambang and more than 50% in Banteay Meanchey.
She added that in the past, the Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Dith Tina, had already explained about this problem that the solution to the agricultural sector is to look at the whole and from all angles, not just one part. No. The other solution must be a solution that involves all stakeholders.
