(Kampot): Dr. You Sokun, Deputy Governor, asked people to join the fight against diabetes, while the relevant departments are concerned about the increase in the number of people with diabetes.
Dr. You Sokun said that diabetes is caused by unhealthy diet and lack of exercise. The consequences of this disease are heart damage, eye damage, kidney damage, leg ulcers can even cause amputation. Diabetes treatment is lifelong, there is no cure. But it can be prevented by eating a healthy diet and exercising properly.
On that occasion, Dr. Nha Bunthorn, Director of Kampot Provincial Health Department, stated that diabetes has become a global health problem according to the report in 2017, the world has 425 million people with diabetes and experts estimate that By 2030, that number could reach 942 million.
Dr. Nha Bunthon said that the celebration of World Diabetes Day, which was held today, was held for the first time to raise awareness about the effects of diabetes on families. Education, prevention and management of diabetes and promoting a global movement together to fight diabetes, a major global health issue.
According to the director of the provincial health department, the number of diabetics is increasing alarmingly, and every eight seconds, one person dies of diabetes.
