General Sao Sokha receives the remains of 49 Cambodian fighters from Vietnam and brings them back to Cambodia
(Vietnam): General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the National Gendarmerie and Chairman of the Technical Working Group, led a delegation and a Cambodian technical team to receive the remains of Cambodian Armed Forces. A total of 49 people / billion from Vietnam brought back to Cambodia.
The remains of the Cambodian fighters are kept at the Cambodian Martyrs' Monument in Sous Ram Village, Long Yao Commune, Kammy District, Dong Nai Province (Don Nai), Vietnam. Dong Nai is located east of Ho Chi Minh City (Prey Nokor).
This ceremony is called "Opening Ceremony of the Tomb of Fighters of the Armed Forces of the Cambodian National Salvation Army" which took place on the morning of November 26, 2022.
At the ceremony, General Sao Sokha, on behalf of the Technical Working Group for the Repatriation of the Remains of Veterans of the Armed Forces of the Cambodian National Salvation Army, the Inter-Ministerial Commission of the Kingdom of Cambodia thanked the Party, Government, Army and people of Vietnam for their support. To the movement towards the overthrow of the genocidal regime and directly.
He said that the 7th Military Zone, the authorities and the Vietnamese people in Dong Nai province have provided support and sharing in the situation where the country has just liberated its national unity and territory to the establishment of the Armed Forces of the Cambodian National Salvation Army at the request of Samdech Techo. Hun Sen was the same fighter.
The general said that more than 44 years have passed since the 49 comrades who were sacrificed and died in the difficult circumstances were buried in Dong Nai province. Take care to provide land, issue a certificate from the Ministry of Culture, leaving the area as a historical site.
Although the remains of the 49 fighters were repatriated, in order to preserve the historical site and the values of Vietnam-Cambodia friendship, at the request of the Cambodian side, the Vietnamese friend will continue to prepare the inscription, preserving the area as a historical heritage as evidence of historical truth. For tourism researchers and as a reminder of the Cambodian-Vietnamese friendship.
