The war between Russia and Ukraine is a hot issue for the world. The issue prompted the United Nations to vote on one of the members of the United Nations, calling the war a Russian invasion of Ukraine. This election was supported by many countries, but also a small number of countries, including ASEAN member countries, chose not to support and stand in the middle (abstention).
Cambodia is a close friend of the former Soviet Union as well as Russia today. There are many conclusions that Cambodia's decision on this matter may support Russia or opt for abstention, as some ASEAN members do.
But it came as a surprise when they heard the decision of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia. Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, has declared his unwavering support for the United Nations, calling the war a Russian aggression against Ukraine.
