(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation, stated that the adjustment of monthly and annual tax returns online will make it easier for taxable enterprises.
He said that the enterprise can easily calculate the amount of bias to be paid or referenced as a loan and kept in the history of the application for correction, and taxpayers can monitor the status of the application and do not need to come to the General Department of Taxation to monitor. That no.
The remarks of the Director General were made during the meeting to review, discuss and provide input on the draft procedures and workflow of the revision of the monthly and annual tax returns, held on November 25, 2022.
The purpose of this meeting is to review, discuss and provide input on the draft of monthly and annual tax returns that will be implemented for the taxpayer management unit in carrying out the work of revising this declaration. Efficiently manageable and ensure sustainable tax revenue collection.
It should also be noted that the current monthly and annual tax correction work is done through a direct request to the tax administration and the new tax return form must be completed instead of the old one, which is wrong. The current practice makes the adjustment of tax returns unmanageable, which poses a risk of loss of tax revenue and deduction of value-added tax credit.
In addition, the implementation of the current tax correction process makes it difficult for taxpayers to prepare application documents and monitor the response from the tax administration. On the other hand, for tax officials, it is also difficult to manage and monitor the correction of enterprise declarations.
In particular, this new workflow allows taxpayers to apply for monthly and annual tax returns online without having to fill out an application and attach the relevant documents to the tax administration, simply filling in the data in the system and Monitor the status of requests in the online system of the General Department of Taxation.
The Minister of Delegation requested in-depth discussions to scrutinize and provide comprehensive input on the workflow procedures of the annual and annual tax returns in order to enhance the efficiency of the management of the declaration. The enterprise tax will also facilitate the taxpayer in fulfilling the enterprise's tax obligations.
On that occasion, Minister Kong Vibol stated that it is expected that the tax revenue for 2022 may reach around 115% or more compared to the financial law plan for 2022 management.
As the leader of the General Department of Taxation, he remains committed to working hard to ensure more efficiency in the implementation of tax revenue management for 2022 for the benefit of the national budget and to be Basis for implementation in 2023.
He said poor management of tax returns could lead to the risk of tax evasion, VAT credit deductions. Therefore, through the Cross Check mechanism, the General Department of Taxation has found and taken a series of tax measures for some enterprises that have deducted VAT credit incorrectly.
He said that the E-Tax Service provides support and help solve all the challenges in using the system and programs online of the General Department of Taxation. Battambang Provincial Governor Assigns Red Cross Donation to a Woman with Breast Cancer in Battambang City
