Iran tightens border security to prevent what it says is infiltration by Kurdish opposition
Baghdad: Iran's state media reported on Friday that Iran had sent more special forces to strengthen its northern border with Iraq and prevent what it said was an intrusion by opposition groups. Kurds. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Friday, November 25, 2022.
The deployment is aimed at preventing the influx and smuggling of weapons into the north by Kurdish opposition groups in exile in Iraq, which Tehran claims is staging anti-government protests across the country. So far, however, Iran has not provided any evidence to support the claim.
Iran has several military bases near the Iraqi border, where troops have been stationed for decades.
