(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sous Yara, Chairman of the Committee on Foreign Affairs, Cooperation, Propaganda and Information of the National Assembly, said that the relationship between the ASEAN Summit and the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (APA) is to fulfill what the Head of Government and The governments of each country cannot negotiate.
Mr. Sous Yara's remarks were made on November 24, 2022 as he answered questions from journalists at a press conference on the outcome of the 43rd ASEAN-AIPA Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) held by the Cambodian Parliament. Hosted from 20 to 25 November 2022 at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Sous Yara confirmed that the organization of the Inter-Parliamentary Assembly, also known as Apay, was to establish parliamentary diplomacy for peace. The establishment of diplomacy is gaining momentum in the face of geopolitical competition, so governments and governments in each region are trying to pursue their own national interests.
"Therefore, only parliamentary diplomacy is softer in the debate," he said. "Thus, parliamentary diplomacy has been strongly encouraged to be linked to the (ASEAN) Heads of State Summit to complement each other, which can not be discussed within government and government."
In addition, Mr. Sous Yara said that MPs are a direct messenger to the people, so decided to create a program is a face-to-face meeting between the Speaker of the regional parliament or the Speaker of the IPA with the head of state. Or the Head of Government of ASEAN. The meeting was an opportunity for the head of government to hear the concerns of the people of ASEAN, which has a population of more than 650 million.
At the same time, he said that the IPA meeting is also to strengthen parliamentary institutions to discuss and initiate for consultation.
