Cambodian Human Rights Committee files complaint at Correctional Center and Prison
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Keo Remy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, on November 24, 2022, led members and volunteer lawyers of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee to file a complaint at the Correctional Center. 1 (M1) Correctional Center 2 (M2) and Phnom Penh Capital Prison (PJ).
Mr. Keo Remy took the initiative to set up a complaint box for prisons and correctional centers in order to further strengthen cooperation between the Cambodian Human Rights Committee and prisons in promoting respect and protection of the rights and freedoms of detainees. .
Through this box, all detainees can secretly file their complaints regarding irregularities in prisons, as well as the exercise of their rights and freedoms, to the Cambodian Human Rights Committee for investigation and resolution.
The filing of the three complaint boxes above is a starting point and a pilot project before reaching the decision of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee to file complaints in all prisons throughout the capital-province.
The Cambodian Human Rights Committee would like to thank and commend the General Department of Prisons, as well as prisons and correctional centers throughout the capital-province, for their close cooperation in promoting, respecting and protecting the rights and freedoms of detainees, as well as Strengthen the efficiency of prison management.
