(Phnom Penh): As of November 25, 2022, it has been 17 years since Cambodia's Big Skin Shadow Theater was inscribed on the UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity list on November 25, 2005.
Big skin theater is an art that has a history when Brahmanism came to Cambodia. In the past, this type of art was only seen in two or three ceremonies a year and was rarely performed in public. These ceremonies include the Khmer New Year, the King's birthday and the coronation, or in the worship of famous figures.
