(Tbong Khmum): On the morning of November 24, 2022, Dr. Ouk Rabun, Minister of Rural Development, presided over the groundbreaking ceremony for the rehabilitation of a concrete road with a length of 11.50 km. Government provided through the Ministry of Rural Development.
The groundbreaking ceremony for this rural road was held at Kdol Leu Primary School, Kdol Leu Village, Trea Commune, Krouch Chhmar District, Tbong Khmum Province, with the participation of Mr. Seak Leng, Chairman of Tbong Khmum Provincial Council and Dr. Cheam Chansophorn, Provincial Governor. Engineering Corps, Ministry of National Defense, Departments around the province and civil servants, the Armed Forces and the people.
Mr. Kong Phoeun, Advisor to the Ministry and Director of the Department of Rural Roads of the Ministry of Rural Development, reported that the concrete road currently being rehabilitated is 11 km long and 500 m wide, 8 m wide, with a 1 m long sidewalk. The road connecting Tra commune to Krouch Chhmar commune at the Prek Ta Duong bridge in Krouch Chhmar district is located along the Mekong River.
Mr. Kong Phoeun said that in 2012, this road was built with a paved road with financing from the Asian Development Bank, only 5 meters wide, narrow condition, a lot of traffic, including overweight transport, making this road Damaged. The rehabilitation of this section of road is at the same time that the concrete section of the road from the base of the Kizuna Bridge to Trea commune has been built and is already large.
Dr. Ouk Rabun received a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, to the people in Krouch Chhmar district and asked for understanding from the people who have houses or travel on this road may be difficult. Or dust when the road is under construction, but when it is built, it will be easier for people to travel.
Dr. Minister emphasized that this is a project of the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, using the national budget to use the construction period of 25 months from the opening date of this site until December 2024 with a contract. Rehabilitated by the Department of Engineering, Ministry of National Defense, under the budget of the Ministry of Rural Development.
