According to traders who collect rice directly from farmers, the problem is that they collect rice directly from farmers at a low price by spending a lot on the road, paying for the cost of transporting trucks, loading workers, loading and unloading boats, and paying road authorities. And the boat dock, so it costs a lot. If farmers sell directly to Vietnamese ports, buy 1 kg of mixed rice for 1,100 riel, 1 kg of dry fragrant rice for 1,300 riel.
