Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara: National Tourism Vocational School is the first public school in tourism and a center of excellence using national and international standards.
On the occasion of the high-level representation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, at the groundbreaking ceremony for the National Tourism Vocational School in Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville this morning, November 24, 2022, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara affirmed that The school will also be a center for high-quality tourism and hospitality vocational training to meet the needs of post-Kovid-19 tourism professional training.
The groundbreaking ceremony for the National School of Tourism was held near Aeon Mall 2, Phnom Penh, and was attended by the French Ambassador to Cambodia, Dr. Jacques Perle, Dr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, and Ms. Sondrian Busse, Director of the French Agency. For Development (AFD) in Cambodia, including many national and international guests.
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara also expressed his belief that the two national schools will be tourism centers in accordance with national and international standards, which are necessary and assess the professional skills necessary for the development of tourism in Cambodia. Now and in the future, participate in implementing the policy of the Royal Government, which has identified human resources as the first priority for the development of the nation.
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara also requested the French Ambassador and the French Agency for Development (AFD) to cooperate and facilitate the French Tourism Vocational Training School in partnership with the National Tourism Vocational School of Cambodia. Continue to support the National School in training and strengthening the capacity of officials and teachers.
On that occasion, Mr. Jacques Perle also praised the success of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the fight against Kovid-19 and the effective implementation and implementation of roadmaps for the restoration and promotion of tourism in Cambodia and After the crisis of Kovid-19 on time.
He also expressed his pleasure and congratulations for the construction of the two National Tourism Vocational Schools, which will contribute to strengthening the quality and competitiveness of Cambodia's tourism sector.
The construction of the National School of Tourism Vocational School in Phnom Penh is planned to be 4 storeys high with a total construction area of 7,326 square meters on an area of 4,000 square meters, planned to cost 3,451,972.11 dollars, and in Sihanoukville to build 4 storeys. Similarly, there is a total construction area of 6,713 square meters on the location of the Provincial Department of Tourism, currently planned to cost 3,088,183.17 dollars.
The architecture of both school buildings is well designed in accordance with the standard and based on the design, including:
Location 1: National School of Tourism Vocational Training in Phnom Penh: 2 buildings, 2 floors in front, 4 floors in the back, including classroom, office, lecturer, computer room, meeting room, model room for hotel service, food service And beverages, travel and tourism services, libraries, restaurants and first aid rooms, storage rooms, parking, hedge systems and green spaces.
Location 2: National School of Tourism Vocational Training in Sihanoukville: 1 building, 1 floor, 4 floors in the front and 4 floors in the back, including the office of the Department of Tourism, classroom, office, lecturer, computer room, meeting room Implement models for hotel services, food and beverage services, travel and tourism services, including libraries, restaurants, first aid rooms, storage facilities, parking and hedge systems.
