(Tbong Khmum): Dr. Ouk Rabun, Minister of Rural Development, this morning, November 24, 2022, presided over the groundbreaking ceremony for the rehabilitation of a concrete road with a length of 11.50 km, a new goal of the Royal Government. Provided through the Ministry of Rural Development.
The groundbreaking ceremony for the rural road was held at Kdol Leu Primary School, Kdol Leu Village, Trea Commune, Krouch Chhmar District, Tbong Khmum Province. Engineering, Ministry of National Defense and civil servants, the Armed Forces and many citizens.
Mr. Kong Phoeun, Advisor to the Ministry of Rural Development and Director of the Department of Rural Roads of the Ministry of Rural Development, reported that the concrete road that is currently being rehabilitated is 11 kilometers long and 500 meters wide and 8 meters wide. 1 meter on each side of the road, which connects from Trea commune to Krouch Chhmar commune at the point of Prek Ta Duong bridge in Krouch Chhmar district, Tbong Khmum province, is located along the Mekong River.
Mr. Kong Phoeun said that in 2012, this road was built with a paved road under the financing of the Asian Development Bank, only 5 meters wide, narrow condition, a lot of traffic, including overweight transport, making the road This suffers damage. The rehabilitation of this section of road is at the same time that the concrete section of the road from the base of the Kizuna Bridge to Trea commune has been built and is already large.
Dr. Ouk Rabun sent a message of greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to the people in Krouch Chhmar district as well as people all over the country and asked for understanding from the people who have houses or do Travel on this road may be difficult or dusty when this road is under construction, but once built, it will be easier for people to travel.
The Minister said that this is a project of the Royal Government led by Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, using the national budget and will take 25 months to build from the opening date until December. 2024 by receiving a restoration contract by the Department of Engineering, Ministry of National Defense under the budget of the Ministry of Rural Development.
He added that the Ministry of Rural Development has set the goal of the rural road development policy that by 2030, all villages and communes will be connected and have adequate access roads, and at least 75% of all villages in the country will have access roads. Season.
