Minister of Economy gives 7 recommendations to develop Cambodia's rice sector to have more potential
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Economic and Financial Policy Committee, stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia continues to give high priority to promoting the development of Cambodia's rice sector. An important sector in ensuring national food security, supporting economic growth and creating jobs for the people.
Speaking at the Closing Ceremony of the 2022 Annual Meeting of the Rice Federation of Cambodia on November 23, 2022, he gave seven recommendations to the Rice Federation of Cambodia, which has just elected a new leader in the fourth mandate. To contribute to the development of Cambodia's rice sector to its full potential, which will contribute to supporting economic growth and improving the living standards of farmers.
These seven recommendations include:
First. Continue to strengthen the implementation of the five-year strategic plan (2023-2027) to promote Cambodian rice exports to international markets through cooperation with relevant ministries and institutions, and in particular increase capacity for rice market research and analysis. Local and global rice, as well as transparent market information sharing.
Second. Increase internal unity by adhering to the principles of transparency, fairness and mutual respect in order to increase bargaining power with buyers, strengthen competition with other exporting countries, and examine the possibility of formulating pricing strategies. One of the federal framework for selling rice to international markets.
Third. Continue to promote the Cambodian rice brand in the international market and seize the opportunities from the market and accelerate the diversification of export markets within the framework of the free trade agreement that Cambodia has: the framework of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement and Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP).
Fourth. Continue to cooperate with relevant ministries and institutions in promoting the production of pure seeds such as fragrant rice and rumduol rice and supply to farmers and farming communities at a reasonable price through the mechanism of public-private partnerships.
Fifth. Continue to strengthen the capacity of rice mills to optimize rice processing, financial management and business planning, as well as to consider the possibility of mergers or acquisitions in the supply chain between mills and exporters. Small to increase the excellence of the scale economy (Economic of Scale).
