Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia and President of the 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly, presided over the second plenary session of the 43rd IPA General Assembly with the participation of parliamentary delegations from ASEAN member countries. Eight countries include: Brunei Darussalam, Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos, the Philippines, Singapore, Thailand and Vietnam.
In this session, the minutes of the meeting were presented by the IPA Women's Parliamentary Committee, the IPA Young Parliamentary Committee, the IPA Political Committee, the IPA Economic Committee, the IPA Social Affairs Committee, and the IPA Organizing Committee. Second, the approval of the reports of these six expert committees was also approved.
The draft decisions of the six IPA Expert Committees were discussed at each committee meeting on 21 and 22 November 2022.
The meeting also held a ceremony to hand over the flag of the IPA Observatory to the Nepalese Parliament, the Azerbaijani Parliament and the United States Parliament, which has been the IPA Observatory since the 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA).
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Chairman of the Meeting, highlighted the importance and role of the Parliamentary Institutions of ASEAN Member States in contributing to the promotion of regional cooperation in order to maintain stability, security, economy, investment, tourism and socio-economic rehabilitation. After the Kovid crisis 19.
He added that the 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly is a demonstration of the close cooperation between regional parliaments and dialogue partners to respond more effectively to regional and global challenges.
Phnom Penh Capital Hall Announces Temporary Avoidance of Traffic Around 7 January Monument on November 26
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration on November 23, 2022 announced the temporary avoidance of all types of traffic on Norodom Blvd. November 26, 2022
In the announcement that Fresh News received from the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, it was stated that the reason for avoiding the traffic was because at the 7 Makara Palace, a meeting was held with CPP officials under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party.
In order for the above program to run smoothly, maintain security, safety, order and public order as well as avoid traffic congestion, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will avoid all kinds of traffic on Norodom Blvd. from 5:00 am on the 26th. November 2022 until the end of the program.
