Students, teachers, parents, parents and authorities ask the management to help build a school building because the old school building is rotten and afraid of causing harm to students.
(Kampong Chhnang): Students studying at Hun Sen Koh Russey Primary School on the back of Koh Kandal Tonle, Prolay Meas Commune, Kampong Leng District, with 215 students, on the evening of November 22, 2022, raised their hands in salute to the leadership and the Minister of Education Youth and Sports, please help build a new school building with 6 rooms for them to study safely.
Because one building has 5 rooms where the students are currently studying, the steel structure has decayed, which is a high risk during the study. Due to the strong winds, the school building shook and the students had to run out of the classroom for safety, fearing that the school building would collapse and endanger them.
Regarding this case, Mr. HUN Narin, Director of Hun Sen Koh Russey Primary School, said that this school building was a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, which was built during 1997 and is now 25 years old. . At present, there are 215 students, 87 females and 5 teachers, 3 females.
In the past, he also reported to the district education office and the provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports regarding the dilapidated school building. And recently, through the village chief and the parents of the students, the principal also made a proposal to build a new school building with 6 rooms to provide students with safe learning. But do not know if the proposal has reached the management or not.
Separately, Mr. Nget Sroy, Chief of Koh Russey Village, on the evening of November 21, 2022, also said that in the past, district and provincial working groups also visited this dilapidated school building. And asked the village chief to help find another place to prepare for the construction of a new building, because the location of the old building can not build a new building.
For this reason, he recently raised money from the parents of students to buy land from the people behind the old school building, which is 65 meters by 100 meters, 13 million riels. But so far, more than two years have not seen the leaders to help build a new school building.
