Five points of view of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the opening of the 9th ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting on the morning of November 23, 2022, including:
* First, to promote the ASEAN Center, which generally refers to the centralized role of ASEAN in setting the agenda and the ability to define and modify results.
* Second: Promote regional security in accordance with the law, environment and openness. The ASEAN Perspective on the Indo-Pacific is an important vehicle for achieving regional security innovations. We welcome all Indo-Pacific initiatives, as long as these initiatives promote peace and development, are not used against any country and are in line with the ASEAN Middle East and the ASEAN Indo-Pacific Vision.
* Third: Strengthen security and defense cooperation based on trust and people at the core. We have identified the security and well-being of the people as a fundamental part of our policy of security and international cooperation. Mutual trust is the foundation of international cooperation.
* Fourth: Improve security in all aspects. The Kovid-19 pandemic is a warning sign that we need to pay more attention to health security. Climate security is another important issue that we need to mobilize more efforts and resources. Civil-military cooperation on all aspects of security is becoming increasingly important.
* Fifth: Promoting cooperative security. With the increasing complexity and multifaceted nature of security and cross-border threats, we need to work more closely to address these challenges and obstacles.
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stressed that open, honest and cordial relations and dialogue are the way to the elimination of tensions, the prevention of future conflicts and the establishment of "secure security." Harmony ”based on mutual respect, understanding, trust and mutual benefit. We must work together to address our traditional and non-traditional security challenges.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen further asserted that at the time of his request, none of the ASEAN Member States had considered the recurrence of civil war in the region. But now Myanmar is moving towards civil war. According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, civil war has already erupted in some parts of Myanmar.
The Prime Minister emphasized that Cambodia, as a victim of more than three decades of civil war, has some experience to share with other countries in making peace, building peace, maintaining peace and building a post-war nation. .
Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, who used to earn a living to end the civil war and seek peace for the motherland of Cambodia, said that having learned about the peace process in Cambodia, especially under the win-win policy in the 1990s. , Samdech Techo is working on three points now around the end of the civil war.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated:
* First, we must keep the door open for political dialogue and negotiation.
* Second: We must ensure the safety, justice and well-being of all parties.
* Third: We need to be proactive while taking responsibility for the peace process. National ownership is crucial to peace talks.
