Phnom Penh: Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, on the afternoon of November 22, 2022, led a delegation of the Ministry of Commerce to meet with Mr. Sadhan Chandra Majumder, Minister of Food, Bangladesh and the delegation focused on important work. To strengthen bilateral relations, connectivity, cooperation and future strategic activities in importing rice from Cambodia into the Bangladesh market.
The Minister extended a warm welcome to the Minister of Food of Bangladesh and the delegation on the occasion of leading the delegation to pay an official visit to Cambodia in order to strengthen and expand bilateral cooperation, especially in promoting trade cooperation. Karma.
During the meeting, the Cambodian Minister of Commerce expressed optimism about the positive growth of bilateral trade in the first nine months of 2022, amounting to 22 million US dollars, an increase of 56%. Compared to the same period in 2021. He also highlighted the potential for bilateral cooperation to further boost bilateral trade.
In addition, the Cambodian Minister of Commerce requested the Bangladesh side to set out a number of work directions to enhance economic and trade cooperation in line with the indications of the two countries' leaders, including:
