Health officials say high stunting and overweight rates are a threat to the country's sustainable economic development.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Prak Sophoan Neary, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, on November 22, 2022, stated that high stunting and overweight rates are a threat and hinder the sustainability of economic development, human resources and continued growth. Of the country.
On this occasion, Ms. Prak Sophoan Neary stated that solving the problem of stunting and overweight is important and necessary for Cambodia to achieve its goal of sustainable development by 2030.
Ms. Prak Sophoan Neary said that the three major policies to promote the feeding of infants and young children are: start breastfeeding immediately during the first hours after delivery, exclusive breastfeeding. Only the first 6 months of life and continued breastfeeding until the child is 2 years old or older, along with supplementation from the age of 6 months, providing nutritious, safe, age-appropriate food. Of infants and children.
In addition, Mr. Hou Kreun, Director of Helen Keller, added that the training course for journalists on nutrition and infant and child nutrition reporting aims to increase knowledge and capacity among journalists and strengthen cooperation between the systems. Outreach to food security and nutrition workers and infants and children.
In addition, Mr. Hou Kreun stated that during this training, journalists and participants have formed the Nutrition Champion Journalists Group (CJCC) for the following purposes:
* Encourage journalists to increase the dissemination of information and strengthen media relations and coordination with institutions working in areas related to the food system, food security and nutrition, and infant and child rearing.
* Provide a forum for journalists and other stakeholders to discuss information gaps in the field of food systems, food security and nutrition and infant and child feeding in the Cambodian media.
