Nepal Parliament Speaker Asks Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin to Strengthen Cooperation between the Two Countries, Especially in Trade and Tourism
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, receives here this morning Mr. Ganes Prasad Timil Sina, President of the Union Parliament of Nepal, at the National Assembly.
During the meeting, Mr. Ganes Prasad Timil Sina requested Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin to help strengthen the cooperation between the two countries, especially in the fields of trade and tourism.
Mr. Ganes Prasad Timil Sina expressed his deep gratitude to the President of the National Assembly as well as the National Assembly of Cambodia for supporting the National Assembly of Nepal to become an observer parliament at the 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly. Becoming an observer parliament not only strengthens the cooperative relations between the Cambodian and Nepalese parliaments, but also gives the Nepalese parliament the opportunity to expand cooperation with other IPA members.
He said that Cambodia and Nepal signed a direct flight agreement in 2018 and hoped that the agreement would be implemented soon to open up opportunities for both countries to benefit from each other, especially in the field of tourism. Because Cambodia and Nepal have a majority of Buddhists.
On that occasion, the President of the National Assembly of Nepal also invited the President of the National Assembly to lead a delegation to visit Nepal.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin stated that Cambodia and Nepal have had diplomatic relations for a long time, since the early 1960s during the Sangkum Reastr Niyum regime, and also interrupted during the catastrophe of Cambodia. By war and genocide. Later, diplomatic relations were re-established in 1999, and this relationship has been continuously enhanced to this day.
He also congratulated Nepal on its remarkable progress and development, which has steadily improved its socio-economic status and continuously improved its living standards.
Samdech is proud to observe that over the years, the leaders of the two countries, Cambodia and Nepal, have shown a strong will to strengthen and expand the existing good relations and cooperation to be better and stronger through Exchange visits between leaders and the signing of a memorandum of understanding.
