Thailand, Saudi Arabia agree on energy and tourism cooperation (Video inside) (Bangkok): Thailand and Saudi Arabia have signed a number of agreements to boost cooperation in areas including energy and tourism as the two countries recover. Gradually restore full diplomatic relations. According to the Bangkok Post.
The two countries last weekend signed an agreement on energy cooperation, a memorandum of understanding to establish a Saudi-Thai Cooperation Council and another agreement to promote tourism.
The Bangkok Post quoted a Thai government spokesman as saying the two countries would also find ways to boost direct investment.
The energy agreement will cover hydrogen fuel, carbon sequestration and storage of clean and low-carbon energy technologies, the Ministry of Energy said on Saturday.
