The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to send three CMAC technical officers to complete mine action training missions in Ukraine (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen has recently decided to send Three CMAC technical officers to complete mine action training mission in Ukraine.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said this on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the closing ceremony of the 30th anniversary of the National Convention on Mine Action in Cambodia on Tuesday morning, November 22, 2022.
"Recently, the Royal Government has decided to send three technical officers from CMAC to carry out mine action training missions in Ukraine under the auspices of the Japan Assistance Project to assist Ukraine in demining." This is the confirmation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
He also reminded that with the experience of mine action in the past three decades since 2006, Cambodia has been trying to share its demining forces to contribute to the relief of many countries facing and affected by landmines. And unexploded ordnance such as Sudan, South Sudan, Chad, Mali, Central Africa, Cyprus, Lebanon, Syria and Yemen.
Over the past 16 years, 8,302 Cambodian Blue Hat soldiers, including 580 women, have completed their missions and become part of the United Nations family to contribute to world stability. This has made the national and international community marvel at Cambodia's mission with the highest honor in the world under the umbrella of the United Nations.
Samdech added that the contribution of Cambodia and the work of Cambodian heroes in 2022 was congratulated by the Deputy Secretary-General of the United Nations.
