Key Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Closing Ceremony of the 30th Anniversary of the National Convention on Mine Action in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): This morning, Tuesday, November 22, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the closing ceremony of the National Convention on the 30th Anniversary of Mine Action in Cambodia. The event took place at the Koh Pich Exhibition and Conference Hall.
The following are the main contents of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's opportunity to close the 30th National Convention on Mine Action in Cambodia:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that as a peace-loving country, in 1997, Cambodia signed and became a State Party to the Convention on the Prohibition of the Use, Storage, Production and Transfer of Anti-Personnel Mines, or Ottawa Convention in 2000
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that at the end of 2011, Cambodia hosted and chaired the 11th Meeting of the States Parties, which was recognized as one of the best and most successful meetings in the history of Cambodia. Meeting of the movement to ban the use of anti-personnel mines.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the number of victims of landmines and unexploded ordnance has dropped sharply from 4,320 in 1996 to less than 100 per year on average over the last 10 years. .
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalled that in a recent meeting with the Secretary-General of the United Nations, Samdech proposed to set a demining goal in the Millennium Development Goals.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the meeting between Samdech and the Secretary-General of the United Nations did not discuss Cambodia's internal issues.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech and the Secretary-General of the United Nations have been good partners since the 1980s.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed outrage at some who said that the UN Secretary-General had instructed Samdech on Cambodia's internal affairs.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia continues to build great achievements, such as demining, demining, and horizontal and vertical construction in high-risk mission areas. The work of Cambodian heroes in 2022 ranked second in the ASEAN community and 12th out of 120 countries donating troops.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that recently, it was decided to send 3 technical officers of CMAC to complete the mission to help train mine action skills of Ukraine under the support of the Japan Assistance Project to help Ukraine destroy landmines. .
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia has reached the declaration of five provinces, including Stung Treng, Kep, Prey Veng, Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that under the Samdech Techo project for mine action "provide safe land, create a smile", 7 more provinces will be declared mine-free provinces. Those provinces include Tbong Khmum, Kampong Cham, Kampong Chhnang, Takeo, Kampot, Svay Rieng, Kampong Speu and Kratie.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in meetings with countries attending the ASEAN Summit and related meetings in the past, Samdech requested assistance to clear mines in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that about $ 10 million has been spent on demining, with about $ 8 million left. Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call on philanthropists to support the budget for demining activities.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he will talk to the Minister of Economy to use the national budget for mine clearance in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the meeting with the US President did not mention Seng Theary. Talk only about the democratic space.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommends opening cooperation with Thailand to clear mines along the two countries' borders.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommends the continued cooperation and support of development partners, friendly countries, the private sector and philanthropists in terms of technical, budget and material in the demining mission in Cambodia to achieve the objectives of the National Strategic Plan for Mine Action 2018- 2025 and achieving the goal of "Cambodia without mines" by 2025.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen Instructs Ministries and Institutions with National Development Projects Related to Demining and Explosive Ordnance Disposal to Cooperate with the Mine Authority to Determine Appropriate and Effective Mine Clearance Methods to Ensure Mine and Explosive Ordnance Disposal Operations Comply with quality regulations, safety and cleaning standards.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen encouraged the Ministry of Health and relevant institutions to continue to pay attention to providing free health services and professional treatment to demining operators.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed the Mine Authority to revise the legal documents and harmonize the structure of mine action management in order to address the threat posed by mines and explosive remnants and to continue to implement the "Mine Action Village Mechanism" successfully.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen encourages national and international demining operators to increase cooperation with the Mine Authority to further strengthen the management of the mine action sector and to send Cambodian forces in the field of mine action abroad and to study. Practically speaking, the possibility of reducing the area threatened by landmines and explosive remnants is to ensure the safety, efficiency and effectiveness of this important work.
