This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Closes the 30th Anniversary of the National Convention on Mine Action in Cambodia
The Cambodian Authority for the Management of Mine Action and the Relief of People with Disabilities on November 21 opened the National Convention on the 30th Anniversary of Mine Action in Cambodia. The conference was held under the theme "Provide safe land, create a smile".
Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Cambodian Authority for Mine Action and Demining Assistance The sacrifice of the physical and mental strength of the mine action operator.
The conference is also an expression of gratitude for the generosity of donors and development partners who have continued to support Cambodia's efforts and expresses gratitude to all deminers.
The Senior Minister said that during the 30 years from 1992 to 2022, Cambodia in the joint mine action mission of the Royal Government of Cambodia, donors, development partners, national and international operators and all stakeholders have made significant contributions to solving the problem. Affected by landmines and explosive remnants of war in Cambodia.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch also said that since 1979, 65,004 people have been affected by landmines and explosive remnants of war, of which 19,818 have died. With joint efforts, the annual number of casualties has dropped from 4,320 in 1996, the year with the highest number of casualties to 44 in 2021.
According to Mr. Ly Thuch, as of October 2022, Cambodia has 2,001 square kilometers of suspected mines and remnants of war, of which 703 square kilometers are mines and remnants of war. 1,298 square kilometers, including cluster munitions.
It should be noted that Cambodia, as a affected country, the Royal Government has not been indifferent in clearing mines and unexploded ordnance, in which the Royal Government has directly contributed funds to mine action. For more than 30 years, the Royal Government has provided more than 200 million US dollars to participate in mine action in Cambodia, as well as support the institutional process and monitor the implementation of the National Strategic Plan.
Under the National Movement of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, people from all over the country have actively supported and contributed their personal donations to the campaign. As of July, the campaign has received more than $ 17 million.
However, Mr. Ly Thuch continued to call on all development partners to maintain and increase assistance to all national and international operators in Cambodia, through the Mine Authority, bilaterally or multilaterally, to implement the National Strategic Plan. Mine action 2018-2025.
Mr. Ly Thuch also expressed his deep gratitude to all donors, development partners and stakeholders who have been actively involved in providing technical, material and financial assistance to mine action over the past 30 years. In the cause of contributing to poverty reduction, promoting the development and economic growth of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
