Royal Government decides to release an additional $ 10 million for rice procurement in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia, through the State Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture, has announced an additional $ 10 million for rice procurement in Cambodia. This is according to the press release of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture on providing additional funding for rice procurement in Cambodia, obtained by Fresh News on November 21, 2022.
Please note that in recent days, the price of rice has fluctuated in some rice-producing provinces, especially Battambang and Banteay Meanchey, due to the large harvest season and the same harvest, making the amount of rice. Sales are large at the same time.
This makes it impossible for mills to collect all the rice, which leads to lower rice prices compared to the beginning of the season. Therefore, the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture calls on farmers in rice-harvested areas to set up harvesting programs with their local mills to avoid simultaneous harvesting, which could lead to over-harvesting. There is a reduction in the price of rice.
