(Phnom Penh): On Monday evening, November 21, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the official opening ceremony of the 3rd National Sports Competition and the 1st National Sports for the Disabled held at the National Stadium. Techo Legacy.
The National Sports Event was first organized by the Royal Government of Cambodia in 2016 with the aim of strengthening the capacity of athletes and athletes to participate in the 32nd SEA Games in 2023, which Cambodia is hosting, which Cambodia is looking forward to. Remember for about 64 years. The event is designed in the style of the SEA Games to strengthen the capacity of the Southeast Asian Games Organizing Committee.
National sports events are held every two years. But in 2020, the event was canceled due to the Kovid 19 pandemic.
The Minister of Education also emphasized that the event of the National Sports and Sports for the Disabled aims to improve the quality of the organization of national competitions and to reach the standard of regional competitions, as well as to prepare well and Win a lot of medals in the 32nd SEA Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games 2023.
The event also aims to provide an opportunity for all national sports federations to develop the capacity of trained technical officers by giving them the opportunity to participate in the organization and judging of the actual competition on the field.
The event is also a test of the opening and closing ceremonies in preparation for hosting the 32nd SEA Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games in 2023. South Korea seeks China-Russia cooperation on North Korea
SEOUL: South Korea on Monday called for active cooperation between China and Russia to prevent North Korea from continuing missile tests as the United Nations Security Council (UN Security Council) on Monday. Prepare for a meeting on the launch of the ICBM intercontinental ballistic missile last week. This was released by the AFP news agency on Monday, November 21, 2022.
The South Korean Foreign Ministry said in a statement that Kim Gunn, envoy for security and peace on the Korean Peninsula, had talks with the Chinese and Russian ambassadors in Seoul and asked the two ambassadors to help. Provide co-operation to hold North Korea accountable for its provocative actions.
According to the South Korean Foreign Ministry, Kim called for active cooperation from China and Russia, which are permanent members of the UN Security Council, and asked Beijing and Moscow to play a constructive role in preventing North Korea from engaging in hostilities. Other provocative actions will help push Pyongyang back to the negotiating table.
Last week, US President Joe Biden met directly with Chinese President Xi Jinping and said Beijing has an obligation to try to persuade North Korea to refrain from resumption of nuclear tests.
This year, Pyongyang has tested more missiles than ever before, while Washington and Seoul have warned in recent months that North Korea may resume its first nuclear test. Since 2017 at all times.
BEIJING, Nov. 19 (Xinhua) - The 29th Informal Meeting of APEC Leaders closed in Thailand on November 19. During the meeting, Chinese President Xi Jinping delivered a keynote speech, highlighting a number of key initiatives and practical measures around building a common destiny of the Asia-Pacific community and promoting regional economic integration. Obtain a response and active support from all parties.
From these keynote speeches, the outside world can see that China has always focused on this key word, "one-community common destiny of the Asia-Pacific", urging the parties to "uphold the right direction of cooperation." "Asia-Pacific" also commented on the issue of "how to deepen Asia-Pacific cooperation."
Cambodia-China Friendship Radio Cambodia launches National Convention on the 30th anniversary of mine action in Cambodia under the theme "Provide safe land, create a smile"
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Cambodian Authority for Mine Action and Mine Action Disability Management, on the afternoon of November 21, 2022, opened the 30th Anniversary of the National Convention on Mine Action in Cambodia under the theme "Provide "Safe land creates a smile."
He said that celebrating the 30th anniversary of mine action in Cambodia today is an opportunity for all of us:
* Recognize the historic achievements of mine action in Cambodia * Appreciate the skills and dedication of mine action operators * Express gratitude for the generosity of donors and development partners who continue to support Cambodia's efforts Appreciate your ingenuity in bringing new technologies to detect, clear and develop protective equipment and express gratitude to all deminers.
Operators found and destroyed millions of landmines and explosive remnants of war, including 1,151,232 anti-personnel mines, 26,112 anti-tank mines and 3,028 other unexploded ordnance. .659 tablets.
He added that at the same time, mine action still faces some challenges. As of October 2022, Cambodia has 2001 square kilometers of suspected land mines and explosive remnants of war, of which 703 square kilometers are mines and 1298 square kilometers of war remnants, including Cluster bombs. We also face a number of other issues, including:
In addition, the Royal Government has contributed tens of millions of dollars to other countries through the exemption of import duties on equipment, vehicles, and machinery, with taxes borne by the state.
In particular, the Mine Authority will continue to provide a compass to all demining operators and stakeholders through the promotion of safety measures, the preparation, revision and updating of policies, strategic plans, legal documents, demining plans, information management systems and standards of demining operations. In line with the evolution of mine action status.
At the same time, in order to increase international cooperation, on behalf of the Royal Government, I would like to call on all development partners to continue to maintain and increase assistance to all national and international operators in Cambodia through the Mine Action Authority through bilateral. Multilateral to implement the National Strategic Plan for Mine Action 2018-2025.
The National Assembly announces the results of the 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) Executive Committee Meeting
(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly of Cambodia issued a press release on the outcome of the 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) Executive Committee Meeting.
The Executive Committee meeting continued to discuss and approve:
1st: Agenda of the 43rd IPA General Assembly
Second: The agenda for the meeting of the 43rd IPA General Assembly Expert Committee, including: IPA Committee Meeting, IPA Young MPs Meeting, Political Committee Meeting, Economic Committee Meeting, Committee Meeting Social Affairs Committee Meeting of the Organizing Committee of the IPA Dialogue Partnership Committee with the Observer Assembly The hearing between the IPA Delegation and the ASEAN Secretary-General.
Third, it was decided that Indonesia would host the 44th IPA General Assembly in August 2023.
Fourth, welcome the agenda of the proposal to join the US House of Representatives, the Parliament of Nepal, the Parliament of Azerbaijan and the Parliament of Georgia, submitting the proposal for further discussion at the organizing committee meeting on November 22.
Sixth, to approve the inclusion of the emergency resolution proposed by Indonesia on promoting the implementation of the ASEAN Five-Point Code of Conduct for Resolution in Myanmar into the agenda of the Political Committee for further discussion on 22 November.
