The Ministry of Education issued a press release on the process of the Baccalaureate exam on December 05 (Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on November 21, 2022 issued a press release on the preparation of the high school diploma exam. (Bakdup) which will take place on December 05-06, 2022, in accordance with the four principles of the exam: the principles of law, justice, transparency and acceptable results.
In a press release received by Fresh News, it was confirmed that after the completion of the exam, the version will be conducted from December 8 to 14, the process of calculating and adding points by computer and verifying the score from 14 to 14 December 26
According to the Ministry of Education, the announcement of exam results in Phnom Penh and Kandal Province is set for December 27, while in other provinces across the country, December 28, 2022.
Please be informed that a total of 128,134 candidates registered for the exam, including 68,771 females. There are 25 candidates per room, except for the last room and the room with the candidates from the special education high school. There are 221 writing centers with 5,174 rooms. A total of 27,753 judges and judges participated in the examination process.
The Ministry has strengthened close cooperation with six ministries, including the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Health, the National Gendarmerie, the Anti-Corruption Unit, the Federation of Youth Unions of Cambodia and Electricite du Cambodge.
The Ministry will organize the closing of the list of candidates in the capital and provinces twice: the first time on November 28, 2022 so that the candidates can check and find the examination centers that match the alphabet of their names and the second time On December 4, 2022 to check and confirm again about the examination center, room number and table number.
Candidates must strictly adhere to the health and safety rules for the high school diploma examination. Exam session period: 05 December 2022 as set out in Executive Manual No. 34 IKSON dated 11 October 2022, especially to maintain Wear safety goggles and wear the correct mask regularly at the examination center.
The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports calls on all candidates to adhere to the rules of the exam, especially not to hide all kinds of electronic devices into the examination center or exam room. In case of violation of the rules and regulations, the candidate will be automatically disqualified.
