Contrary to some people's misconceptions about this exam, in the press conference on "The process of preparing for the high school diploma exam exam session: 05 December 2022" Minister Hang Chuon Naron stressed that the organization of this exam is encouraging. Students work hard to pursue higher education.
"The ministry does not aim to drop students, but to hold the exam to encourage students to study hard, there is no dropout," he said. Students who fail the exam and the ministry still gives them the opportunity to study for an associate's degree and can go on to higher education, while some countries do not do this. "So if we want to drop him, we will not let him go to higher education."
In addition, Mr. Hang Chuon Naron also rejected all those comments and considered this to be incorrect, because if the Ministry aims to drop it, it will not allow students to go bankrupt to continue their studies through Study for an associate's degree.
The Minister of Education also saw that the country that does not require students to take the exam before the end of the 12th grade is the quality of education is declining. However, he emphasized that some countries do not allow exams, but that country has higher quality and before entering higher education must take the same exam. He added that some countries also have vocational training systems to provide options for students after 12th grade.
He also instructed that all analyzes must be weighed in all aspects to avoid unreasonable remarks. He stressed that the parents of the students have invested a lot of money in their children until the end of the 12th grade, so after graduating, the students must have quality and easy to find jobs after graduation.
It should be informed that the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports will organize the Higher Secondary Diploma Examination (Bakdup) on December 05-06, 2022, in accordance with the four principles of the exam: the principles of law, justice, transparency and acceptable results.
