The 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly opens its first plenary session
The ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly, organized by the Cambodian Parliament, will be held from November 20 to 25 under the theme "Working Together for ASEAN Sustainability, Environment and Resilience".
The 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly, hosted by the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia, is IPA's first face-to-face meeting since the 19th global cholera outbreak since 2019. The 41st IPA General Assembly in 2020, hosted by the Vietnamese Parliament, and the 42nd IPA General Assembly in 2021, hosted by the Brunei Darussalam Parliament, were broadcast on video.
The 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly is an important event in which the Cambodian Parliament and its parliamentary delegations meet to share their experiences and visions within the AIPA family for the common good of nations around the world.
