Mr. HUN Many led a delegation of IPA Young MPs to pay a courtesy call on National Assembly President Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin
(Phnom Penh): As the Chairman of the IPA Young Members of Parliament (YPA), Mr. HUN Many led a delegation of the IPA Young MPs to pay a courtesy call on National Assembly President Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin. And chairing the 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly this morning, November 21, 2022.
To begin with, Mr. HUN Many expressed his deep gratitude to the President for taking the time to attend the 43rd IPA General Assembly this morning to receive a delegation of young IPA MPs. At the same time, he expressed his pleasure that the first meeting of the IPA Young Parliamentarians will be held this afternoon during the 43rd IPA General Assembly, which the Cambodian Parliament will host this year. This 2022.
In this meeting, on behalf of the delegation of young IPA MPs, Mr. Hun Many expressed optimism: "With the additional participation of young IPA MPs, which reflects the commitment of the Parliament of IPA member countries and ASEAN as a whole. "We will achieve the building of an ASEAN community full of opportunities and the active and positive contribution of young people for the common benefit of the people and countries of the ASEAN region."
Samdech Techo stated that with the commitment as the chair of ASEAN and the support of ASEAN members, Cambodia has proudly achieved the success of the 40th and 41st ASEAN Summits and related summits. Recently, ASEAN leaders and partners have adopted a number of key documents and initiatives aimed at promoting the sustainability, environment and resilience of ASEAN, including:
1: ASEAN Leaders 'Vision Statement on ASEAN Working Together: Addressing Common Challenges 2: ASEAN Leaders' Statement on the Post-ASEAN Connectivity Agenda 20253: ASEAN Statement on Building A sustainable future, environment and resilience through the promotion of women entrepreneurship in ASEAN 4: Statement on the digital transformation of the ASEAN education system, etc.
In relation to environmental sustainability and resilience, ASEAN has been prioritizing human resource development, education and vocational training reform in line with the evolution of the digital revolution and the promotion of the role of women and youth in Increasing Economic Productivity and Stimulating Economic Growth in the Post-Kovid-19 Crisis.
On climate change, Cambodia requested ASEAN to consider holding the "ASEAN Green Initiative" at the recent ASEAN Summit to orient the region's development towards a sustainable green future.
He added that in the political and security aspects, Cambodia has continued to prioritize strengthening ASEAN centrality and unity, as well as adhering to multilateralism, an important regional mechanism to contribute to easing geopolitical tensions and Confrontations between superpowers, especially through the continuation of dialogue with partners in various forums.
"Although regional security issues have not yet been fully resolved, I believe that the positive outcomes of the 40th and 41st ASEAN Summits and related summits have made a significant contribution to defining common ground," he added. "Some of the key issues provided for finding solutions to ensure security, stability and development."
