Through his message, he said that we have invested in quality education for young people. We have improved health care services for the elderly. We are fortunate to be in a thriving region that attracts foreign investment, trade and tourism in order to create wealth and achieve more prosperity for our people.
However, we must continue to protect and preserve the peace that has been achieved for a long-term stability. Peace can be shattered at any time by traditional challenges from near or far, as well as many non-traditional threats that can destabilize our society. The long-term effects of the Kovid 19 pandemic will continue to impact our region's economy for years to come.
