(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Cambodian Authority for Mine Action and Mine Action Disabled, attended the opening ceremony of the 30th Anniversary of Mine Action Exhibition. The senior minister confirmed that the annual number of landmine victims has been steadily declining, with 4,320 victims in 1996 and 44 in 2021.
On the occasion of the opening of the 30th Anniversary of Mine Action Exhibition. Senior Minister Ly Thuch stated that on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the Mine Authority, he attended the opening ceremony of the 30th Anniversary of Mine Action in Cambodia, which showcased the long journey of protection. Peace and a joint mission on one of the best humanitarian activities.
He added that the exhibition also showcases the achievements of 30 years of mine action, demining equipment, manual demining, as well as the use of mine detection systems and explosive remnants of war by animals. Dogs and mice).
In addition, there will be demonstrations of victim relief, education, risk reduction, use of information management technology and state-of-the-art equipment to deal with landmines and explosive remnants of war, as well as participation over the past 16 years. So far, 8,302 Cambodian Blue Hat soldiers, including 580 women, have completed missions in 9 countries, and those Blue Hat soldiers.
At the same time, it is an opportunity for all of us:
* Recognize the historic achievements of mine action in Cambodia * Appreciate the skills and dedication of mine action operators * Express gratitude for the generosity of donors and development partners who continue to support Cambodia's efforts * Appreciate your ingenuity in bringing new technologies to detect, clear and develop protective equipment, and * express gratitude to all deminers.
