National University of Battambang organizes consultative workshop on completion of horticultural education program
(Siem Reap): The National University of Battambang, in collaboration with the University of Pennsylvania, organized a consultative workshop on the completion of the Bachelor of Science in Horticulture program and the development of teaching and learning materials under the Higher Education Improvement Project. A study funded by the World Bank.
The main purpose of this workshop is to consult and gather key input from national and international experts to complete the improvement of horticultural education programs and the development of teaching and learning materials on this skill in order to gain recognition at the national level. And international.
Leaders and experts of the Faculty of Agriculture and Food Processing presented and explained the curriculum in detail, as well as the potential of physical materials such as school buildings, experimental farms, laboratories and human resources to support training and research. High quality and job opportunities.
This educational program will be officially launched at the National University of Battambang in the academic year 2022-2023.
It should be reminded that the partnership agreement between the National University of Battambang and the State University of Pennsylvania (PSU) is for 3 years from December 1, 2020 to June 30, 2023, which was signed on December 1, 2020 ago.
