US imposes new sanctions on China, United Arab Emirates over evasion of Iran (Video inside) (Washington) Washington has accused it of facilitating the sale of Iranian petrochemicals and petroleum products to buyers in East Asia. According to Reuters.
The latest US move against evading sanctions on Iran comes as Iran's efforts to revive its 2015 nuclear deal stalled and relations between the Islamic Republic and the rest of the world were strained. The sinking escalated as Iranians continued to protest against the government.
Washington has increasingly targeted Chinese companies over Iran's petrochemical exports as expectations of a resumption of the nuclear deal have been bleak.
"The United States will continue to impose sanctions on those actors who facilitate these sales," he said.
China to step up prudent monetary policy (Video inside) (Beijing): China will step up its prudent monetary policy and stabilize labor and commodity prices in an effort to strengthen and improve the outlook. Economy at a time of increasing risks from the global economy. According to Reuters.
BEIJING (Reuters) - Beijing will maintain adequate liquidity, advising commercial banks to extend lending, Reuters reported citing the third quarterly monetary policy report of the People's Bank of China (PBoC) released this week. Medium and long term and maintain reasonable growth in cash supply and the size of social financing.
"We will attach great importance to the potential for future inflation growth, especially with changes in supply," said the PBoC, committed to stabilizing commodity prices.
Reuters reports that the world's second-largest economy is facing ongoing tensions, including restrictions on preventing the spread of Kovid-19, which has prolonged the risk of a global recession and a recession. The real estate market is down.
Regarding the troubled real estate sector, the People's Bank of China reiterated that "housing is for living, not for profit" and said it would not use real estate as a short-term stimulus.
"(We] will accelerate the use of special loans for the completion of housing and increase lending as necessary, and guide commercial banks to provide sound financial support," the bank said. Each other.
Regarding the depreciation of the yuan against the US dollar, the central bank said that China will increase the flexibility of the yuan exchange rate and keep the currency stable at a reasonable level. According to Reuters.
