Interior Ministry Spokesman: Thirty people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on November 20
(Phnom Penh): At least 30 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on November 20, 2022 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on November 21.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 30 suspects, 14 were arrested in eight criminal cases and 16 were arrested in six drug offenses.
Data show that Japanese companies may abandon their deflationary mindset as they gradually raise prices for everything from fuel to food, while they are under pressure from rising inflation.
Japan's core consumer price index (CPI), which excludes fresh, volatile but inclusive energy prices, rose 3.6 percent in October from a year earlier, Reuters reported. The same as last year, compared with the 3.5 percent growth forecast by economists. In September, the price index rose 3 percent.
This is the highest growth rate since February 1982, and is also higher than the Bank of Japan (BOJ) inflation target of 2%. Rates above this target occur for seven consecutive months.
Despite rising price pressures, which are a growing concern for Japanese households, the Bank of Japan will not join the global trend of tightening monetary policy through raising interest rates.
