The approval of the three countries' parliaments took place at the AIPA Executive Committee meeting chaired by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia and President of the 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh. The 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA43) will be held from November 20 to 25, 2022.
On that occasion, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin announced the appointment of Mr. Chuan LEEKPAI, President of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Thailand as the Vice-Chairman, and the IPA Executive Committee meeting discussed and approved the action plan for the IT General Assembly. The 43rd Dad is as follows:
It should be noted that the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) is a parliamentary forum of ASEAN member countries that brings together the views of the House of Representatives on the promotion of parliamentary mechanisms under a broad vision and close cooperation to address common issues affecting Southeast Asia, as well as The world for security, stability and sustainable prosperity.
AIPA members include Brunei Darussalam, Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, Myanmar, the Philippines, Singapore, Thailand and Vietnam.
The girl whose mother ran to Samdech Techo to save her life is now healthier and has gone home
(Phnom Penh): Don Christine Rosana, a mother of three who ran to save the life of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, is now in better health after receiving intensive care from doctors. Christine Rosana is now out of the hospital at home and able to sit in a wheelchair without fainting.
After receiving an order from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Ms. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, sent the girl to Calmette Hospital for treatment. Thanks to the medical efforts of the girl, Christine Rosana's health has improved steadily. On October 26, the girl was rescued and sent to Kantha Bopha Hospital in Siem Reap for treatment.
After careful examination and treatment by a team of doctors at Kantha Bopha Hospital, which specializes in pediatrics, Christine Rosana's health has improved and she has been released from the hospital.
Despite being allowed to go home, the doctors continued to contact her parents to check on her condition and continue to treat Sana. This is according to the additional confirmation of Ms. Youk Sambath.
Sana was diagnosed with meningitis and encephalitis at the age of one and a half, causing complications and serious complications. Because of this condition, Don Christine Rosana has been living in a plant-like condition for many years. Parents have to live in despair, full of grief and sadness, pity their daughters.
Helping to save Christine Rosana's recovery brings unparalleled hope and excitement for a parent who is full of emotion and deep love for her.
Life-saving multiplication is a great multiplication, nothing can compare. With tears in her eyes, Nuon Niratey expressed her deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for giving her daughter a generous blessing and giving her a new breath of life. Ms. Nuon Niratey confirmed that Samdech Techo's great merits will make her and her family unforgettable.
