Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Parliament Signs Joint Statement on "Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Parliamentary Summit"
(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly of Cambodia issued a press release on the signing ceremony of the Joint Statement of the President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, the President of the National Assembly of the Lao People's Democratic Republic and the President of the National Assembly of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam (CLV) on the "Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Parliamentary Summit." In Phnom Penh on the evening of November 20, 2022.
The signing ceremony took place between Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, Dr. Say Samphoun Phumvihan, President of the National Assembly of the Lao People's Democratic Republic, and Mr. Doeung Dinh Fe, President of the National Assembly of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam.
On the occasion of the 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) from 20 to 25 November 2022 in Phnom Penh, the President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, the President of the National Assembly of Laos and the President of the National Assembly of Vietnam discussed cooperation between the National Assembly of Cambodia and Laos. Vietnam (CLV) to further strengthen the traditional friendship, good neighborliness and long-term cooperation in all fields of the three countries.
The President of the National Assembly of the CLV issued a joint statement on the establishment of the CLV Summit and set the formal approval of the procedure for the meeting.
In the statement, the three National Assembly presidents expressed their strong commitment to expanding and deepening parliamentary cooperation and partnership to maintain and safeguard close and mutually beneficial cooperation. Mutual cooperation between the National Assembly of the three countries by promoting political, cultural, economic and security cooperation for the socio-economic development of the three countries.
The purpose of this summit is to:
First, deepen the friendship, solidarity and cooperation in all fields among CLV countries. Second, promote the exchange and dissemination of information, experiences and good implementation of the functions and duties of the CLV National Assembly. And third: mobilize financial resources to implement programs and projects under the framework of the CLV Development Triangle (CLV-DTA). The first summit will be hosted by the National Assembly of Laos in 2023.
This parliamentary cooperation framework will create more tangible benefits based on mutual respect, understanding, trust and mutual benefit for peace and prosperity (M4P2) for the people of both countries. Three and more. Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan offers cremation to Chhay Vattanak, the husband of Nuom Sophorn in Banteay Meanchey province
