Interview with Chinese Ambassador on the visit of the Chinese Prime Minister to Cambodia and the relevant leaders of East Asia Cooperation
Q1: After the 20th Congress of the Communist Party of China (CPC) was convened, Chinese Premier Li Keqiang led a high-level delegation to attend the East Asia Cooperation Relevant Leaders' Meeting and paid an official visit. Come to Cambodia too. Can the Chinese Ambassador help clarify the significance of this visit?
Q2) The Chinese Prime Minister paid another official visit to Cambodia, the first gap in four years, which attracted widespread attention. Ambassador, please highlight the highlights and fruitful achievements of the Chinese Prime Minister's visit to Cambodia.
The two sides also issued a joint statement and signed 18 documents on bilateral cooperation. Highlights of this visit I would like to highlight three main points:
First, to continue to strengthen mutual trust in politics and to build a common destiny community is deeply rooted in the hearts of the people. The Cambodian side warmly congratulated the successful convening of the 20th Congress of the Communist Party of China, and highly commended China's great achievements, reaffirming its adherence to the one-China principle and supporting all China's efforts to achieve national unity
The Chinese side warmly congratulated the development in Cambodia on its remarkable achievements, reaffirmed its respect for Cambodia's independence, sovereignty and territorial integrity, and supported the Cambodian people to follow the path of appropriate development. In line with its national conditions, it strives to assist Cambodia in safeguarding stability, achieving development and improving the lives of its people.
The two sides stressed the need to accelerate the building of a common destiny between China and Cambodia in the new historical period, discuss and sign a new action plan to build a common destiny between China and Cambodia and send a positive message. That China and Cambodia continue to inherit the foundation and friendship unwaveringly.
China supports poverty reduction in Cambodia, will accelerate projects that benefit the people, such as promoting the third phase of the rural road project, the third phase of rural water supply project, the central hospital project in Sihanoukville and solving problems Dirty water and so on.
Question 3: The relevant East Asia Cooperation Summit 2022 was held for the first time in two years since the outbreak of Kovid. Can you highlight the important achievements that the Chinese side has participated in this time? Has the Chinese side achieved its goals?
At the 10 + 3 Leaders' Meeting, it was stated that safeguarding the process of regional economic integration, promoting the entry into force of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement and implementing the promotion of a stable regional industrial supply chain. Steady and smooth, support 10 + 3 emergency medicine supply reserve center, support the construction of 10 + 3 rice emergency reserve mechanism and support the improvement of risk response capacity.
The Chinese side would like to sincerely thank Cambodia for its correct stance and adherence to justice and truth on the South China Sea issue, not only for its active efforts to safeguard peace and stability in the South China Sea. It is also an important contribution to safeguarding the welfare, stability and development of China-ASEAN relations.
Q5: Next year, 2023, is the 65th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Cambodia. What are your expectations for the future development of China-Cambodia relations?
2023 is the beginning year for China to fully implement the spirit of the 20th Congress of the Chinese Communist Party, also the 70th anniversary of Cambodia's National Independence Day, China-Cambodia relations will welcome a new historical development opportunity.
