(Siem Reap): The ASEAN Intergovernmental Commission on Human Rights (ICHA) has issued a press release on the outcome of the ASEAN Human Rights Dialogue of the ASEAN Intergovernmental Commission on Human Rights. This is according to the press release received by Fresh News on November 20, 2022.
Following the successful organization of the ASEAN Human Rights Dialogue in 2013, 2014 and 2021, the ASEAN Intergovernmental Commission on Human Rights (ICHA) held another Dialogue on 19 November 2022 in Siem Reap in collaboration with the Ministry. Indonesian Foreign Affairs.
This year's ASEAN Human Rights Dialogue coincides with the celebration of the 10th anniversary of the ASEAN Human Rights Declaration (AHRD) and the Phnom Penh Declaration on the adoption of the ASEAN Human Rights Declaration adopted in 2012.
The Dialogue was attended by the 10 ASEAN Member States and a number of national human rights institutions in the ASEAN region, with the aim of providing a regional forum to exchange views among ASEAN member countries and share best practices and experiences in promoting and protecting Human rights in each member country.
Emphasizing the importance of cooperation and sincere dialogue, the Deputy Representative of Cambodia and the President of Icha, Mr. Chin Malin, emphasized, “Icha can build mutual trust and share experiences on the way forward in promoting and "Protect human rights in ASEAN."
The delegation also discussed the progress of ASEAN member states' ratification of international human rights conventions, cooperation with the United Nations, and strategies for implementing the Universal Periodic Review (UPR) recommendations.
Representative Icha reaffirmed his commitment to the promotion and protection of human rights and fundamental freedoms.
The ASEAN Human Rights Dialogue 2022 is co-chaired by Icha-Indonesia and Icha-Cambodia, organized in live and online format. Mr. Nop Rath Nimol: Due to the peace factor, we have the opportunity to meet and play sports like today
