Understand the business: Professional officials advise the conditions for farmers to get a profit of 8% to 12% from the use of preferential electricity
(Phnom Penh): The President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia has shown the methods or conditions for farmers in the agricultural sector, such as farmers, ranchers, producers and processors to use electricity to get a profit of at least 8 to 12% from the implementation. Preferential electricity policy to reduce costs and increase profits.
He noted that for medium voltage users can use an average of 50,000 kilowatts per month. An average of 20,000 kilowatts of low voltage users and those who buy from the public grid can use around 5,000 kilowatts per month.
According to the trial account, these four types of users benefit from 8% to 12% if they use 50% during the day and 50% at night. And for more users will be more profitable.
From 2021, the Ministry of Electricity will expand the electricity tariff to cover all customers who use it for all kinds of agriculture, from livestock farmers, agro-industry and horticulture. Used for activities that serve the agricultural sector, such as pumping, drying, fertilizer production, rice milling, food processing, beverage processing and animal feed factories.
At a forum on the use of electricity for agriculture held earlier this week, Minister of Mines and Energy Suy Sem said that after launching a preferential price policy for more than a year for the agricultural sector. At night, there is still no general practice, as consumers in the sector are not yet aware of this preference.
Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, expressed his belief that if farmers, ranchers and producers fully implement the Royal Government's preferential electricity policy for the agricultural sector, costs will be reduced and profits will be reduced. There will be more.
