The Cambodian Rice Federation issues a press release on the results of attending the 2022 World Rice Conference and receiving the "World's Best Rice" award.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Rice Federation has issued a press release on the results of attending the 2022 World Rice Conference and receiving the "World's Best Rice" award.
At the World Forum, Ms. Kim Srey Roth spoke about the progress of the rice sector, especially the progress on transportation, which is a key factor in the cost of exporting rice. The Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway is an improvement on rail transport that many rice exporters are beginning to use.
Rehabilitation of all ports, including Sihanoukville Port on the multi-purpose port, Phnom Penh Port and Kampot Port, which are under construction and a long-term base for the competitiveness of Cambodian rice exports to international markets.
The Vice President also called and invited all guests to visit and visit the business, including to invest in the rice sector in Cambodia.
As a result, Rumduol rice under the brand name "Jasmine Angkor" was selected as the best rice in the world, selected from more than 40 sample rice samples provided by eight countries. The World's Best Rice Scores and Awards by the ICI International Expert Committee of the United States of America based on the following criteria:
The Best Rice Award 2022 is the fifth time, the first time in 2012, the second time in 2013, the third time in 2014 and the fourth time in 2018. This great achievement is due to the efforts of the Cambodian people in cultivating the beautiful and fertile land of our Tonle Sap Lake.
It should also be noted that Phkar Romduol rice is a seasonal rainy rice variety that has been researched by rice scientists of the Cambodian Agricultural Research and Development Institute of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries since 1990 and was officially released in 1997, a type of rice with the main line of Khmer rice named "Somaly-1771".
