Phare Ponleu Selpak said that its circus performance in Battambang, which lasted a total of 24 hours, 10 minutes and 30 seconds, was the last effort to raise funds to survive the epidemic.
Phare Ponleu Selpak was established by Cambodian refugees and victims of the Khmer Rouge genocide to help lift Cambodian families out of poverty and preserve Cambodian culture.
The "Longest Circus Performance" World Record has been added to Cambodia's list of other world records, including the longest krama, the largest cake, the largest alphabet, and the largest religious building. Angkor Wat temple.
