Mr. Neth Pheaktra's appeal was made on November 19, 2022, after officials from the Kampot Provincial Department of Environment prevented a group of criminals from setting up a Facebook page and demarcating the land of Monivong Bokor National Park. In the Anlong Kmeang area, located in Techo Aphivath commune, Chhouk district, Kampot province, for sale on Facebook.
The Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment pointed out that the 1,800-hectare area that the crooks were mapping for sale was forested in Monivong Bokor National Park.
He said some areas had been illegally occupied by unscrupulous people for sale and that a case had already been filed in court for legal action.
Officials from the Kampot Provincial Department of Environment said that with the new evidence and witnesses, the Kampot Provincial Department of Environment will prepare an additional set of evidence to submit to the court to continue legal proceedings to deal with the perpetrators and their accomplices. Illegal encroachment on state forest land
In this regard, Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that officials of the Kampot Provincial Department of Environment have been cooperating with relevant parties to continue to submit additional evidence on the case and called on the people who cheated the crooks to buy land in the area. Get your money back because the site is the land of Bokor National Park that must be protected and conserved.
Mr. Pheaktra reminded that many people continue to cheat the crooks who sell land, land, no real land and no legal occupation. Some crooks have been pointing out forest land for sale and others forging documents to take state forest land, falsely claiming to be land that people have long enjoyed, in order to ask for clearance.
He also said that some crooks pursued a strategy of winning land, losing money in state land disputes, and that some crooks had hired people to protest and claim land with the authorities while enforcing the law.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment stressed that please do not believe the crooks who claim to buy state land and can make a solid title deed, this is pure fraud.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra added that while some people continue to cheat brokers in buying and selling illegal land, they will face two problems: first, losing their money and property, and second, facing the law with And perpetrators due to encroachment on state forest land and trading of state forest land is illegal.
