The NEC clarified the concerns of some political parties and civil society regarding the review and comment on the draft regulations and procedures for the 7th National Assembly election.
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has issued a statement on the concerns of a number of political parties and civil society organizations regarding the review and comment on the draft regulations and procedures for the election of representatives. National Assembly, 7th legislature, 2023.
According to the clarification received by Fresh News on November 18, 2022, the NEC would also like to inform the public and all stakeholders that the draft regulations and procedures for the National Assembly election. The 7th legislature of 2023 is organized on the following grounds:
First, the Law on the Election of the National Assembly and the Law on the Amendment of this Law
Second: Regulations and Procedures for the 6th National Assembly Election 2018
Third, the principles of modernization and some other principles that the NEC has decided to put into use in the 5th mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022.
Overall, the draft regulations and procedures for the 7th National Assembly Election 2023 almost retain the original content of the regulations and procedures for the 6th National Assembly Election 2018 by simply modifying some technical conditions. The NEC has successfully implemented and successfully elected the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election in 2022, including:
Chapter 1 revised and updated the content related to the election security work in accordance with the Inter-Institutional Plan No. 010, dated October 25, 2021 between the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of National Defense and the NEC.
Chapter 4 includes the use of computer systems to assist in the management of the registration of political parties and the list of candidates (this program was further developed in addition to the registration of candidates for the registration of political parties for the Commune / Sangkat Council elections). 2022).
Chapter 6 incorporates the use of computer systems to control the application and issuance of election identification documents (EAC) in accordance with Joint Instruction No. 034 S.N.N. dated 5 August 2021 Between the Ministry of Interior and the NEC.
Chapter 8: - Includes the use of computer systems to assist in the management, monitoring, verification and summary of election results, including preliminary results, provisional results and official election results (this program is further developed From the 2022 Commune / Sangkat Council Election Result Management Program).
Revise the technical conditions for completing and using the record of vote counting (T. 1102) to be consistent with the 2022 Commune / Sangkat Council Election in order to improve and ensure efficiency, effectiveness and transparency. Higher in controlling election results to another level.
The NEC welcomes the opinions of all stakeholders on the draft regulations and procedures for the 7th National Assembly Election 2023, and the NEC will review and consider all comments. It is based on the spirit of the law and the various legal documents in force. Another 256 vehicles were inspected and fined on November 18, 2022
