The Mine Authority will hold a two-day exhibition on the 30th anniversary of mine action in Cambodia at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center from November 21-22.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Authority for Mine Action and Mine Action Disability, in collaboration with 21 national and international mine action operators and civil society organizations, will hold a public exhibition on the 30th anniversary of mine action in Cambodia for a period of time. Two days from November 21-22, 2022 at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center, with 52 booths on display.
On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the Mine Authority, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Mine Authority, will preside over the official opening ceremony of the exhibition at 9:00 am on November 21, 2022. Congratulations from national and international guests as well as about 300 students.
The exhibition will be open to the public and will feature 30 years of mine action achievements, demining equipment, manual demining, and the use of mine detection systems and explosive remnants of war. Animals (dogs and mice).
In addition, there will be demonstrations of disaster relief, education, risk reduction, the use of information management technology and modern technical equipment to deal with landmines and explosive remnants of war. Day 29 of the 2022 Voter List and Voter Registration: 406,362 Newly Registered Citizens
