The ceremony on November 16, 2022 was attended by the Chief of Staff, the Deputy Chief of Staff, the Director of the Department, the Director of the Office, the Commander of the 14 Military Districts and many other members of the Armed Forces.
On that occasion, Brigadier General Phorn Rithysak also presented the National Defense White Paper to the Phnom Penh Military Police, highlighting some important points, including:
* Since the White Paper on National Defense 2022 is a long-term strategic policy of Cambodia in the field of national defense and security, which has been highly ratified by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, requires this document to be considered as a fish. Sectors and principles for strategic planning, military reform and capacity building of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
At the same time, the 2022 Defense Book is an important tool in international relations, especially Cambodia's goodwill in building trust and transparency with countries in the region.
* Rare peace in Cambodia requires absolute protection, at all costs, to take immediate action for all activities of the color revolution for the harmony and prosperity of the Cambodian nation. .
At the same time, we must raise the value and strive to build evidence of military history, which is the foundation of win-win politics, and bring complete peace and national unity to this day and into the future.
* Linking the front and rear battles is an indispensable factor in supporting the defense. The alliance between the army and public and private institutions will raise the value of the army's great sacrifice and increase the support, both spiritual and material, from the next battle.
From now on, the modernization of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces is a top priority in the military reform process. The capabilities of the Cambodian military will not be forced to remain in a state of disrepair or retreat.
The modernization will not only be limited to Ream naval bases, but also in areas such as air defense, heavy weapons, rescue, peacekeeping operations, counter-terrorism and transnational crime. This modernization does not pose a threat to any country, but rather protects itself and contributes to maintaining peace and stability in the region.
