Cambodian Red Cross summarizes the progress of youth work for 10 months in 2022 and raises the direction of higher education institutions in Phnom Penh (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Cambodian Red Cross Meeting to review the progress of youth development in 10 months 2022 and raise the work direction of the 24 higher education institutions in Phnom Penh.
The ceremony was held at the Cambodian Red Cross Headquarters on November 17, 2022 under the chairmanship of Mr. Pit Chamnan, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross and Permanent Vice Chairman of the Youth and Volunteer Support Working Group. The heart of the Cambodian Red Cross.
The meeting was also attended by the leaders of the General Secretariat and the 5 Departments of the Cambodian Red Cross, the Rector, the Vice Chancellor, the Advisors and the CRC Youth from the 24 higher education institutions in Phnom Penh, a total of 90 people.
Following the welcome and interest of Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross on the objectives of the meeting, the meeting heard a brief report on the progress of the CRC's youth development work for the first 10 months of 2022 and the direction. Continuation of work in 24 higher education institutions in Phnom Penh, reported by Ms. Som Sereyvath, Director of the Human Resources Department of the Cambodian Red Cross.
The report also reflects on the activities of the Cambodian Red Cross Youth Advisers of the 24 higher education institutions in Phnom Penh, which have been in line with the Cambodian Red Cross Strategy 2021-2030, despite the challenges. Some, but most higher education institutions still achieve better results.
The meeting included a panel discussion between youth advisors and youth from the 24 higher education institutions on gaps, challenges and suggestions to improve the report format as well as provide ideas for planning. 2023 to be better as well.
In addition, there are some suggestions from young people and youth advisors around the establishment of a telegram group to provide information to each other, as well as the distribution of all humanitarian activities on social media more widely. To participate in the promotion of humanitarian work in the society.
At the same time, these inputs will continue to strengthen the knowledge and capacity of the youth to be ready to host the 20th Meeting of the National Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies in Southeast Asia and the 2nd Southeast Asian Youth Forum. 2 in the coming 2023.
Closing Remarks: Mr. Pit Chamnan brought a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and Chairman of the Youth Action Support Team and CRC Volunteers to the members of the ceremony. All as well as confirm that Samdech Kittipritthbandit highly values the activities of the youth of the Cambodian Red Cross.
He also praised the youth, along with all the youth advisors, through the group discussions, reflecting that the young people are very brave and very understanding on expressing opinions in the right direction.
