(Battambang): The Battambang Provincial Administration and the Battambang Provincial Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation have launched a training course on the implementation of cash assistance programs for vulnerable families during inflationary pressures and floods.
The ceremony was held on November 17, 2022 in the presence of Mrs. Keo Dana, Deputy Governor of Battambang Province, Mr. Phuong Sithy, Director of the Provincial Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, Mr. Iv Kosal, Director of the Provincial Planning Department, Mr. and Mrs. 14 districts and 103 commune chiefs in Battambang province, a total of 234 people.
Ms. Keo Dana stated that in response to this difficult situation, the Royal Government of Cambodia, under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has launched a program to support vulnerable households during inflationary pressures. This is in order to improve the well-being of families living near the poor, with members of the elderly, the disabled, children, people living with HIV and so on.
The Deputy Governor said that these issues show consideration and attention, the long-term vision of the social protection system has really built and promoted an effective and financially sustainable social protection system to serve the goal. Politics to reduce and prevent poverty, vulnerability and inequality.
She added that in order for the training to run smoothly and be productive as well as potential within the framework of the operator, she would like to recommend eight points:
First, all participants must pay attention to listen to the presentation to get new knowledge and more good experiences to implement their work to get good results and high efficiency.
Second, the Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, especially program executives, continues to coordinate and strengthen all-round cooperation with relevant ministries, institutions and development partners, especially within the sub-national and local administrations, which are important operator actors. And what is needed to improve the performance of our program
Third, continue to use the knowledge, skills, experience and mechanisms available to increase the efficiency and effectiveness of program implementation.
Fourth, continue to strengthen the capacity of human resources through various means to increase work efficiency
Fifth, continue to use monitoring and evaluation mechanisms to ensure that the program will run smoothly in accordance with the plan and expected results
Sixth, request the Director of the Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation to continue to promote the implementation of the program more effectively.
Seventh, I would like to ask you, as the Board of Governors of the district, to strengthen the mechanism to monitor the implementation of the program, especially to encourage and encourage commune / sangkat program implementation officers.
Eighth: Request all media to continue to promote the widespread implementation of the cash subsidy program for flood-vulnerable families for the common benefit of the Cambodian people, especially families living near the poverty line. .
Ms. Keo Dana strongly expects and believes through this training and helps to increase specific knowledge and skills to make the implementation of the program transparent, accountable, honest and successful. Theft! In one night, a thief stole two motorcycles, shot and robbed a motorcycle, cut a power line in Daun Keo city and intercepted a necklace in Tram Kak district, causing people to be very afraid of safety (Video inside)
(Takeo): In just one night, two motorcycles left by the owner in a house with a closed fence were broken into by two thieves who broke through the fence and stole the door while the owner was away. But falling asleep.
This activity has caused people to be very afraid of security and safety issues, especially at night, as one day before this case, there was also an activity of burglars breaking into motorcycles in another house, unless the owner The house was shot by a thief, but luckily it was not.
One night, two thieves stole two motorcycles and disappeared from midnight on November 9, 2022 in Thnal Bek village, Rokar Krao commune, Daun Keo city, Takeo province, but until November 17. In 2022, the police have not yet cracked down on the thieves.
According to the report and the activities of the thieves in the video, it was revealed that on the night of the incident, he left the two motorcycles in the house with the fence closed and locked the door properly, then went to sleep forever. It was early in the morning when he realized that the motorcycle was missing. He then checked the security camera and saw two thieves on a motorcycle, who stopped near the house where the incident took place.
In connection with the theft, the owner of the house asked the Takeo provincial authorities to help find his fashion back and help find the group of thieves to be punished according to law.
In particular, at 3:00 AM on November 7, 2022 at a house in Trapeang Sala village, Rokar Krao commune, Daun Keo city, Takeo province. Two thieves broke into a house and broke into the door of a house, stole a motorbike, but when the owner shouted, the thieves fired two shots, but fortunately they did not.
At that time, the two thieves pulled out two unknown pistols and fired two shots, but did not hit the victim. At the same time, the thieves started the stolen motorcycle, did not catch fire, beat the motorcycle and ran to another motorcycle of unknown brand, escaped safely. After the incident, the police arrived at the scene and found 1 gun, 4 bullets, 2 shell casings and a pair of shoes.
Such insecurity has caused people to be very scared and requested the above-mentioned local authorities to take measures to eliminate theft and robbery so that they can have confidence and comfort. .
Separately, in Daun Keo city, there were also thieves stealing and cutting power lines, but the police have not been able to find them yet.
