(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has issued a press release confirming the progress of the solution to the problem of falling rice prices in Battambang and Banteay Meanchey provinces. This is according to a press release received by Fresh News this morning, November 17.
The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries confirmed that after Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, appointed two Undersecretaries of State, including Mr. Khy Kosal and Mr. Chhum Chhunly and professional officers of the General Department of Agriculture to solve the cost. After the rice, today the team arrived in Battambang province to meet with stakeholders and especially to meet with farmers.
