Fresh News staff successfully completes professional journalism course from renowned news university in Beijing, China
(Beijing): Ms. Seng Chanmulika, Vice President of Fresh News' English Working Group, has successfully completed the Communication and Progress Study of the People's Republic of China.
She received intensive training on a number of major topics, including poverty alleviation, Chinese media, technological progress, ecological evolution, China-China cooperation, and China's contribution. On social protection and the challenges the world is facing.
During her studies, she gained a broad understanding of China, including the effects of the giant economy, comprehensive cooperation between China and friendly countries, as well as the power of technology, which has had a profound effect on building a peaceful, harmonious community. Together and shared dreams in this era of globalization.
"While the world is actively changing, this study reflects the reality of China and China's rapid development, especially the path to poverty eradication, which is a great achievement in more than 100 years," said Mulika. "China's years have passed."
Ms. Molika also received training on public relations leadership and the use of modern technology to serve the media and in other relationships that are very important to individuals and institutions both now and in the future.
Please be informed that Ms. Molika has been working for Fresh News for almost 5 years, including part-time experience. She is a major figure in the English language industry. Ms. Molika's mission is to disseminate factual information with clear, accurate and fast sources to help fight counterfeit information in the digital age and spread Cambodia's positivity to the world.
