"Solar power generation must be an integral part of Cambodia's efforts to expand access to affordable energy and the transition to cleaner energy," Asakawa said. "ADB is pleased to support the establishment of the National Solar Park, an important project not only for Cambodia but for Southeast Asia as a whole."
The Solar National Park project demonstrates the potential for effective large-scale solar energy development in Cambodia through the mobilization of resources from both the public and private sectors. In this project, an internationally competitive bidding process is designed to bid for the private sector in two phases: 60 MW and 40 MW.
ADB provides support at all stages of the project. This support includes the provision of infrastructure, connectivity and transmission of roads and sewerage, operational assistance and assistance to the EDC on the components of private investment in the project, as well as the selection of private sector for support and structuring teams. And the mobilization of private sector financing for the construction of the 60-megawatt power plant.
