(Phnom Penh): A fire broke out in a house of a villager, causing a surprise to the people and local authorities called the fire truck to intervene to spray water. This incident happened at 6:30 AM on November 16, 2022 in Lor Kambor village, Sangkat Svay Pak, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh.
Colonel Prohm Yorn, director of the Fire Prevention and Rescue Police Office, told Fresh News that after receiving information from residents, they reported to 666 that a fire was burning in a house immediately. Also ordered fire trucks at all targets in Phnom Penh to help rescue.
Colonel Prohm Yorn said that the fire was difficult to intervene due to the location of the fire, due to the narrow road conditions, making it difficult for fire trucks to intervene to the target. In fact, the fire brigade had to pull a water pipe into the burning area to prevent the flames from spreading to the houses of people near the scene.
In the above operation, the police used 19 fire trucks of the Fire Prevention and Rescue Police Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police to use 19 water trucks, and 1 fire truck from Russey Keo District Fire Truck used water. One truck and two fire trucks at the Olympia shopping mall use water for two trucks.
The fire was caused by an electric shock that completely damaged six houses built of stone under the trees, but did not cause any injuries or loss of life.
