At the meeting, the two customs administrations briefed on the progress of each unit's performance, focusing on tax and tax revenue collection, trade facilitation, prevention and suppression of tax evasion and fraud, and customs cooperation. And so on.
The two sides praised the cooperation between the two countries' customs administrations in the past and the good progress in implementing the Memorandum of Understanding signed on October 4, 2019 in Hanoi, Vietnam. Bilateral talks between the two customs administrations in March 2018 in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam.
As the bilateral meeting at the level of Director General of Customs took place just one day after Cambodia successfully hosted the ASEAN Summit and related summits, Dr. Kun Nhim briefed the Vietnamese customs delegation on the results. The key points of those meetings were to focus on the outcome of the bilateral meeting between the two countries' top leaders and the Cambodia-Vietnam Investment and Trade Promotion Forum.
After vigorous discussions, the two countries' customs administrations agreed to further strengthen and expand cooperation on the following key points:
1: Continue to strengthen cooperation on the prevention of goods evading taxes and illegal cross-border transport through joint operations, strengthen the mechanism of liaison officers (Focal points) to exchange information at both the General Department level and at the gate Boundaries.
2. Accelerate the export and import trade to promote trade facilitation between the two countries. The Vietnamese side agreed to maximize the facilitation of the transit of goods through Vietnam to Cambodia, in accordance with the principles of legal trade flows and to prevent illegal immigration under the transit regime.
3. Continue to coordinate with relevant ministries and institutions to study the possibility of implementing a joint inspection mechanism at the Bavet International Border Crossing, Cambodia and Mok Bai, Vietnam.
4: Agreed to assign IT officers to work together to develop an information technology system for exchanging brief information online about the identity of transit goods and means of transportation of those goods.
5: Exchange study visits with customs officials to increase friendly cooperation and learn from each other's experiences.
7. Hold the next bilateral meeting in Vietnam in 2024.
The meeting was held in a happy, friendly, highly cooperative atmosphere and ended with fruitful results.
