The Ministry of Agriculture sent a team to inspect and find appropriate solutions on the spot for farmers in Battambang and Banteay Meanchey on rice prices.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has sent a number of target teams to Battambang and Banteay Meanchey provinces to inspect and find appropriate solutions for farmers during the rice harvest.
According to a press release obtained by Fresh News on the night of November 15, 2022, after the Ministry learned of the recent decline in rice prices in Battambang and Banteay Meanchey. Decided to send two Undersecretaries of State, Mr. Khy Kosal and Mr. Chhum Chhunly, as well as the working group of the General Department of Agriculture for actual inspection in both provinces.
Be aware that the whole of November until mid-December is the time to harvest the rainy season rice, especially the varieties of Phkar Romduol, which is why the mills are congested and affect the price of rice as last year. . This year, too, the harvest is still plentiful and the rush has been going on since the beginning of November. Although rice crops were affected by the floods.
In Battambang and Banteay Meanchey provinces, many rice mills are busy collecting, drying and grinding this kind of rumduol flower according to their respective capabilities and capabilities.
The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries calls on farmers who face specific problems to contact the Ministry's working group directly at 095 951 111 (for Battambang Province) and 012 838 937 (for Banteay Meanchey Province) for the working group. The ministry has full access to information and coordination with local mills.
At the same time, the Ministry calls on you on social media to stop posting false information that the Ministry ignores to help solve. Posting such information will cause concern to farmers who have not yet harvested the time to hurry to harvest substandard rice for sale, which will further lower the price of rice. Check out the gallery of important international events on November 15, 2022!
