(Pali) - US President Joe Biden and his Turkish counterpart Recep Tayyip Erdogan on Tuesday discussed the deadly bombings in Istanbul and international efforts to export grain to Ukraine. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, November 15, 2022.
The two leaders discussed on the sidelines of the G20 summit in Bali, Indonesia, addressing a number of issues that are at the heart of close but often tense relations between the two countries.
The White House said in a statement that Biden expressed "deep condolences" for the tragedy that killed six people in a bomb attack on a busy street in Istanbul on Sunday, stressing that the United States Always stand by your NATO ally.
During the meeting, the two leaders also discussed an international agreement to transport Ukrainian grain exports across the Black Sea to world markets.
