(Phnom Penh): Mr. Duch Son, Member of the National Election Committee (NEC), confirmed that the process of checking the voter list and voter registration 2022 for the past 26 days in communes across the country took place. Smooth in a calm environment, no violence and no threats.
Mr. Duch Son made this statement on the morning of November 15, 2022, during a meeting with election stakeholders to publicize the general situation surrounding the voter list and commune registration process. Sangkat Provisional Results of Voter List and Voter Registration and Challenges in the Voter List and Voter Registration Process.
Mr. Duch Son added that as of November 13, 2022, the NEC had issued ID cards to a total of 41 national journalists, four women from six units, as of November 14, 2022. The total number of political party agents officially recognized by the commune council was 7,479, 1,586 of whom were women from six political parties.
At the same time, Mr. Duch Son continued that during this period, the NEC received one complaint against the Chief of the First Deputy Sangkat of Sangkat Or Russey III, Khan 7 Makara, Phnom Penh. This complaint was rejected by the NEC. Meanwhile, the NEC has officially recognized a total of 3,155 national observers from associations and non-governmental organizations, 1,054 of whom are women.
NEC members also released preliminary results of the 2022 voter list, which included 9,519,603 people, 5,066,641 women, or 87.52 percent of the eligible population. Total voting for 26 days of voter registration and voter registration process.
In addition, Mr. Duchson emphasized that for migrants, they usually have to register in the new commune, they have to go to the voter registration group in the new commune and show their documents for the voter registration team to work. Transfer his name from the old commune to the new commune. When posting the first voter list, he had to go and check his name again to make sure he was registered to vote in the new commune.
The NEC has specific measures for political party agents and observers to monitor voter registration at all polling stations across the country. The NEC has always paid close attention to this task to facilitate the general process, however, the observation work is not to obstruct the process of voter registration and voter registration.
He also called on all stakeholders, including political parties, associations, non-governmental organizations, media units and authorities at all levels, to help disseminate and encourage people to go and check the voter list and register to vote. Timely.
