Modern plastic banknotes are currently being developed in Australia by the Federal Reserve, the CSIRO Scientific Research Agency and the University of Melbourne, Australia. The banknotes were first printed in Australia in 1988. By 1996, the Australian dollar (A $) had been completely converted from plain banknotes to plastic banknotes.
Romania became the first country in Europe to print plastic paper in 1999 and became the third country in the world to completely convert plain paper into plastic paper in 2003. After Australia and New Zealand.
