(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Cashew Association and a number of civil society organizations have been gradually seeking a market for cashew farmers as two Vietnamese companies pledge to buy more than 70,000 tonnes of cashew nuts as the cashew harvest season approaches. 2023.
According to the association's president, Cambodia's cashew nuts exported to Vietnam are raw because so far the price of Cambodia's processed cashews is more expensive than Vietnam's, making it difficult for Cambodia to compete in the international market.
In 2023, the Cambodian Cashew Association estimates that the production of cashew will increase between 800,000 tons to 1 million tons if the weather is favorable, while in 2022 due to weather conditions, cashew yield is only about 660,000 tons.
The cashew harvest starts from February to May.
