In the past, on the expressway, there was a lot of congestion at the entrances and exits when there was a lot of traffic on this road. Especially on national holidays or weekends due to payment. The program takes about two months to set up.
To solve this problem, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, in collaboration with the Ministry of Expressways, in collaboration with other financial institutions, decided to find a way to solve the problem through technology. Finally, a program to insert money into license plates and automatically deduct money when crossing the freeway was created. This program is applicable to about 10 financial institutions.
Mr. Heang Sothearyut, Director General of the Ministry of Public Works, Technology and Public Relations of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, said: "Fast speeds on weekends or on public holidays, this program will make it easier for people without having to wait a long time to pay."
Heang Sotheayut added that the program requires car owners to deposit money in advance. Upon entering the expressway and at the exit, the system will pay the cash / top up the balance through the ANPR automatic camera and pay through the partner banking system of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport.
He added that the trial process began on November 14, with only one right-of-way payment route in Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville. In particular, from November 18 onwards, all payment channels will be launched.
In addition, Mr. Heang Sotheayut also called on all citizens to participate in the program of deposit into the license plate to increase convenience, reduce congestion, reduce the use of cash and avoid the risk of infection. Also.
