(Phnom Penh): It is not only ASEAN leaders and leaders of ASEAN dialogue partners who have been given hospitality and services with care, even the media. In the ASEAN Summit and related summits in Cambodia last week.
The summit brought together a total of nearly 2,000 national and international journalists covering major events in Cambodia. This number is confirmed to be a large number compared to the ASEAN Summit and related summits in the past.
Participating journalists receive the highest attention from the Ministry of Information. The information center at Sokha Hotel is equipped with audio equipment to provide pictures from the meeting, making it easy to access information from the meeting room.
Information in this digital context requires the Internet. The information center provides high-speed internet access, making it easy for reporters to send pictures and videos for publicity.
Not only is the facility convenient for retrieving and providing information, but eating is also very important.
At the information center, lunch is served with a variety of dishes, accompanied by desserts and fruit. In addition to lunch, there are also two snacks and coffee, in the morning and in the afternoon.
The center is equipped with air conditioning to the bathroom. Therefore, no matter how busy the news is, their hearts are still cold and cannot be heated.
Overall, during the reporting period, there were no internet complaints or malnutrition. Journalists do not seem to have a hard time getting and providing information.
The Ministry of Information has prepared many officials waiting to coordinate and meet the needs of journalists quickly. In addition, Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, was present at the Information Center to manage the situation and respond to the needs of journalists.
Journalists who have been covering Cambodia now have expressed their satisfaction with this excellent arrangement.
