(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, in cooperation with the Ministry of Mines and Energy, the Electricity Authority of Cambodia and Electricite du Cambodge (EDC), on the morning of November 14, 2022, organized an important dialogue forum on the use of electricity for agriculture. How to help farmers, growers, producers and processors in the agricultural sector to fully implement the Royal Government's preferential electricity policy to reduce production costs.
The Minister expressed confidence that if farmers, ranchers and producers fully implement the Royal Government's preferential electricity policy for the agricultural sector, costs will be reduced and profits will be greater. .
Mr. Suy Sem, Minister of Mines and Energy, said that since 2021, the Royal Government has set a policy to implement electricity tariffs for agriculture at a lower cost than other types of electricity and special privileges. The electricity consumption of all types of electricity consumers in the agricultural sector at night from 9 pm to 7 am is allowed to pay only 480 riels per kilowatt hour.
"I think the agricultural sector is the bravest because the agricultural sector is difficult to make a profit very soon, it takes time and there are many challenges, so the Royal Government has a preferential electricity policy. "Industry and agriculture, and agriculture has a special advantage in addition to industry."
Mr. Keo Rattanak, Deputy Prime Minister and Director General of Electricite du Cambodge (EDC), urged farmers, ranchers and producers to fully implement the Royal Government's policy on electricity tariffs for the agricultural sector by applying. Go to the service provider near your location. When fully implemented, the Royal Government may examine the possibility of further concessions.
"We want this policy to be taken one step at a time, and we will study together to find out what else we can do to help each other, because our goal is the same," he said. "Agriculture, we walk."
Mr. Keo Rattanak stated that the preferential price of 480 Riels per kilowatt hour for the agricultural sector from 9 pm to 7 am is the price subsidized by the Royal Government, which means that the Royal Government sells electricity at a loss that the cost of electricity in At present, the price is about 1,000 riel per kilowatt hour.
Mr. Yim Viseth, President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia, encouraged farmers, producers and ranchers to use electricity at night as much as possible to reduce costs through this preferential electricity policy.
