According to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the joint statement between the two countries has the following 15 points:
1: In response to the visit of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, His Majesty Sultan Haji Hassanal Bolkiah Muy Isadin Vadula of Brunei paid a state visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia. On November 14, 2022. The visit is an important event as the two countries mark the 30th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic ties this year.
2. During this state visit, the Sultan was given a royal patronage. He laid a wreath and paid his respects at the Independence Monument and at the shrine of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the King Father of Cambodia, the King of Cambodia, the former King of Cambodia.
3. The Sultan had a royal hearing with His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, who hosted a state dinner at noon in honor of the Sultan.
4. The Sultan also had a bilateral meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia. The bilateral meeting was held in a warm and cordial atmosphere, during which the two sides discussed fruitful work on various bilateral cooperation and exchanged views on regional and international issues of common concern. Common interests.
The two sides stressed the importance of promoting regular communication between senior officials from relevant ministries and institutions of the two countries to boost cooperation in various fields.
7. The two leaders agreed to continue to strengthen cooperation in the field of defense and security through the exchange of information on terrorism and transnational crime, as well as the exchange of senior defense officials, capacity building projects and the possibility of signing agreements. On the Memorandum of Understanding on Defense Cooperation.
8. The two leaders pledged to promote bilateral trade and investment exchanges by encouraging the private sector to seek more business opportunities in potential sectors and ensure the effective implementation of their duties. Agree on the avoidance of double taxation and the prevention of tax evasion related to income tax.
9. Both sides agreed to exchange experiences and good practices on industrial modernization in line with the Industrial Revolution 4.0. The Cambodian side has encouraged direct investment from Brunei to jointly develop agro-industrial and knowledge-based industries.
10. The two leaders agreed to expand cooperation in emerging areas such as the green economy and the digital economy.
11. The two leaders agreed to promote people-to-people contacts through enhanced cooperation in the fields of education and human resource development, tourism and culture, as well as air and sea links between countries. Both. The two leaders also acknowledged the importance of cooperation in the field of information and media to enhance mutual understanding.
12: The two leaders welcomed the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding on Youth Cooperation and the Memorandum of Understanding on Cultural and Fine Arts Cooperation on August 11, 2021 via video and agreed That will effectively implement all the documents already signed.
14: The Sultan and the Prime Minister welcomed and presided over the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding between the Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Government of the Sultan of Brunei on bilateral consultations to be established. A framework to deepen bilateral relations and expand cooperation between the two countries.
15. The Sultan thanked His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Prime Minister and the people of Cambodia for the warm welcome and warm welcome to him and the delegation. .
