(Kampong Thom): Mr. Ok Sim, a disabled veteran in Kampong Thom province who joined the army in 1979, just received a new house as a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit in Prey Banlech village, Achar Lak commune Stung Sen.
The handing over of this house took place on November 13, 2022 through Major General Som Sun, Commander of Kampong Thom Military Operation Area, President of Kampong Thom Cambodian Veterans Association.
Mr. Ok Sim stated that he was 63 years old and enlisted in the army in 1979 as the Commander of the 1st Squadron in the 5th Division of Preah Vihear Province and was wounded in the left leg in 1987 during the battle. With the enemy in the battle of O Po, Preah Vihear province. He is survived by his wife and five children, who work in the bicycle / motorbike business to supplement their daily living, combined with the government's monthly salary.
Lt. Gen. Som Sun stated that seeing that his life was difficult and he could not afford to build a decent house on his own, the committee of the Cambodian Veterans Association in Kampong Thom province asked for a decision to build a house donated by Samdech Techo. It is the back of the 224th house, built high above the ground, with concrete pillars, steel beams, planks, wall panels, smart ports, galvanized roofs, grinders and staircases.
During the handover ceremony, Lt. Gen. Som Sun brought the gifts of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet and Mrs. Pech Chanmony to give him an additional 50 kg of rice, 2 boxes of noodles, 1 box of pure drinking water, fish sauce and soy sauce. 2 carry and some kitchen equipment as well as some budget.
