Samdech Techo Hun Sen's assessment was made on November 12, 2022, when he co-chaired the ASEAN-Canada Summit with Canadian Prime Minister Justin Trudeau at the Sokha Hotel in Phnom Penh.
According to the Prime Minister, 45 years ago, with the common commitment and desire to maintain peace, stability and prosperity in both regions, the long-term partnership of ASEAN and Canada has brought outstanding achievements. All sectors will play an important role in addressing regional and global challenges, especially improving the well-being and livelihoods of the people.
The ASEAN-Canada Dialogue was established in February 1977 after the first official meeting between the Canadian Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs and the ASEAN Standing Committee. In 1981, the ASEAN-Canada Economic Cooperation Agreement (ACECA) was signed, laying the groundwork for industrial, trade and technical cooperation between the two sides.
By 2020, trade between ASEAN and Canada will reach $ 16.2 billion, and foreign direct investment (FDI) from Canada to ASEAN will reach $ 5.1 billion. This is according to the latest report on the overview of ASEAN-Canada dialogue relations released by ASEAN in October 2021.
