Xi Jinping is expected to visit Saudi Arabia in December and will attend a summit between China and the Persian Gulf countries with leaders of the Persian Gulf Cooperation Council. The GCC has six members.
When asked by reporters about the main agenda for the visit of Chinese President Adel Al-Jubeir, a senior official for Saudi Arabia's foreign affairs, he replied: "We look at "We care about regional and global stability and security, as well as ways to further increase trade and investment flows between the two countries."
He said that visits between Chinese and Saudi leaders were common as China was Saudi Arabia's largest trading partner, while Saudi Arabia had large investments in China and China had large investments in Saudi Arabia. It is no different from Riyadh's other trading partners or strategic partners, such as the United States, the United Kingdom, France and Germany.
Xi Jinping's planned visit to Saudi Arabia comes at a time when relations between Riyadh and Washington have deteriorated due to disagreements over oil supplies and in the face of US concerns. Around the expansion of cooperation between Arab countries in the Persian Gulf and China.
