US and India become ASEAN's all-round strategic partner (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): At the ASEAN-US Summit on the evening of November 12, 2022, the ASEAN-US Supreme Leaders announced the establishment of a comprehensive strategic partnership. As the ASEAN-India relationship has been upgraded to the same strategic partnership. This is according to Kong Phok, the official spokesman for the 2022 ASEAN Summit.
At a press conference highlighting the feasibility of the 40th and 41st ASEAN Summits and related summits hosted by Cambodia, Kong Phok emphasized that after the establishment of this partnership, it is necessary for the country ASEAN members as well as the United States to find out which areas are the priority tasks to be included in this new partnership.
"ASEAN leaders and President Joe Biden have already announced the establishment of a comprehensive strategic partnership, so after the establishment of this partnership, it is necessary for ASEAN member countries as well," the official spokesman said. "Like the United States, to find out which areas are the priority work to be included in this new partnership."
According to Kong Phok, if we look at the relationship between ASEAN and the United States, it is already comprehensive, which means that the United States and ASEAN member countries have cooperated in many fields, including economy, security, society and culture.
He sincerely hopes that after establishing this comprehensive partnership, the United States and ASEAN member countries will be able to deepen and deepen this partnership, especially in areas that are important priorities for the region. These include the digital economy, joint efforts of ASEAN members to address climate change.
However, Mr. Kong Phok emphasized that what is seen as a fruitful cooperation in the coming years is the cooperation between ASEAN member countries and the United States to prevent the spread of disease. Kovid 19 and after this installation, other areas will also be able to be considered for strengthening relations between ASEAN member countries and the United States.
It should be informed that this initiative to raise the level of ASEAN-US relations was made during the ASEAN-US Special Summit to be held in Washington DC on 12-13 May 2022, which Samdech Techo Hun Sen The Prime Minister of Cambodia and US President Joe Biden co-chaired the meeting.
At this meeting, ASEAN leaders and the President of the United States reaffirmed their joint commitment to further strengthen and build the ASEAN-US Dialogue Partnership, which is indispensable for ASEAN and the United States as well. For the region and the international community. These relations are the foundation for promoting and maintaining peace, security, stability and prosperity in the region.
Apart from ASEAN-US, Mr. Kong Phok also confirmed the establishment of this comprehensive strategic partnership between ASEAN-India.
"ASEAN and India leaders have expressed satisfaction over the progress of ASEAN-India relations, especially the upgrading of ASEAN-India relations as a comprehensive strategic partner," Kong Phok said. In this regard, the ASEAN-India Leaders have adopted the Joint Statement on the ASEAN-India Comprehensive Strategic Partnership.
