(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Saturday, November 12, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Mr. Kishida Fumio, Prime Minister of Japan, paid a courtesy call and discussed work.
The Prime Minister of Japan arrived in Cambodia this morning. His current presence in Cambodia is to attend the ASEAN-Japan Summit, the ASEAN Plus Three Summit, and the East Asia Summit.
The Japanese Prime Minister is also scheduled to hold a bilateral meeting with US President Joe Biden. He will also hold trilateral meetings with US and South Korean presidents to discuss North Korea's nuclear weapons.
It should be noted that in March 2022, the Prime Minister of Japan paid an official visit to Cambodia.
Cambodia and Japan formally established diplomatic relations on January 9, 1953. This relationship will last for 70 years in 2023. Cambodia and Japan upgraded their relationship from a normal level to a strategic partnership in December 2013.
On January 28, 2018, Japan opened a consulate in Siem Reap, in charge of five provinces: Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Oddar Meanchey, Preah Vihear and Kampong Thom.
Starting from this excellent relationship and cooperation, Cambodia and Japan have also boosted investment and trade in significant growth. Cambodia is Japan's eighth largest trading partner in ASEAN. In 2021, the trade volume between Cambodia and Japan will reach about 1.7 billion US dollars.
Cambodia's exports to Japan include clothing, footwear, furniture, cosmetics, paper, stationery, leather, animals, metals, and more. In particular, the goods that Cambodia imports from Japan include: machinery, cars, meat, electrical appliances, furniture, paper, cotton, all kinds of fabrics, plastic products, sports equipment, all kinds of spare parts and so on.
As for investment, from 1994 to 2020, there are 144 Japanese investment projects in Cambodia with a total capital of nearly 3 billion US dollars.
