(Prey Veng): At least three students died in a boat sinking and six others escaped death as they took a boat trip on Lake Ta Ei after school.
This incident happened at 8:15 am on November 12, 2022 at Boeung Ta Ey, Tnot village, Kampong Russey commune, Po Rieng district, Prey Veng province.
Police in Po Rieng district said that prior to the incident, a group of nine schoolchildren were riding in a 6-meter wooden boat when the boat sank, causing three people to drown and six children to drown. Others swam and people rescued from death.
Authorities confirmed that school children who suffered from the sinking of the boat include:
First: Name: San Ly Meng, Male, 16 years old, Residence: Kampong Russey Village, Kampong Russey Commune. Second: Name: Porun, Male, 15 years old, Prey Meas Village, Kampong Russey Commune. Kampong Russey village, Kampong Russey commune, Po Rieng district, Prey Veng province.
Police said that after the incident, the Kampong Russey police force cooperated with the Po Rieng District Inspectorate and the people to search for all the bodies in the water at 11:12 and handed over the bodies to the families for the traditional ceremony.
Po Rieng district authorities also called on students in their free time from school not to play in the water to avoid possible accidents.
