The celebration took place during the Prime Minister of Australia's courtesy call and discussion with Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo's personal assistant, in this meeting, the Prime Minister of Australia highly appreciated the attention of Cambodia on the issue of Myanmar.
In addition to the issues of ASEAN and Myanmar, Samdech Techo and the Prime Minister of Australia also discussed bilateral relations between Cambodia and Australia.
The Prime Minister of Australia highly appreciated the leadership of Samdech Techo, which has made Cambodia develop rapidly.
The Prime Minister also expressed satisfaction with the cooperation between the two countries. In particular, the growth of Australian investment in Cambodia.
Mr. Anthony Albanis informed Samdech Techo that Australia will continue to support the development of sustainable development programs, digital economy, smart energy, green economy and other sectors to contribute to the stability and prosperity of Cambodia and other countries in the region.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his satisfaction with the Cambodian-Australian relationship and also thanked the Prime Minister of Australia and the Australian Government for their assistance to Cambodia's development from the beginning. In particular, the end of the recognition of the Khmer Rouge at the United Nations in 1983.
He also thanked Australia for assisting Cambodia in agriculture, helping Cambodia find peace, helping Cambodia develop human resources, provide vaccines to Cambodia and contribute to Cambodia's development by providing assistance and promoting investment in Cambodia.
"I am optimistic that the strong partnership and cooperation between ASEAN and Australia will continue to provide many more benefits to our people to promote regional and inclusive development," he said. Sustainability, efficiency and prosperity.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also praised Australia for its unwavering support for the ASEAN Community through its active participation in ASEAN-led mechanisms.
He added that under the ASEAN-Australia Comprehensive Strategic Partnership Framework, he commended the speed and achievements of both sides in a short period of time through a number of initiatives, especially the Australia Initiative for the Future of ASEAN. Which will provide cross-sectoral support for the implementation of the ASEAN Perspective on the Indo-Pacific, which is the specific need of ASEAN countries.
Please be informed that Australia has been a strong, resilient and cohesive partner of ASEAN. Australia became ASEAN's first dialogue partner in 1974.
