Experts show the potential and investment opportunities in the condo market in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Experts in the field of condominiums in Cambodia show the opportunities and potential for local investors to invest in the condominium market, because the lives of Cambodians are more prosperous, combined with the flow of investment from abroad. Investment in the condominium sector has improved.
"The condominium market is a long-term development and a good choice for both local and foreign investors, as the growth of Cambodia's affluent population will continue to increase, including the influx of foreign investment," Khon Kongkea said. And foreigners who come to do business in Cambodia.
He added that condominiums are condominiums, a potential market share in the real estate sector in Cambodia. Currently, the supply of condominiums in Phnom Penh is about 30,000 units, or equivalent to nearly 100 buildings, this number is estimated to increase to About 80,000 units by 2025.
However, due to the effects of Kovid 19 and the global economic crisis, the supply of condominiums seemed to increase slightly, while the market price of condominiums showed a small increase compared to before the outbreak of Kovid-19.
According to research from real estate companies, condominiums currently cost an average of $ 1,500-3,000 per square meter, while average rents range from $ 8 to $ 14 per square meter per month.
ERA Real Estate is a world-class real estate company founded in 1971 based in the United States. Today, this world-class real estate company has approximately 40,000 professional agents with 2,200 operating offices in 37 countries around the world.
The presence of ERA Cambodia in the Cambodian market for more than 4 years has made a significant contribution to the Cambodian condominium market with highly professional service agents, enabling the company to sell more than 30 large condominium projects. The combined investment of these projects is worth billions of dollars.
