Elderly and disabled grandparents living in Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province receive a gift from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen
The granddaughter of a widow with five children has not yet found a job after the Kovid-19 crisis. Currently, the above family lives in Anlong Kong village, Trapeang Kong commune, Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province.
On that occasion, the First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross brought the words of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who sent a message to visit, sympathize and consider the life of Grandma and Grandpa.
She also told her grandparents, "Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen is always monitoring the well-being of the people, and after seeing the information about this difficult case, Samdech is very emotional and sympathetic." "Extremely, and immediately sent a team to help alleviate the difficulties in life and as an encouragement to grandparents."
She also instructed the widows and daughters to continue to take care of their grandparents and encourage them to go to the hospital for treatment and to live hygienically, drink boiled water and clean the environment around the house, especially to encourage their children. To be able to study for a prosperous future.
The grandparents and daughter were overjoyed and expressed their deep gratitude to Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen for taking care of them and encouraging them to hope for the future with their gifts. Humanitarian relief also helps.
Please note that the gifts given to the grandparents include: rice, noodles, fish, soy sauce, milk, water, ears, air, food, mosquito nets, blankets, sarongs, scarves and some money. CRC Kampong Speu Branch also donated some groceries and supplies. Separately, the Cambodian Red Cross also supported the widow who is the daughter of the above grandparents, including: rice, noodles, fish sauce, soy sauce, mosquito nets, blankets, sarongs, scarves and some money.
