At the same time, in support of the implementation of the above policy framework, the Royal Government has just announced the implementation of the Digital Government of Cambodia Policy 2022-2035 to supplement and guide the way to digitalize the public sector governance system at both levels. National and sub-national levels aim to build a strong, intelligent and clean government.
Mr. Vongsy Visoth also said that Kovid-19 is no longer a major challenge as before, but that the world and our region are facing greater uncertainty due to the risks and complexities and pitfalls. Many: geopolitical competition, economic downturn, rising inflation and energy shortages, as well as the worsening effects of climate change.
"Of course we are in a difficult situation, but it also gives us the opportunity to achieve sustainable economic recovery, resilience and the environment in each region and country," he said. Well.
He also said that the digital economy has been growing rapidly in the process of economic recovery. Accelerating the capture of digital technologies, especially new technologies that support and relate to the Fourth Industrial Revolution, is a key policy agenda of ASEAN.
In this context, Mr. Vongsey Visoth presented some ideas to promote and accelerate the integration of ASEAN digital economy as follows:
1. ASEAN, as well as all member countries, should be well prepared to meet the necessary conditions for the digital age, including: the formulation of relevant policies, regulations, as well as the development of infrastructure and other support conditions to facilitate The rise of the digital economy, a major source of regional growth.
2. Cooperation between sectoral institutions and the pillars of the ASEAN Community must be closely coordinated and work together more deeply to accelerate the digital revolution to promote economic recovery after the Kovid-19 crisis and to Build long-term resilience in the region to be able to withstand future crises.
3: Of course, it is necessary to increase spending on the development of the digital economy, but at the same time the government must remain prudent on the budget. Therefore, strategically, we should focus on increasing the revenue from the digital economy, and the government should strengthen its capacity through cooperation with stakeholders to monitor and record digital transactions and develop reliable tax policies for the digital economy.
4. ASEAN should work together to reduce the development gap in the region. In this regard, ASEAN needs to continue to promote knowledge sharing and capacity building programs among members to increase a deeper understanding of the potential of the digital economy.
5. Digital economic integration needs to strengthen digital connectivity, and consultations with stakeholders such as businesses, including micro, small and medium enterprises, are important in bridging the digital gap. Some sharp measures should focus on: expanding access to financial services, using cost-cutting technologies and intermediary tools such as digital payment services, etc.
6. In line with the new ASEAN Roadmap 2025 Together, ASEAN should seize new opportunities from digital technology and take measures to prepare for various risks. All sectoral working groups should focus on digital trends and incorporate them into strategic action plans and work programs to use digital technologies for regional integration and cooperation, especially economic development.
