Regarding bilateral cooperation, the two Prime Ministers were pleased with the outcome of the 14th meeting of the Cambodia-Laos Joint Commission for Bilateral Cooperation (JCBC) and reiterated the importance of promoting bilateral relations. Parties to increase trade and investment. The two sides encouraged the relevant authorities to implement the signed documents on energy cooperation.
The two Prime Ministers noted with pleasure that both sides had achieved the demarcation and demarcation of about 86% of the joint border line and agreed to assign the Joint Boundary Commission of Cambodia and Laos (JBC) to finalize the draft treaty. Demarcate the state border between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Lao People's Democratic Republic to be signed during the Prime Minister's visit to Laos next year.
