Ratanakkiri Provincial Authority Dismantles Fences That Block Roads from Passing a Rubber Plantation in Lumphat District and Warns of Legal Action in the Case of Plantation Blockers
The owner of the rubber plantation that blocked the road to prevent people from passing through and did not follow the instructions of the authorities is Long Meng Kruy in Chong Ra village, Patang commune, Lumphat district.
The dismantling of fences to prevent people from passing through and transporting agricultural products to the market took place on the morning of November 11, 2022, led by Mr. Khan Chamnan, Deputy Governor of Ratanakkiri Province.
Apparently, in dismantling the roadblock to prevent people from passing through, Mr. Long Meng Kruy "did not object to the authorities, but he briefly told the authorities that the road was only open for 10 days, that is, the road will be closed. "Again, people are not allowed to pass by, they do not know how big he is, so he dares to say such words."
The Deputy Governor of Ratanakkiri Province emphasized that the working group came down today under the order of Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun, Provincial Governor, to remove the fence to block the road for people to cross again, after the authorities informed Mr. Long Meng Kruy, the owner of the plantation. Rubber (road blocker) dismantled by himself, but when the deadline, he refused to dismantle, so the team dismantled the road fence today.
Mr. Khan Chamnan stated: "Please depend on this road, do not worry about the owner of the rubber plantation blocking the road again, if he dares to block the road as mentioned above, please report to the authorities immediately, then the team will go down "Removing the fence and not repeating it, he faces legal action."
