(Phnom Penh): The project to build a large multi-purpose logistics center (warehouse) in Cambodia with an investment of more than $ 200 million has been officially unveiled in conjunction with the 40th and 41st ASEAN Summit at Sokha Hotel Phnom Penh. PPLC Multipurpose Logistics Center will be an important link for trade in the region and can help strengthen Cambodia to become an important logistics hub.
Speaking at the launch of the project, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth said that the transport and logistics sectors are two interconnected and backbone sectors and also a driving force for economic integration in all sectors. Productivity and economic growth. The Deputy Prime Minister added that the PPLC will help strengthen connectivity in the transport and logistics sectors within the framework of the Greater Mekong Subregion (GMS), ASEAN and the world.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol expressed support for Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth's remarks. The Senior Minister added that PPLC plays an important role not only in strengthening Cambodia's connectivity with regional trade and among the Greater Mekong Subregion (GMS) countries, but also to improve the efficiency of multimodal transport, including Roads, railways, waterways, deep-sea ports and air transport in Cambodia.
He added that PPLC will also create an efficient ecosystem, reduce transportation costs, improve competitiveness, including supply chains and boost regional economic growth.
"PPLC is set out in our Logistics Master Plan as a strategic project to support Cambodia's integration into the ASEAN Intelligent Logistics Network (ASLN) and to promote Cambodia's economic development and business connectivity. In the real ASEAN region. This was confirmed by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol.
He added that inter-regional relations are a testament to the strong bilateral relationship between Cambodia and Singapore and also within the ASEAN framework. This relationship is characterized by joint competition between ASEAN member countries.
In line with the ASEAN Connectivity Master Plan 2025, which aims to reduce supply chain costs, increase the speed and reliability of supply chains in each ASEAN member state, the PPLC aims to strengthen the economy and promote regional integration. Such as skills training to expand the industry.
Dr Robert Yap, Chief Executive Officer of YCH Group and Chairman of the ASEAN-Singapore Business Council, said that in the transport sector, efficiency and capacity mitigation in the post-epidemic era are being facilitated through Systematic interconnection.
He added that PPLC's multi-logistics infrastructure was built with the aim of achieving a seamless connection across ASEAN countries, strengthening its capacity through strong diplomatic ties between Singapore and Cambodia.
"We are committed to deepening our partnership and working with more Singapore-based companies to deepen their infrastructure capabilities across the region." This is further confirmed by Lavan Thiru. Commentary: The story of the China International Import and Export Fair sharing the future will never end
