Ministry of Industry announces project to improve water supply in southwest of Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): In recent years, Phnom Penh has grown significantly in terms of infrastructure development, satellite city development, increase in trade and investment. In 2011, the Royal Government decided to expand the administrative area of Phnom Penh by transferring 20 communes of Ponhea Leu, Muk Kampoul, Kien Svay, Kandal Stung and Ang Snoul districts of Kandal province to be under the control of Phnom Penh Capital Administration.
The growth and expansion of the administrative territory of Phnom Penh has made the water supply in Phnom Penh very challenging. In fact, the current demand for clean water in Phnom Penh as a whole is about 746,000 m3 / day. The capacity of the water treatment plant of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority in all 4 locations is only 630,000 m3 / day.
To address these challenges, the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, under the strong support of the Royal Government, especially the two guardian ministries, the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation and the Ministry of Economy and Finance, has been implementing investment projects in the water supply system. More beautiful as follows:
2. The second phase of the Bak Kheng water supply project, with a capacity of 195,000 m3 / day and a total water supply network of 188 km, is scheduled to be completed in the first quarter of 2024.
3. Takhmao City Water Supply System Expansion Project with a capacity of 30,000 m3 / day, which is scheduled to be completed in December 2024.
Meanwhile, Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority is continuing to cooperate with development partners to study the Bak Kheng Water Supply Project, Phase 3, Niroth Water Supply Project, Phase 3, Water Supply Project, Techo International Airport, Takhmao City and Water Supply Project. The middle sand, too.
The two sides agreed that in the new era, accelerating the construction of the Cambodian-Chinese common destiny community is a common aspiration and in line with the fundamental interests of the two peoples. For peace, stability and development in the region.
The two sides agreed to promote the implementation of the "Cambodia-China Joint Destiny Community Building Action Plan" signed in 2019 and update the following action plans:
(A): Strengthen advanced strategic communication. The Chinese side will continue to welcome the royal visit of His Majesty the King and His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia to China. Chinese leaders look forward to the visit of Samdech Techo PM and other Cambodian leaders at an appropriate time on both sides.
(C): Make full use of military exchange and cooperation mechanisms by enhancing the relationship between defense and military institutions at all levels of the two countries through practical cooperation such as joint training and co-operation, provision of military equipment; Technology, health services, logistics and multilateral security.
Law enforcement cooperation will be further strengthened by focusing on the suppression of human trafficking, online gambling, cyber fraud and crime through the facilitation of close cooperation on capacity building and information exchange. Efforts will be further focused on the implementation of the Cooperation Agreement within the framework of the Cambodia-China Joint Working Group on Safety and Security, Belt and Road.
Major projects such as the Angkor Siem Reap International Airport project, the Sihanoukville-Hong Kong submarine fiber optic network project, and supporting infrastructure projects such as roads, bridges, logistics and warehousing will be accelerated. The two sides support close cooperation on clean energy to support the green economy, energy efficiency and efficiency, and the reduction of greenhouse gas emissions in Cambodia.
(F): Cambodia actively supports and participates in the Global Development Initiative in line with the United Nations' commitment to implementing the "Sustainable Development Agenda 2030". Cambodia supports the Chinese side's proposal for a global security initiative and is ready to cooperate with China on global security governance for comprehensive security, cooperation and sustainability.
In this regard, Cambodia and China call on the relevant parties to continue to fully and effectively implement, deepen practical maritime cooperation and achieve the South China Sea Code of Conduct as soon as possible on the basis of mutual consent. Build the South China Sea into a sea of peace, friendship and cooperation.
The joint statement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of China, obtained by Fresh News on November 11, 2022, emphasized that both sides stressed the importance of adhering to true multilateralism, modernization and democracy. International relations and the development of global governance towards greater justice and equity.
At the same time, the Cambodian and Chinese sides agreed to adhere to the basic norms of international relations, protect international impartiality and justice, and oppose all forms of political hegemony, unilateral power and monopoly, Cold War ideology, and interference in internal affairs. Of other countries and two standards.
Both sides supported and said that countries should exchange and cooperate on human rights on the basis of equality and mutual respect, rather than politicizing on human rights issues.
The Cambodian and Chinese sides agreed to further strengthen coordination and cooperation in the multilateral framework, including: Mekong-Lanchang cooperation and ASEAN-China cooperation to jointly promote the development of the Mekong-Lanchang Common Destiny Community; Closer ASEAN-China comprehensive strategic partnership with meaning, content and mutual benefit
In a joint statement between the two governments, China supported Cambodia in hosting the relevant ASEAN Summit and praised Cambodia's active role in promoting sustainable and long-term development in the region.
According to the joint statement, 2022 will be the 100th birthday of His Majesty the King and 2023 will be the 65th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and China.
Both sides agreed that the traditional Cambodian-Chinese friendship, cherished and cherished by His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk and President Mao Zedong, Prime Minister Zhou Enlai and previous Chinese leaders Is the common treasure of both peoples.
In the new era, under the leadership of the Cambodian leadership and President Xi Jinping, Cambodia-China relations have continued to grow to a new level, achieving fruitful progress in building a common Cambodian-Chinese community of destiny.
