Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Maintaining Unity, Solidarity and Centrality is the Top Priority to Ensure ASEAN Sustainability (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of ASEAN, Attracted Leaders All ASEAN members maintain that unity, solidarity and centrality are priorities to ensure the sustainability and resilience of ASEAN in the face of future problems and challenges.
In 2022, the Association of Southeast Asian Nations, or ASEAN, will be about 55 years old. At the opening ceremony of the 40th and 41st ASEAN Summits in Phnom Penh on Friday morning, November 11, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as the chair of ASEAN, highlighted that for 55 years, ASEAN has achieved The main objective is to build a peaceful, modern, resilient and resilient ASEAN community.
While highlighting the spirit of unity and joint efforts of ASEAN to achieve many achievements, however, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted some challenges for ASEAN. Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that ASEAN must always be vigilant because the socio-economic situation of ASEAN and the world is still fragile and fragmented.
"We are at a crossroads where the lives of millions of people in the region depend on our ideals and long-term vision, our right policies and decisions, and our realistic approach to tackling it," he said. "The strategic challenges we are all facing."
Currently, ASEAN seems to be facing a number of issues that threaten the disintegration of the ASEAN Community, such as the issue of Myanmar and the geopolitical rivalries of the superpowers, leading to the identification and adoption of different political tendencies among ASEAN member countries.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's remarks were seen as a wake-up call for ASEAN leaders to strengthen the spirit of solidarity to strengthen ASEAN.
"We must all focus on the common goal of common development for peace, stability and excellence in the region," he called on ASEAN members. "All of our relationships do not happen by chance, but through many years of hard work, commitment and effort."
