1: In principle, Timor-Leste is allowed to join the 11th ASEAN member.
2. Give Timor-Leste observer status and allow Timor-Leste to participate in all ASEAN meetings, including the plenary sessions of the ASEAN Summit.
3. Develop a roadmap based on the neutral criteria for full membership of Timor-Leste, including the key achievements identified by the report of the three pillars of the ASEAN Fact-Finding Mission and assigned to the Coordinating Council. ASEAN to create this roadmap and submit it to all ASEAN leaders for approval during the 42nd ASEAN Summit.
4. All ASEAN Member States and external partners must fully support Timor-Leste in achieving those goals through capacity building and other necessary support for accession. Timor-Leste is a full member of ASEAN.
