In 2022, Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, was elected Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council. In a face-to-face meeting with ASEAN leaders, the duke led members of the business community from ASEAN member countries to attend this important meeting.
Oknha Kith Meng stated that on behalf of the Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council, we fully support the ASEAN-ASEAN Community, work together to address all challenges and continue to promote ESG (environmental, social and governance) reforms in a True justice and sustainability.
The duke also called for ASEAN to speak out on the immediate end of hostilities between Ukraine and Russia and to allow for peaceful and diplomatic talks.
Duke Kith Meng emphasized that ASEAN and the world as a whole face historic risks. Not only does it affect business and industry, but it also risks our future and the future of our children.
Level one: is what we call existence risk. It is said that the days of the Ukraine-Russia war are not over, which means that we may be closer to nuclear war. In addition, the risks of climate change and the possibility of an increase in other epidemics are facing us.
The second level: global economic risk. It has been suggested that the global economic crisis may be just in time. Rising inflation, constraints affecting food and energy security are more obvious than ever. It is unfortunate that the development gap among nations is widening.
Level 3: In our backyard, that is the risk in ASEAN. We have always proclaimed the cohesiveness and stability of ASEAN, but the Myanmar issue is an unfinished agenda. The political geography of the superpowers has threatened to divide and divide us. The harmonization and integration of our economy (as we move forward) seems to lack the “doable” spirit that is so desperately needed.
