Minister of Agriculture: Abolition of measures to prevent the export of rubber and unprocessed rubber trees abroad, giving farmers the option to grow family rubber can be sold to high prices
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has issued a new circular on the revocation of Royal Government Directive No. 10, dated 23 June 2003, on measures to prevent the export of rubber and unprocessed rubber wood. Overseas.
Regarding the revocation of the circular on measures to prevent the export of rubber and unprocessed rubber wood, Mr. Dith Tina confirmed to Fresh News that it is a serious consideration of Samdech Techo Prime Minister to give farmers a choice. Family-grown rubber can be sold to high-priced markets.
The minister explained that in the past, when all rubber plantations were state-owned, the government required all state-owned rubber companies to process rubber for higher value-added before exporting. Later, the rubber plantation was privatized by the Cambodian government into the rubber plantation of a private company. Can be exported.
The minister added that the case for companies contracted with the state is a different case from the family rubber farmers. That is, all companies have an obligation to process rubber at a high price before it can be exported.
According to the data of the General Department of Rubber of the Ministry of Agriculture, as of August 2022, Cambodia exported 194,014 tons of rubber and 20,629 cubic meters of rubber wood.
Cambodia has a total rubber area of 404,044 hectares, of which 310,193 hectares are rubber plantations, accounting for 77% and 93,851 hectares are maintenance lands, equivalent to 23%. Thousands of people have gathered to seek justice. From the tragedy at the Indonesian football stadium
