The following is the full text of the invitation from the General Department of Taxation: Kampot pepper exports fall by almost 50% due to protracted war between Russia and Ukraine
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Nguon Lay, President of Kampot Pepper Promotion Association, said that the export of Kampot pepper, which is a geographical indication (GI) product to the international market this year, has decreased significantly due to the war crisis between Russia and Ukraine, which has narrowed the Kampot pepper market this year, while the domestic market for tourists has not improved.
He said the drop in exports was due to the effects of the war between Russia and Ukraine and the weakening of the euro, which had hurt exporters, causing them to delay buying from farmers.
According to the association's president, Kampot pepper production is estimated at 206 tons in 2022. But the pepper harvest is not 100% complete yet, so the company can order and export later. The price remains the same: black pepper at $ 15 per kilogram, red pepper at $ 25 per kilogram and white pepper at $ 28 per kilogram.
He said the drop in exports had severely affected smallholder farmers as they had to pay for labor and cultivation maintenance, which is why some farmers have decided to sell pepper at lower prices. Under the market without using the name Kampot pepper. Large companies growing large tracts also suffered losses.
