Samdech Techo Hun Sen and ASEAN Leaders Meet with the ASEAN Business Advisory Council (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of November 10, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the Head of State / Government of ASEAN continued. Meet and discuss with ASEAN Business Advisory Council.
The ASEAN Business Advisory Council was established in 2001 by the ASEAN Heads of State / Government. The Council is tasked with providing input and reporting from the private sector to help drive ASEAN's efforts towards economic integration.
In addition, the Council also provided feedback on the implementation of ASEAN Economic Cooperation and proposed priority areas for consideration. The main activities of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council focus on identifying and identifying challenges to facilitate and promote economic cooperation and integration.
During the meeting, Duke Kith Meng raised a number of issues that pose a threat to doing business. These include the war in Ukraine, climate change, epidemics, the global economic crisis, rising inflation, Myanmar's problems and geopolitical competition.
In response to the above issue, Duke Kith Meng expressed his full support for adhering to the ASEAN Central Committee and ASEAN together to solve all challenges.
At the same time, Duke Kith Meng called on ASEAN to intervene to immediately end the conflict between Ukraine and Russia and allow the start of peaceful and diplomatic talks.
Duke Kith Meng also called on ASEAN to continue to be at the heart of an open, equitable and responsible multilateral trading system that adheres to the rule of law. Continue to promote environmental, social and governance reform in a truly fair and sustainable manner.
