Spokesperson: The Ministry of Education may test Chinese language education programs in 20 high schools in the future, while Korean language is being tested in 6 high schools.
This confirmation was made after Cambodia and China signed a Memorandum of Understanding on the joint development of Chinese language learning programs in public secondary schools (public schools), which the Cambodian side represented by Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports. And the Chinese side, represented by Mr. Wang Wentian, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia on November 9, 2022.
Mr. Ros Sovaja stated that "The Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the Ministry of Education of the People's Republic of China on the development of joint Chinese language education programs in secondary schools has reached the pilot phase of the implementation of Chinese language education programs. In 20 high schools in only two or three provinces.
Mr. Ros Sovacha said that for technical work, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports will set up a commission to continue working with the Chinese side.
Mr. Ros Sovacha emphasized that the Memorandum of Understanding aims to promote people-to-people exchanges and strengthen friendship between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the People's Republic of China.
According to a spokesperson for the Ministry of Education, the current foreign language education program in the Cambodian education system consists of: English from 4th to 12th grade, French from 4th to 12th grade and Korean language. Grades 7 to 9 in 6 high schools.
Mr. Ros Sovacha confirmed that Korean language education is based on the volunteerism of students in this pilot phase.
The six high schools that have been testing the Korean language include: Starting in 2020, Preah Yukanthor High School, Sisowath High School and Boeung Trabek High School, and starting in 2022, Chbar Ampov High School, Russey Keo High School and Freedom High School.
