Cambodia, China Hold a Handover Ceremony for Takeo Temple Renovation and Preservation Project
(Siem Reap): Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and High Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Mr. Li Keqiang, Prime Minister of the People's Republic of China, handed over and received the renovation project. Preservation of Takeo temple of Angkor historical site.
The ceremony was held on the morning of November 10, 2022 with the participation of Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information and Governor of Siem Reap, Director General of APSARA Authority, as well as many other national and international guests. Siem Reap city.
On this occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara stated that Cambodia's growth and development is inseparable from the close Cambodia-China cooperation, especially grants, grants, interest-free loans and concessional loans in the field. Many important, including the provision of vaccines against Kovid 19.
In addition to all these conservation activities, other Chinese public and private institutions have also contributed to the preservation, promotion and promotion of Cambodian cultural heritage. In particular, the handover ceremony of the Takeo Temple Restoration and Preservation Project at this time is a clear testament and a result of the immortal cooperation between the two nations of Cambodia and China.
Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara expressed his position that the Royal Government of Cambodia will continue to adhere unconditionally and unambiguously to the "one-China policy" as well as fully support the Chinese government's "Belt and Road Initiative" in On all regional and international forums, especially together, build "one community, one destiny for humanity."
Mr. Ly Ker Chheang stated that seeing that the historical site of Angkor shows the great glory as well as the pride of the Cambodian nation, so now China has also helped to restore the Takeo temple of the historical site of Angkor, which is The second time under the framework of UNESCO helped Cambodia.
Mr. Li Keqiang believes that the project to restore and preserve the Takeo temple will benefit Cambodia as well as strengthen cooperation between China and Cambodia, as well as cultural and civilized exchanges between countries in the world.
The Chinese Prime Minister hopes that the cooperation between China and Cambodia will contribute to the Angkor historical site as well as encourage the people of the two countries to better understand the culture of the two countries.
