Sends Suspect to Ratanakkiri Provincial Court in Violent Case
(Ratanakkiri): The light criminal police force of Ratanakkiri Provincial Police on the morning of November 10, 2022, sent a suspect in a case of intentional violence to the Ratanakkiri Provincial Court.
The suspect, Khon Seang Khun, 40, a plantation worker, resided in Ol village, Patang commune, Lumphat district.
The arrest of a suspect after receiving a complaint of intentional violence against a woman named Chim Sonita in Ol village, Patang commune on November 3, 2022.
After the violence, the Office of Minor Crimes, in cooperation with the Lumphat District Inspectorate, went to the scene to investigate.
The operation was led by Mr. Hang Sambath, Deputy Prosecutor of the Provincial Court, until November 8, 2022, although the suspect was detained and remanded in custody at the Ratanakkiri Provincial Police Commissioner's Office of Minor Crimes.
According to the police officer, at 17:00 on November 3, 2022, the victim, Chim Sonita, dragged a water pipe to give water to someone who crossed the suspect's border, then the water pipe broke at the border. The victim then shouted at his brother, "Why not look at the water?"
Keo Pheakdey, Deputy Prosecutor and Spokesman for the Ratanakkiri Provincial Court, at 10:50 a.m. on November 10, 2022, told Fresh News that the judicial police officers of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Police had sent the suspects. The above has come to court, but has not been charged yet, that is, the proceedings are ongoing.
