Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the "Four Strategic Goals" under the pillars of the ASEAN Economic Community include: First, strengthening digital connectivity, science and technology, and second: bridging the development gap for ASEAN competitiveness. , 3: Promoting ASEAN integration, environment, resilience and competitiveness; and 4: ASEAN as a global for growth and development, aiming to promote sustainable economic growth, environment and resilience. .
"We must all work together to ensure that ASEAN remains an attractive and vibrant region for trade and investment," he said.
At the same time, Samdech Techo stated that in an environment where the socio-economic situation has returned to normal, the private sector must be more actively involved to promote the development of environmentally friendly, resilient and sustainable areas through priority activities. Five main points.
This statement was made by Samdech Techo, President of ASEAN, at the opening ceremony of the ASEAN Business and Investment Summit 2022 in Phnom Penh on November 10, 2022.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that achieving the restoration of economic growth as well as the resumption of socio-economic activities in the region in the past would not have been possible without the active participation of the private sector.
In the context that the socio-economic situation has returned to normal, Samdech emphasized that the private sector has a more important and indispensable role in joining ASEAN more vigorously to promote the development of environmentally friendly areas. Durability and sustainability such as:
1. Stimulate economic activity, trade, and investment, especially further foreign direct investment, as well as maximize the benefits of the existing ASEAN Free Trade Agreement.
2: Development of information technology, digital technology, research and development, and promotion of innovation
4: Promoting fraternal development, environment and promoting digitalization with the promotion of reducing the digital gap
5: Complementing the financial needs for the rehabilitation of sustainable socio-economic development, etc.
The Prime Minister stated that for Cambodia, in order to restore and promote the national economic growth in a sustainable, sustainable and environmentally friendly manner, the Royal Government has approved a new "Law on Investment" and set out a "Strategic Framework and Program for Economic Recovery of Cambodia." "To live with Kovid 19 in a new normal path for 2021-2023."
He added that as the chair of ASEAN in 2022, Cambodia would like to fully support the ASEAN Business and Investment Summit. Cambodia expresses its commitment to work closely with ASEAN Member States and all ASEAN Dialogue Partners to lead the ASEAN Economic Community towards resilience, sustainability, environment and high competitiveness.
The meeting was held at Sofitel Phuket Tra Phnom Penh. The ASEAN Business and Investment Summit is a major event in Southeast Asia and an important forum for the business community to meet directly with country leaders and company presidents to address challenges in Southeast Asia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "As a party to the ASEAN Agreement, Cambodia reaffirms its commitment to the trading system in accordance with the rule of law and welcomes all business and economic cooperation." "Investment from all ASEAN member countries and all parties."
Moreover, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in order to contribute to the response to the effects of climate change, natural disasters and environmental damage, Cambodia proposed the establishment of the "ASEAN Green Agreement". Contribute to helping guide ASEAN towards a green, sustainable and highly competitive future in economic terms.
Samdech Techo stated that as the chair of ASEAN in 2022, Cambodia would like to fully support the ASEAN Business and Investment Summit. Cambodia is committed to working closely with ASEAN Member States and all ASEAN Dialogue Partners to lead the ASEAN Economic Community towards resilience, sustainability, environment and high competitiveness.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that the Royal Government has been working to increase investment in infrastructure, both physical and digital; Improve the quality of logistics services, increase the efficiency of public services, promote skills development and modernize the social security system.
