(Phnom Penh): China has provided more than $ 200 million in loans for the construction of bridges and roads in Kratie province and the project to expand National Road 7 into four lanes from Skun to Kampong Cham.
The loans for the two projects were signed on Wednesday evening, November 9, 2022, under the chairmanship of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Li Keqiang, Prime Minister of China. The loan agreement was signed between Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, and Wang Win Thien, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, confirmed to Fresh News that the bridge across the Mekong River and the connecting road in Kratie province has a total length of nearly 2 kilometers at a cost of more than 100 million dollars.
Separately, the project to expand National Road No. 7 into 4 lanes from Skun to Kampong Cham provincial town with a length of more than 40 kilometers at a cost of more than 100 million.
According to the Senior Minister, both of the above projects have already been studied and the time to open the construction site is to wait for the time of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia. The minister confirmed that the official opening time could be at the end of 2022 or the beginning of 2023.
Please note that China is the country that has provided the most aid and loans for the construction of roads and bridges in Cambodia. The report shows that 29 road infrastructure projects using Chinese concessional financing and grants have been completed, with a total length of more than 3,000 kilometers, with a budget of nearly 2 billion US dollars.
The project is constructing 3 roads with a length of 363.96 km with a budget of 529.98 million US dollars. There are 9 major bridges completed with a total length of 8,565 meters, with a budget of approximately 290.05 million US dollars, and 1 bridge under construction with a total length of 996 meters, the bridge across the Bassac Sitbo River of the ring road project. 3 Using a budget of 56.04 million US dollars.
