The symbolic inauguration of the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway took place after the two leaders presided over the signing of an agreement on 18 documents between Cambodia and China.
The Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, the first expressway in Cambodian history, was put into operation on October 1, 2022, after more than three years of construction.
The Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway with a total length of 187.05 km was opened for construction on March 22, 2019 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. This road connects Village 1, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh to Village 1, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province.
The expressway is divided into three lanes and three lanes, including:
In case of heavy traffic, drivers can use both lanes, while heavy vehicles must adhere to the lane for normal traffic. In the case of vehicles on any lane, driving faster is not considered overtaking and the vehicle behind them must use the warning light.
The 18 documents were signed after a bilateral meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Ly Kheang, who attended the ASEAN Summit and related meetings hosted by Cambodia and paid an official visit.
The 18 documents include the following:
1. Concessional loan agreement in US dollars for the construction of a bridge across the Mekong River in Kratie province and a connecting road.
Concessional Loan Agreement in US Dollars for the Expansion of National Road 7 (Skun-Kampong Cham).
3: Letter of delivery - Receiving the master plan for the transportation system in Cambodia.
4: Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation in Agricultural Trade between the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia and the Ministry of Commerce of China.
5. Certificate of handover for the second phase of rural road improvement project under a grant from the Chinese government.
6- Certificate of handing over the project on sending 19 Chinese traditional medicine experts to fight Kovid 19 to Cambodia.
7. Certificate of handing over and receiving of emergency supplies for the supply and support of Cambodia as the chair of ASEAN.
8- Certificate of handing over and receiving Chinese aid projects to improve the school environment and the supply of educational equipment in Cambodia.
9. Memorandum of Understanding on the Joint Development of Chinese Language Learning Programs in Public Secondary Schools in Cambodia.
10. Agreement on Cooperation in Science, Technology and Innovation.
11: Memorandum of Understanding on Strengthening Cooperation on Veterinary Medicine, Bio-Veterinary Materials and Animal Feed Additives
12: Animal Vaccine Assistance Agreement.
13. Protocol on phytosanitary requirements for pepper exports from Cambodia to China.
14: Protocol on the requirements and requirements for the inspection of animals and animal hygiene for natural fishery products exported from Cambodia to China.
15. Agreement on the Prevention of Illegal Theft, Excavation and Export and Import of Cultural Property.
16. Agreement on the establishment of the Cambodia-China Traditional Chinese Medicine Center.
17: Memorandum of Understanding on the provision of tools and means to respond to climate change under the framework of South-South Cooperation.
18: Certificate of Acceptance for Engineering Work Project Supporting the Improvement of People's Livelihood of the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway Construction Project under a Grant Grant from the Chinese Government.
