The Minister of Foreign Affairs of Ukraine made this remark during a courtesy call and discussion with Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen on Wednesday morning, November 9, 2022 at the Peace Palace.
The misery of the war in Cambodia could not be erased from the Golden Book of history. In a meeting with Samdech Techo Prime Minister, Mr. Dimitro Kuleba also reminded of the bitter past of Cambodia.
Arriving in the land of the former smoke of war and witnessing the development of Cambodia today, the Ukrainian Foreign Minister excited and rejoiced with all Cambodians who have put out the flames of war. Peace and rapid development like this.
Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo's personal assistant, told reporters: "His Excellency the Minister said that he was very excited and congratulated Cambodia for going through the flames of war, genocide, but so far. Cambodia enjoys peace, stability and rapid and beautiful development. "This is the desire of every Ukrainian."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that Cambodia has experienced the pain and suffering of war and foreign aggression, so Cambodia understands the feelings of the Ukrainian people.
Samdech Techo shared his condolences and shared the difficulties with all Ukrainians. He also wished the people of Ukraine peace and development.
During the meeting, the Ukrainian Foreign Minister thanked Cambodia for its support to Ukraine through the issuance of the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Statement, as well as the call for an immediate end to the use of force and the return to talks to end the war.
The Minister also thanked Samdech Techo for being the co-founder of the United Nations General Assembly Resolution against the invasion of Ukraine.
The Ukrainian Foreign Minister described these gestures as an expression of Cambodia's concern over what is happening in Ukraine.
The Prime Minister emphasized that Cambodia's position on the war in Ukraine is to adhere to and adhere to the principles enshrined in the UN Charter and international law.
He added that Cambodia has always opposed aggression, threats or violence against the sovereignty and territorial integrity of independent states. The Prime Minister added that Cambodia does not support the separation of states and the invasion of territory from other countries.
It should be noted that on November 1, 2022, Samdech Techo and Mr. Vladimir Zelinsky, President of Ukraine, also had a telephone conversation regarding the war in Ukraine.
During the meeting, the President sought the continued support of Cambodia against Russian aggression and also thanked Cambodia for always showing its opposition to Russian aggression on Ukrainian territory.
