History of the Independence Monument's National Independence Day Celebration November 9
(Phnom Penh): Every November 9th, Cambodia celebrates the National Independence Day at the Independence Monument under the high presidency of His Majesty the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni. The top leaders of the Senate, the National Assembly and the Royal Government from various ministries are also invited.
Citizens, students, youth scouts and Red Cross youth in large numbers also attended the Independence Monument celebrations.
Why is the Independence Day celebration held at the Independence Monument? In what year was the Independence Monument built?
After the full independence from the French colony on November 9, 1953, it was built and inaugurated in 1958 during the reign of King Norodom Suramarit (1955-1960), the father of King Norodom Sihanouk.
The Independence Monument was erected as a symbol of Cambodia's independence from France on November 9, 1953, and as a monument to the dead for the national cause and to celebrate freedom and independence from foreign rule.
At the end of 2007, Phnom Penh Capital Hall built and improved the Independence Monument to be more attractive, such as adding colorful lights at night and changing the water park around Khoeun, etc. This improvement It costs about 500 million riels. Due to its dilapidated condition, it sometimes fell into pieces of cement, which was a danger of danger at some point.
In 2012, the Royal Government of Cambodia also decided to renovate for the second time at a cost of $ 800,000 to more than one million US dollars, which was completed before the Independence Day, November 9, 2012.
The five-tiered Independence Monument, which features 100 serpent dragons, is another highlight of the afternoon, as the sun sets over the statue, revealing a cast. The essence of style will brighten the entire Independence Monument. Drunk, please do not drive! 6 killed, 10 injured in road accidents nationwide on November 8
