Samdech Techo Hun Sen: In 2022, Cambodia will collect more taxes than planned, which can be up to 115 percent (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, revealed that in 2022, Cambodia will be able to collect up to 115 percent of taxes. Exceeding the set plan.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said this on the evening of November 8, 2022, on the occasion of Samdech and Mr. Pham Minh Chinh, Prime Minister of Vietnam, presiding over the opening of the Cambodia-Vietnam Investment and Trade Promotion Forum 2022.
"This year is a year that we are very proud of with the increase in revenue, we have collected tax revenue according to our budget law for just over 10 months, we have achieved more than 100 percent of the plan," he said. It's done. ”
"This year, we hope to achieve at least 115 percent of our internal revenue, so this is part of the cost we have to support our people." This is the additional confirmation of Samdech Techo.
It should be noted that by the first 10 months of 2022, the General Department of Taxation has collected tax revenue for the national budget of 2,945.95 million US dollars, equivalent to 104.48% of the plan set by the 2022 budget law. The tax department collected 4.48% of the planned revenue, equivalent to $ 126.41 million.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said this on the evening of October 8, 2022, on the occasion of Samdech and Mr. Pham Minh Chinh, Prime Minister of Vietnam, presiding over the opening of the Cambodia-Vietnam Investment and Trade Forum 2022.
"The world situation is difficult to predict, but what should be clear is that we should make sure that our relationship does not change. This is a good point." This is the confirmation of Samdech Techo.
Samdech considered that this is a complementary economy. "Although the global and regional economies have changed, it is difficult to predict, but what we need to believe is that the partnership between Cambodia and Vietnam is still good and will continue to complement each other forever," he added.
It should be noted that Cambodia and Vietnam, countries with a land border of about 1,270 km, established official diplomatic relations on June 24, 1967. The relationship was severed in 1970 and reunited in 1979.
In 2005, Cambodia and Vietnam upgraded the relationship to "traditional good-neighborly relations and strong, long-term and comprehensive cooperation in all fields."
Relations and cooperation between the two countries have been continuously enhanced and have always supported each other, both regionally and globally. Under this good relationship, Cambodia and Vietnam have always supported and provided assistance for each other's development.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Encourages Vietnamese Investors to Invest and Do More Business in Cambodia (Phnom Penh): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen Encourages Vietnamese Investors to Invest and Do Business in Cambodia Increasingly in Cambodia, especially in areas with high potential in Cambodia, such as modern agriculture, food processing industry and light manufacturing industry.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: "I would like to encourage Vietnamese investors to invest more business operations in Cambodia, especially in areas with high potential in Cambodia, such as modern agriculture, food processing industry and industry. Lightweight manufacturing and so on.
According to a report by the Cambodian Ministry of Commerce, the total bilateral trade volume between Cambodia and Vietnam from January to July 2022 compared to the same period last year increased by more than 34% in the investment sector. According to the Council for the Development of Cambodia, private investment from January to October 2022 increased by 1.3% compared to the same period last year.
However, Samdech Techo noted, "We do not see the presence of new Vietnamese investment projects in Cambodia this year and in 2021, unlike before, there was a crisis of 19 Kovid, in which Vietnamese investors came to invest a lot in Cambodia. "Especially in agriculture and telecommunications."
He said that in 2022, the situation seems to be better for Cambodia, according to the forecast of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Cambodia is expected to achieve growth of around 5.5% in 2022 and 6.6% in 2023. This is an additional confirmation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The gradual recovery of the Cambodian economy is due to the proactive and authoritarian efforts of the Royal Government through the introduction of timely and socio-economic stabilization measures with the strong participation of the people. Cambodia, in the spirit of fighting the Kovid 19 crisis, has formed a community outreach and has contributed to strengthening the foundation for a stronger redevelopment for Cambodia.
This was stated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Cambodia-Vietnam Investment and Trade Promotion Forum 2022 held in Phnom Penh on November 8, 2022.
"If you look at the number of foreign tourists who visited Cambodia from January to September 2022, Vietnamese tourists ranked second with a total of more than 280,000 people, more than three times compared to the same period. The same thing happened in 2021. ” This is according to Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
At the same time, the number of tourists from the two countries is expected to increase further by accelerating outreach activities as well as increasing connectivity among destinations and tourism products.
He added that in order to be ready to receive more foreign tourists, the Royal Government of Cambodia has been building a new Phnom Penh International Airport in Kandal Province and a new Siem Reap International Airport, which is scheduled to be completed by the end of 2023.
