Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Cambodia intends to link the production chain of automobiles and electronics through the development of the country strategy (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, said that Cambodia intends to link the production chains of automobiles and electronics. By developing a plus country strategy, especially with Vietnam as the first choice.
"Cambodia intends to link the automotive and electronics production chains by establishing a country plus strategy, especially with Vietnam, which is the first choice of foreign investors in both sectors to relocate production." This is the confirmation of Samdech Techo.
Samdech hopes that Cambodia will receive investment projects to support the supply of production lines in both sectors, especially electronics for Vietnam.
Samdech gave the example of Minibia, a Japanese company based in Thailand, which, when Thailand faced problems, especially during the Kovid 19 crisis, expanded its production in Cambodia.
"Investment experience: You can invest in Vietnam, you can also invest in Cambodia, you can invest in Thailand, you can also invest in Cambodia, you can invest in Cambodia, but when you have an emergency, their supply chain continues. " This is according to the additional confirmation of Samdech Techo.
However, Samdech acknowledged that Cambodia's human resources are still limited, requiring training to keep up with the situation, and that Cambodia and Vietnam need to work together on this training.
He added that the construction of the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway, which will begin construction soon, will play an important role in connecting Phnom Penh with Vietnam, reducing shipping time and possibly. Help solve traffic congestion on National Road No. 1, which is the main road connecting Phnom Penh to Bavet.
