BEIJING, Nov. 6 (Xinhua) - The 14th high-level ministerial meeting of the General Assembly of signatories to the "Wetlands Convention" concluded in Wuhan, Hubei Province, China on Friday. Officially, urging the parties to take action to prevent and systematically divert risks posed by deforestation around the world.
The Wuhan Declaration is the fruitful result of this meeting. After 51 years of signing the Wetlands Convention, despite identifying 2,466 major international wetlands and 43 wetland cities, 19 regional initiatives and parties Efforts have been made to achieve sustainable wetland conservation, but the amount of natural wetlands worldwide is still reduced by 35%.
Tan Guanmin, deputy director of the National Department of Forestry and Grasslands, said the Wuhan Declaration is an important document that brings together the common ideas of the parties and expresses the common will of the world to declare to the world the commitment. And China's responsibility to enhance the construction of ecological civilization and promote the cause of wetland conservation.
Acting Governor of Pursat Province Introduces 8 Measures to Disseminate Education and Take Hot Measures on Invasion of Forest Land in Protected Areas in O'Som Commune
(Pursat): Mr. Cheng Lay, Acting Provincial Governor, represented by Mr. Chiao Tai, Governor of Pursat Province, recently introduced eight major legal measures to disseminate education, guidance and take hot action on deforestation and forest encroachment. Illegal hunting of wildlife traps in geographical protected areas, O'Som commune, Veal Veng district, Pursat province.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Cheng Lay informed that he had flown frequently and had seen a lot of encroachment on forest land in O'Som commune.
At the same time, he also disseminated education, introduced and introduced eight hot measures, including:
First, land clearing activities have been completed with the implementation of the border demarcation policy. The current border demarcation, attended by a meeting of the Ministry of Environment, received and examined the presentation of experts that there are red areas as conservation areas, yellow areas as sustainable use areas and green areas as community areas to be considered. Accept to register state land.
Second: Management of the village administration, Appendix Monty, the district administration should prepare technical documents for discussion with the cadastre and submit to the provincial administration for review. Separately, the issue of handing over or demarcating the territorial administration is drawn up by the Ministry of Interior.
Third, there are two types of land registration applications: state land and private land:
Fourth, the use of enjoyable land other than land registration is not fully legal, it can be revoked at any time to be developed in any field according to the actual needs. The land will be confiscated by the district or provincial administration. In this case, the Wildlife Alliance and rangers understand that long-term crops will not be affected, but new crops must be dealt with immediately.
Fifth, to support the activities to suppress illegal logging and encroachment on forest land, so please local authorities, communities, people, please cooperate with the forces of the Wildlife Alliance and rangers, and especially the organization to review the additional budget for the people to protect us. Prevent patrols and please stop confirming the forest land purchase and sale letter.
Sixth: Immigrants, commune chiefs, village chiefs, post chiefs must be able to deal with those who come to cut down the forest and can update the workers on the farm.
Seventh, before confirming the deed of sale of forest land, the deed of ownership must be examined. Show via satellite every 5 days the activities of the forest landscape, how it has changed) Land policy and the environment.
