Solidarity Charity Parade at Bakan Pagoda Collects 84 Million Riels and $ 1,700 for Building Achievements in Monasteries
(Pursat): The Solidarity Kathin, initiated by Mr. Ing Tibola and Mrs. and his team, Mr. Cheng Lay, Acting Provincial Governor, and Ms. and US expatriate Mum Se and Buddhists from inside and outside the province to dedicate their lives to God. Monks who have been waiting for the rain for a quarter at Bakan pagoda in Trapeang Chong commune, Bakan district, Pursat province, collected 84 million riels and 1,700 dollars.
On the afternoon of November 6, 2022, the Kathina Association held a three-round procession around the Preah Vihear Temple with the participation of the three monks, nuns, Ta Chi, and Buddhists from all over the world.
According to Acharya Wat, the meaning of Kathina Festival is that according to the Buddhist tradition and worship of the Cambodian people for a long time, Kathina Festival can only be done for 29 days from the 1st day of the month of Assoch. The 15th day of the lunar month, which is dedicated to the monks on any day, and a pagoda can only be done once a year.
Acha said that the Kathin is a skirt that the grandparents bring a garment sewn with stubbornness called Chivor to give to the monks who have been waiting for the rain for 3 months already. For a person who should do so in accordance with the rules of the Buddha, he is born a full-fledged Kathina, while the unfortunate is the ancestor of the Kathina practitioner, who has received many blessings, and the monks who have received the throne and approved it also have five kinds of alms.
Venerable Lay Kan, Chief Bishop of Bakan Pagoda, is adamant that the association will raise 84,000,000 Riels and US $ 1,700 for the construction of various achievements in the pagoda.
The following is the full text of Li Keqiang's message:
At the invitation of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, I will soon pay an official visit to Cambodia, one of the oldest and most beautiful civilized countries in the world. Relevant Leaders' Meeting on East Asia Cooperation.
This is my first visit after the outbreak of Kovid 19 in the last three years, and the first stakeholder meeting on East Asian cooperation will be held in person. Together for 2 years.
Over the years, the relationship between China and Cambodia has been constantly developing. His Excellency Xi Jinping, President of the People's Republic of China, paid a visit to Cambodia in 2016 and presented the "Friendship of the People's Republic of China" medal to Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia for Freedom, Dignity and Happiness in 2020. These are set as new pages for the relationship between the two countries.
Under the complicated and changing currents in the international and regional arena, as well as the emergence of instability, uncertainty and insecurity, the countries in the region must maintain a stable environment, maintain the momentum of development, and continue to inherit. Together experience history, seize real opportunities and create visions for the future.
The world today is in an age of challenge and hope. In this great era, whether big patterns or great wisdom or big emotions, such as mutual respect, equality, mutual learning, cooperation, mutual success, openness and mutual understanding, the friendship between China Cambodia, as well as East Asia Cooperation, has always adhered to as a model force, a healing force and a forward force on the international and regional stage.
Faced with new opportunities for in-depth development of technological and manufacturing reforms, train new impetus for cooperation in areas such as 5G, AI and smart cities, accelerate the transformation of the digital socio-economy, especially by The period of establishing cooperation on a wide range of international technological innovations so that the achievements of transboundary technology create benefits for all mankind.
Faced with climate change and energy security risks, China is willing to work with ASEAN to build a clean energy cooperation center to achieve low-carbon and sustainable green development.
Facing the impact on people's lives caused by Kovid 19 We are pleased to help improve people's lives through pilot projects such as the China-Laos Railway Poverty Alleviation Initiative in East Asia. Etc. Stabilize the supply of food and energy sources, accelerate the admission of ASEAN students to study in China, and deepen humanitarian relations, such as culture, tourism.
As the world's largest developing country, we will focus on doing our best to ensure that the Chinese people can live a good life. Since the beginning of 2022, China's economic development has gone through an unusual period. Affected by complex factors, both domestic and foreign, the economic process has been facing downward pressure beyond expectations.
China adheres to the national policy of open base, and the gateway is bigger. We will strengthen government institutions, give market control, improve service reform, continue to create a market-oriented and international trade environment, so that China can be at the forefront of opening up the region. Investing and sharing development opportunities with the world.
Cambodia has a saying that comes the way, there is hope. The path we take may not be smooth, but no mountain is higher than man, no road is longer than a foot. We look forward to working with countries in the region, including Cambodia, to move forward, overcome all storms, so that China-Cambodia relations as well as East Asian cooperation can be further developed and provide new opportunities. More rich.
