A large crowd of people came to participate in the 5th traditional boat race and Kathina at Wat Svay Romeat, Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): Wat Baray Mohan Ti Ratanaream, also known as Wat Svay Romeet, located south of the Teuk Thla baray in Sangkat Teuk Vil, Siem Reap City, organized the 5th traditional boat race to preserve the community's traditions and celebrations.
This year's traditional mini-boat race and charity event will last for two days on November 5 and 6, 2022, with 13 pairs of boats participating, each with a capacity of six people.
Ms. Keo Molina, who lives in Sangkat Kork Chak, Siem Reap, was very happy to attend the boat race and the Kathina ceremony at Wat Svay Romeat. She came to visit as a family, as well as many neighbors also came to participate in this program.
Tin Heur, who lives in Siem Reap's Teuk Vil district, also said that this year was very happy, as the program missed two years due to the Kovid-19 epidemic. In the community as well as around the world. And this year, a large number of people came to participate in the 5th traditional boat race and the Kathina at Wat Svay Romeat on this occasion.
Meanwhile, Mr. Krouch Loun, who lives in Sangkat Teuk Vil, Siem Reap City, said that he saw the smiles of all the people who came to participate in the boat race and the Kathina ceremony was very happy, even though the weather was a bit hot. By. He said that he wants to have this program every year so that people can have fun and participate in the Solidarity Charity.
