MANILA (Reuters) - A homemade bomb exploded on a bus, killing one passenger and injuring 10 others in the southern Philippine city on Sunday, officials said. Suspected to be part of a kidnapping attempt. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Sunday, November 6, 2022.
Military and police officials say investigators are trying to determine if the attackers were from the same armed group that carried out similar bombings years ago to extort money from bus companies operating in major cities. The south of the country or not.
Regional Army Commander General Roy Galido said the bus company "received constant kidnapping messages". He said the military and police were working with bus owners to arrest the kidnappers, who may have been outraged by the bus company's refusal to provide them.
