(Preah Sihanouk): The police force of Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province, in cooperation with the police force of Bit Trang commune, led the anti-drug force to crack down on a drug case.
The operation was carried out under the direction of Major General Chuon Narin, Sihanoukville Provincial Police Commissioner and under the direct command of Mr. Oung Vuthy, Prey Nup District Police Inspectorate at CIA Pram point in Chamnot Ream village, Bit Trang commune, Prey Nup district, Preah Sihanouk province. Suspicious number one.
Local authorities confirmed that on November 5, 2022, at 3:00 PM, Lieutenant Colonel Oung Vuthy, Prey Nup District Police Inspector, led the anti-drug force to crack down on a drug case at C-5 point in Chamnot Ream village. Bit Trang Commune, Prey Nob District, Preah Sihanouk Province. The operation arrested a suspect named Nuon Meas, male, 26 years old, factory worker, residing in Po Thuong village, Bit Trang commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province.
The confiscated items included four packs of suspected drugs, and a mobile phone.
On the same day, at 16:00, the above suspects cooperated with the police to arrest two more suspects at a rented room in Po Thuong village, Bit Trang commune, Prey Nob district, Sihanoukville province.
The two suspects are Chan Rat, male, 30 years old, factory worker, currently living in Po Thuong village, Bit Trang commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province, and Preun Seiha, male, 27 years old, factory worker, currently living in Po Thuong village, Bit Trang commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province. . The confiscated evidences include: 3 packs of suspected drugs, 2 mobile phones.
