Sunak succeeded Liz Truss as prime minister last week. On Thursday this week, his spokesman told reporters that the idea of relocating the embassy was being examined by the previous administration, which was aimed at the former government's consideration of the possibility of moving the British embassy out of Tel Aviv. To Jerusalem.
Asked if the UK was still considering plans to relocate the embassy, spokesman Sunak said the current government had no plans. For decades, the United Kingdom has set up an Israeli embassy in Tel Aviv, as in most other countries, even though Israel considers Jerusalem its capital.
Jerusalem has been a major issue in the decades-long Israeli-Palestinian conflict, with Palestinian authorities insisting that the entire city of Jerusalem should be the capital of a future Palestinian state, while the eastern part of the city is now under its control. Israel since 1967.
However, despite international opposition to the recognition of Jerusalem as the capital of Israel, the United States opened its embassy in the city in 2018 under the leadership of former President Donald Trump, breaking free from decades of politics. Washington. The move was welcomed by Israel but criticized by Arab states and Western allies.
