The seven vehicles returned to their owners were seized by mobile weighing officers in Battambang province and stored at the Puk Chhma truck weighing station in Sangke district, Battambang province. Mr. Ek Rath, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Public Works and Transport, in charge of cracking down on overweight trucks, together with the relevant authorities in Battambang province, returned the vehicles to their owners on Friday morning, November 4, 2022.
With the return of the car to the owner, Mr. Ek Rath also instructed the car owner to stop overweight and also explained the aspects of the land transport law on the weight limit and show the impact for the road caused by the transport. Overweight, too.
He emphasized to the car owners that the ministry was still cracking down on all overweight trucks. In that case, for the car that was caught and if found guilty of the second offense will be punished more severely. In addition to fines and a one-year suspension, drivers face the revocation of their driver's licenses and even shut down their transport businesses.
Truck owners who get their vehicles back into business have promised to stop overweight, but they have also called for some intervention to make their transport business more profitable.
Ms. Kim Srey Mom claimed that she was aware of the transport rules and some difficulties for the road from this transport. But she has no choice because if the weight is limited by law, it is less profitable because the price of oil is higher and the cost of transport remains the same.
Ms. Srey Mom promised to stop overweight and called on all transport operators to stop overweight. But she also called on the owners of the goods to help increase the cost of transporting them, because the price of fuel goes up, they have no profit left.
She also asked the relevant authorities to check the possibility of helping them. Otherwise, they may face a car stop or the bank may confiscate the car because the transport business is not profitable.
Overcrowding has been found to be one of the main causes of road damage and unusability due to the technical nature of the road. The transport formula found that one truck over 10 tons was equivalent to 10,000 vehicles traveling on the road. If one truck weighs more than 30 tons, it is equivalent to 81,000 vehicles traveling on the road.
To prevent road damage caused by overcrowding, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, has taken drastic measures in accordance with the Road Transport Law. In addition to the fine, there is also the seizure of overweight trucks from 20 percent up to one year.
Ek Rath told Fresh News that after the hot crackdown, especially the seizure of the car, the transport business has been alerted to the implementation of the transport law. Under 2021 and 2022, overweight transport by law has decreased significantly, he said.
However, Mr. Ekrat showed continued to take hot action against this overweight truck without any exceptions or concessions. The operation is also conducted fairly, with no favors or exceptions for the powerful. That is, all overweight vehicles must be fined, and overweight vehicles of 20% or more must be fined and the vehicle must be stopped for one year.
He called on all transport operators to abide by the transport law and not to be overweight. He claimed that the crackdown on overweight trucks was not to demand money from transporters, as the fine could not be offset by the amount of road damage costing millions of dollars. No.
Please note that Article 60 of the Road Law states that users of heavy vehicles transporting goods on the road will be fined and the vehicle will be confiscated if they carry out the following transport activities. Under:
This article also stipulates that in case of offense, the total weight load as well as the offense on the maximum weight of the thigh shall be fined in both cases.
In case of having already received the transaction penalty once but continue to commit the offense, the transaction penalty shall be doubled and the company's transportation business shall be stopped for one year. The vehicle owner is responsible for loading and unloading the cargo and vehicle maintenance fees themselves.
