Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly: Food safety is a complex task that needs to be monitored
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly said that food safety is a complex task that requires the coordination of food control activities by the authorities and the participation of the private sector, producers and consumers.
Mr. Yim Chhay Ly addressed the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on the occasion of the 9th National Nutrition Day, which clarified the purpose of the Royal Government of Cambodia to organize the National Nutrition Day every year to raise awareness. Publicize across the country the importance of food security and nutrition in contributing to human capital development, work efficiency, economic growth and social progress.
He stressed that food safety is a complex task that requires the coordination of food control activities by the relevant authorities and the involvement of the private sector involved in the value chain, production and consumers. Economic and social progress has changed the way Cambodians live and eat.
Taking this opportunity, the Deputy Prime Minister made the following calls:
* First, please celebrate this National Nutrition Day to all localities in Cambodia to increase public awareness throughout the country about the importance of food security and nutrition to contribute to human resource development, contribute to efficiency. Employment will contribute to economic growth and social progress.
* Second: All relevant ministries, institutions, sub-national administrations, development partners, civil society, the private sector and the community must pay attention to the implementation of the eight recommendations of the head of the Royal Government, as contained in the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the celebration of the day. Ninth nutrition to be highly effective.
* Fourth: Let the people join together to improve food safety by paying close attention to the production, processing, storage and distribution of food products to be hygienic, safe and quality in accordance with technical standards and requirements on hygiene and Food safety.
* Fifth: Strengthen the coordination, cooperation and communication between the competent institutions responsible for food inspection and sub-national administration of the capital and provinces to implement the law on food safety effectively.
