On this occasion, Mr. Teng Sichun also mentioned the fruitful cooperation carried out by the China-ASEAN Interbank Association and the ASEAN + 3 Interbank Cooperation Mechanism, which strongly supported the recovery. Of regional economy and sustainable development.
As a new development of cooperation and in line with the direction set by the 24th ASEAN Plus Three Summit, as well as the 25th ASEAN Plus Three Ministers of Finance and Governors Meeting of the Central Bank of ASEAN Plus 3, Member Banks of CAIBA and APTIBCM Sign the Joint Statement on "Promoting Cooperation, Sustainable Development and Linking Infrastructure".
The Joint Statement reflects the commitment of member banks in supporting their respective government and central bank efforts in economic recovery in the wake of the Kovid-19 pandemic. Finance and green and sustainable development.
To this end, member banks also affirm their support for enterprises and projects of regional scope through cooperation, such as: joint lending tools, multi-currency lending funds, interbank lending. And other joint ventures of investment and lending.
Under the theme "Promoting Sustainable Development Cooperation and Infrastructure Connections", member banks as well as CAIBA and APTIBCM Observer Bank shared and exchanged meaningful knowledge and experiences on a variety of topics, including: :
(1): Promoting financing focused on the social environment and governance (ESG) in the post-epidemic period of Kovid-19; (2): Promoting regional financial cooperation to strengthen infrastructure connectivity (3). : Promoting the financial environment to support small enterprises in the post-Kovid-19 epidemic; and (4) Promoting regional financial cooperation through digital innovation.
At the meeting, member banks also highlighted the importance of promoting further cooperation, especially in the current challenging economic environment.
