Leaders will also attend the Second ASEAN Global Dialogue on Post-Kovid-19 Rehabilitation, which will be attended by the presidents of a number of key international organizations. Leaders of a number of ASEAN dialogue partners are also expected to attend.
At the official closing ceremony of the 40th and 41st ASEAN Summits, Prime Minister Hun Sen will hand over the ASEAN Chair to the President of the Republic of Indonesia, Joko Widodo, as the rotating chair of ASEAN next year.
During the planned meeting, Prime Minister Hun Sen will also hold bilateral meetings with a number of delegates.
Economists around the world are worried that the US will continue to raise interest rates, which will worsen the global economy.
BEIJING, Nov. 3 (Xinhua) - The US Federal Reserve announced on Tuesday that it would raise interest rates by 0.75%. This is the fourth time the US Federal Reserve has raised interest rates by 0.75% in a row, and the sixth time the US has raised interest rates this year.
This has caused concern around the world. According to a survey of 100 economists around the world conducted by the CGTN network of China Central Radio and Television with Renmin University in China, a series of US rate hikes will The world economy is in deep recession.
Ninety percent of economists commented that the risk of rising inflation and economic stagnation would increase because of this, and 94% thought that a series of rate hikes could put developing countries at risk of debt. Increasingly.
Cambodia-China Friendship Radio Senior Minister Son Kunthor: SMEs are the backbone of the economy, meeting the needs of more than 90% of total enterprises and services in Cambodia
This emphasis was made on the occasion of Senior Minister Son Kunthor's participation in a workshop on "What startups need to know" held on the campus of Western University, Phnom Penh on 3 November. 2022.
Senior Minister Son Kunthor stated, "Small and medium enterprises (SMEs) serve as the backbone of the Cambodian economy, meeting the basic needs of more than 90% of all goods and services in Cambodia, which contribute to providing employment opportunities for the people. In the country to have a prosperous life.
Senior Minister Son Kunthor said that in order to cultivate entrepreneurial ideas for start-ups, the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Micro-Enterprises has already organized several sharing seminars at various educational institutions in the capital and provinces since 2018.
In addition, the President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Micro-Enterprise emphasized that students at all levels and professors are the goal to cultivate business ideas for them to have a basis for consideration and further research before deciding to start a business.
Senior Minister Son Kunthor also said that in the era of globalization, trade and economic integration in the region and the world, as well as the establishment of the Free Trade Area (FTA), the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Industry has a duty to promote And encourage professional entrepreneurs and micro-entrepreneurs.
In addition, the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Micro-Enterprises is responsible for promoting production and services using local raw materials, combining modern technology and e-commerce strategies to compete and gain market share. Both regionally and globally. This was further confirmed by Senior Minister Son Kunthor.
Senior Minister Son Kunthor confirmed that the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Industry is a private legal entity serving the public interest under the initiative of Samdech Vibol Sok An, former Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Council of Ministers, together with the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation.
Senior Minister Son Kunthor stated that the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Micro-Enterprises is a complementary mechanism for the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and is divided into two parts: first: focusing on occupations (handicrafts) and second: focusing on micro-enterprises.
