The latest election results, announced on Thursday, show that Netanyahu and his right-wing group, which was largely considered a source of political turmoil in Israel a few years ago, now win 64 seats. Out of 120 seats in the National Assembly. His main rival in the coalition, led by incumbent Prime Minister Yair Lapid, won 51 seats.
According to the Prime Minister's Office, Lapit congratulated Netanyahu on his success and instructed his officials to arrange a transfer of power. Netanyahu will have 28 days to form his new government, which is expected to be the most right-wing government in Israeli history.
Benjamin Netanyahu was Israel's prime minister for 12 years between 2009 and 2021. The victory represents the return of the former Israeli prime minister, as between 1996 and 1999.
