On the same day, seeing the difficulties and requests of the people, the teachers brought 1 ton of cement, 43 tiles and some money to the principal of O'Sala Primary School, Kampong Svay Commune, Kampong Svay District to repair the classroom. In order for students to study properly.
Citizens, teachers, thank you to Ms. Khuon Khundy and Mr. Kuy Leang Ky for their support in materials and budget for the construction of a school with appropriate classrooms as well as aesthetics to attract students to study. Bless you and the tycoon, as well as your family, may you be happy, do not be sad.
Announcing the inauguration of Mr. Im Ron Hassan as Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, a senior official of the Ministry of Interior advised to work hard to serve the people
(Phnom Penh): Another Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh was officially inaugurated on the afternoon of November 3, 2022 under the chairmanship of Mr. Leng Vy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, Representative of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior. Mr. Mab Sarin, President of Phnom Penh Capital Council and Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh.
Mr. Khuong Sreng on that occasion instructed Mr. Im Ron Hassan, who has been appointed as the new Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, to pay close attention to good cooperation with the relevant ministries, institutions, 14 districts and civil society. Perform work with a high sense of responsibility and good internal unity.
In addition, Mr. Leng Vy instructed the Phnom Penh Capital Administration to continue to maintain security, public order, improve people's lives and continue to work to solve the remaining problems in society. As for the armed forces in the ranks of the Phnom Penh Municipal Unity Command, they must continue to manage the situation, prevent crimes well and inspire the people to participate in making sure that the villages and communes are safe.
In order to make Phnom Penh more beautiful, he asked the Capital Authority to manage the construction properly according to the technical standards, continue to plant trees in public places, improve the environment by inspiring people to pack and store garbage properly and encourage Garbage collection company on time.
TOKYO (Reuters) - Japan's Defense Ministry is considering deploying supersonic missiles by 2030 to strengthen its defense capabilities by increasing its counter-attack capabilities, the Nikkei reported on Thursday. This was released by the AFP news agency on Thursday, November 3, 2022.
The Nikkei claimed that Tokyo was trying to strengthen such capabilities as Russia's invasion of Ukraine changed the global security situation and the number of missile tests unprecedented this year by North Korea, plus an increase in military action. China has been posing a serious threat to Japan.
The Nikkei continued in its report that the Japanese government plans to revise its national security strategy, along with other key defense documents, before the end of 2022, and that the position on counter-attack and supersonic missiles could be correct. Mentioned in those documents.
At the same time, Ms. Sin Ket Arun, Head of Fundraising Office of the Angkor Hospital for Children, said that the Angkor Hospital for Children needs about $ 6 million a year to treat and consult children and other activities. Most of the children who come for treatment have diseases such as respiratory infections, diseases caused by poor hygiene, dengue fever, cancer, diseases related to the nervous system, AIDS, and many other diseases.
In addition, on behalf of the Angkor Department of Children, Ms. Sin Ket Arun also expressed her happiness after seeing the great contribution of the people, especially companies that always have the initiative to create various programs to work together. Raise funds to help the Angkor Children's Department, which is in dire need of funds to save the lives of children.
