The high-level forum discussed topics such as freedom of serviceization, investment and trade facilitation, the RCEP agreement and production structure, and cross-border challenges, with keynote speeches by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. .
The forum is attended by leaders and ministers of RCEP member countries, the Joint Committee on the RCEP Agreement and its affiliates, senior researchers, councils and business associations, researchers from the ASEAN and East Asia Economic Research Institute, the ASEAN Secretariat and other stakeholders. Other.
The event consisted of two rounds of discussions, in which the first round of discussions, speakers and panelists exchanged views on the establishment of the RCEP agreement, as well as the implementation of the ASEAN Agreement since its entry into force, and the second round of discussions included discussions. About the main chapters of the ASEAN Agreement and its implications for the local economy and regional integration.
The event has three main objectives:
1. Recall the long journey of the Asean Agreement and highlight the achievements of the agreement and the experience from its early stages of negotiation, as well as explore priority areas to promote the effective use of the RCEP.
2: Develop a deeper understanding of the key elements of the agreement and clarify the implications of the RCEP to local structural evolution and regional integration with the official launch of the second book of the Research Institute ASEAN and East Asia economies.
3. Strengthen stakeholders' awareness of the importance and opportunities of the ASEAN Agreement to facilitate greater trade and investment in the region.
Dr. Ky Sereyvath emphasized that the high-level forum of the 10th anniversary of the RCEP was discussed not only in Cambodia, but also with keynote speakers from other countries, especially Singapore, Malaysia and Thailand.
